{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017TzwvwnFEeJgbnrtGubRd8","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:5f6cc34ac2a5316d581118e9705de1f5d72a2e7c3ad4307a67bf41d7a2188362\",\"sha256\":\"5f6cc34ac2a5316d581118e9705de1f5d72a2e7c3ad4307a67bf41d7a2188362\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-instr-001\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=bc7b6bea55848f0e3b7c067823f9a3fc43b61162e68c1006a72594163023f0cf]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Actual source-first assessment — phase2\\n\\nSame registered nonauthor Reviewer, same fixed tool policy/history and exact163-member claim. This is a new process/Context; mental continuity unknown. No source/toolpolicy/HOW/code/guide edit, retry/fallback, owner disposition, Product acceptance, install/release/benefit or FDV003/full-calculus claim.\\n\\nFIRST read the actual earlier expectation TEXT, producer,18source_inputs and small structural exposure fields using the retained-evidence JSON-pointer SourceRefs in assessment-call.json /phase1_bridge. Do not read the full65KB expectation envelope or whole candidate_population. Read the original captured phase1 evaluation by its separate field pointers (the whole evaluation exceeds8192bytes). Preserve every original predicate/core_value/domain_outcome/evidence/residual/invalidator exactly: source-derived-expectations remains indeterminate/performed_partial and its historical unread scope remains historical. Do not rewrite its null artifact observation or pretend this actor saw the ref during phase1. Actual rp-expect-1 emitted4387cefa103592b5a76c96d288da403f9211bc3107843bc8dbfa63c501653f61, later acquired by Root; phase2 learns that actual bridge now. Structural source-first flags do not certify semantic completeness/mental independence.\\n\\nBEFORE ANY candidate/proof/HOW/code body, read the deciding governing gaps exposed by that actual earlier partial derivation: FD013 remainder after fd-support-tools line230; applicable Product remainder/INTENT/stdo_a_c Product Definition/reference-frame basis/source-owner map; selected RC9 route owners needed for the judgment, including DESIGN_MODULE ontology/Prime/three views/decision-completeness, REFERENCE_FRAME, ACTIVATION, EVALUATION and FOUNDATIONS conjunction as relevant. Use existing exact governing-index and authority/METHOD_INDEX/CLAUSE_POINTERS/headings for all12 immutable member routes. You choose material clauses and deciding expectations, not a full method dump or an author answer. Report unread/unavailable scope honestly.\\n\\nIf needed before candidate exposure, transparently record a SEPARATE supplemental expectation through review.prepare phase=expectation using YOUR text and actual new earlier governing source_inputs. Do not relabel/rewrite or raise the original indeterminate judgment. If the host saves/previews that response, do not invent the new ref or claim readable receipt. The mandatory ReturnContract and candidate phase still bind the actual earlier4387 expectation; preserve any supplement evidence/asymmetry separately. Source acquisition metadata route: earlier source.read response.evidence -> evidence.read small OperationEvidence /payload/acquisitions; if oversized use retained-evidence source.read pointer /payload/acquisitions with actual evidence id/hash. Prepared/B64/preview/saved path never equals readable acquisition.\\n\\nThen call review.prepare phase=candidate, exact claim from packet, candidate=the current primary guide locator from assessment-call.json, sources=[],proof=[],comparison=null,expectations=ACTUAL bound4387 ArtifactRef,expectation_body=null. This acquires complete declared population as evidence but bulk base64/native preview is NOT semantic reading. Independently source.read deciding exact current HOW, code/helpers/interfaces/tests/guide and current raw proof in readable selections, preserving actual coverage and omissions. The HOW owns ontology/Prime8/three views/axioms and its whole finite design is part of the task. Current actual public retry proof includes all56 deciding raw files; paths/index in the fixed candidate population. Do not claim all generated fixtures, whole omitted metadata/inventories or vendor/internal streams reviewed.\\n\\nAssess four later predicates SEPARATELY: design-conservation, implementation-conservation, guide-task-criteria, public-use-qualification, under the existing review-evaluation.md. You own each actual core_value/findings/evidence/consequence and performed scope. A qualification gap can remain indeterminate/unperformed without becoming a design/code result; positive technical judgments do not erase original partial/negative/missing evidence. Carry the actual original source-derived-expectations evaluation unchanged, with transparent original provenance; explain later governing acquisitions/supplement separately. No supplied later verdicts or severity scale. Findings require exact support; unsupported triage remains unknown.\\n\\nAll source.read calls use encoding=utf8/max_content_bytes8192, adaptive10–80-line exact parent-hash selections or JSON-pointer fields. Split further on refusal/preview; saved native paths cannot be read with builtins disabled. Selected tools.describe only when needed, never all-inventory bulk. Return exactly one unfenced integer-only closed-return JSON object. Use actual Context.boundaries.activation_identity and current packet coordinates, all5 required IDs, work_result=null. Actual unperformed/unread/unknowns stay explicit. Never fabricate an earlier or new ArtifactRef, standing raise or owner acceptance. Only fixed permitted tools.describe/source.read/evidence.read/review.prepare operations.\\n\",\"coordinates\":null,\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"44ea47c9e7252adebcdacde2eb0bc6074313e2edebe94d7dffd66037c5d9e811\",\"selected_sha256\":\"44ea47c9e7252adebcdacde2eb0bc6074313e2edebe94d7dffd66037c5d9e811\",\"size_bytes\":5165,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"assessment-instructions.md\",\"root\":\"runtime\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"44ea47c9e7252adebcdacde2eb0bc6074313e2edebe94d7dffd66037c5d9e811\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"3a11b322-dd20-486a-86ee-1cbd8555e0a0","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:42:00.050Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:5f6cc34ac2a5316d581118e9705de1f5d72a2e7c3ad4307a67bf41d7a2188362\",\"sha256\":\"5f6cc34ac2a5316d581118e9705de1f5d72a2e7c3ad4307a67bf41d7a2188362\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-instr-001\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=bc7b6bea55848f0e3b7c067823f9a3fc43b61162e68c1006a72594163023f0cf]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Actual source-first assessment — phase2\\n\\nSame registered nonauthor Reviewer, same fixed tool policy/history and exact163-member claim. This is a new process/Context; mental continuity unknown. No source/toolpolicy/HOW/code/guide edit, retry/fallback, owner disposition, Product acceptance, install