{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAz95uR5jXxmVDrQqXL4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017fWNUSS4pqu8sAijnEkbZn","name":"mcp__ac_review__source_read","input":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-fdt-012","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[121,179]},"sha256":"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":996,"cache_read_input_tokens":137352,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":996},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"4898381f-1fbf-43e8-a87c-c4cd59dac7ce","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:44:43.995Z","request_id":"req_011CgAz95cK5npT8Dx7ZHw1e","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017fWNUSS4pqu8sAijnEkbZn":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-fdt-012","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[121,179]},"sha256":"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017fWNUSS4pqu8sAijnEkbZn","display_name":"Source Read","server_display_name":"a_c.graphify.fd-support","tool_name":"source.read"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017fWNUSS4pqu8sAijnEkbZn","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:1a03a00712365c88a666236bad4eb93400e79b575c98fca579c9c48b1199a267\",\"sha256\":\"1a03a00712365c88a666236bad4eb93400e79b575c98fca579c9c48b1199a267\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-fdt-012\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=de5bea8c15bc3ecb60b19d7613594783099131162e3f6d4958a4a635f1755d45]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"**Input:** exact preflighted activation/admission, selected executor operation,\\nexisting grant, permitted tools/territory, material preconditions, effective\\ncontext/settings and selected attempt/resource/observation conditions.\\n**Output/checks:** invocation identity, actual supplied payload/settings,\\nacknowledgments, output/partial-output and effect/termination observations with\\nscope/time, retained attempts and decision-relevant return/exception/basis-change\\nnotifications. Check material bindings before the named effect and expose\\nchanged preconditions without silent rebase. **Limit:** the deterministic\\nwrapper does not make F_P output deterministic or semantic evidence of success.\\nRequests, delivery, evaluation, intended effects and their observed end remain\\nseparate under the selected method; timeout/cancel/interruption preserve its\\nunknown-effect semantics. Fallback observation is bounded by supplied conditions,\\nnot a mandatory polling controller. Owners: [ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act)\\n§1/3 Effects/5; [EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §6 if selected.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-008 — Capture and check a closed return\\n\\n**Input:** returned payload/transport evidence, original activation and return\\ncontract, expected consumer, exact subject/basis and supplied currentness,\\ndependency and independence predicates/evidence. **Output/checks:** preserved raw\\nreturn and provenance, deterministic binding/format/currentness findings and\\nthe exact declared evaluations, predicates, domain outcomes and residuals that\\nwere actually returned. Identify stale/wrong-subject/wrong-basis, missing,\\nduplicate and conflicting evidence without dropping it; expose non-consumable\\nsupport/gaps to the declared consumer. **Limit:** do not relabel a historical\\nverdict as a new verdict, manufacture a result for an unperformed evaluation or\\ntreat schema validity as semantic assessment/acceptance. A transport failure is\\nreported separately using the selected method contract. Owners:\\n[FOUND](fd-source-owner-map.md#found) Results/Conjunction of results;\\n[RF](fd-source-owner-map.md#rf) RF-012;\\n[ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §3/7;\\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §4.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-009 — Prepare independently acquirable review evidence\\n\\n**Input:** exact review claim/candidate and composition boundary, caller-selected\\nsource, comparison subjects, proof/evidence population and method-owned\\nindependence/exposure contract. **Output/checks:** independently resolvable raw\\nauthority/candidate/proof acquisition routes, acquired content where requested,\\nexact byte/record comparisons, and separate assertion/expected-result versus\\nexecution provenance. Support expectation recording before candidate exposure\\nand preserve the actual acquisition/exposure record under the supplied contract.\\nWorkers can acquire their implementation/proof context; Reviewers can inspect\\nthe actual candidate, tests/fixtures and source without author-only privileges.\\n**Limit:** diffs and trace/binding checks are not semantic findings, an independent\\nverdict or adoption of a review recommendation as disposition. Owners:\\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §1–4/6;\\n[ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §3/10/13–16;\\n[EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §9/10/17/19 if selected.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-010 — Execute declared checks and method-owned joins\\n\\n**Input:** exact subject/observations, selected executable or reproducible\\ndecidable predicate/proof contract and its provenance/domain/limits, or a\\nselected method-owned conjunction/translation with required coverage and inputs.\\n**Output/checks:** reproducible `F_D[v]` judgments for the properties actually\\nevaluated, counterexamples/gaps, and joins computed only under the supplied\\nqualified operator. Preserve source predicate, original domain outcomes,\\nnot-performed assessments, uncovered obligations and incompatibilities as the\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[121,179]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23\",\"selected_sha256\":\"c03aa14772d36641555020e6f9f77cb78b09fddc766ea41003413bbd867324eb\",\"size_bytes\":3883,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[121,179]},\"sha256\":\"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"5725eac7-cfa3-4f02-bcb4-8bcf1e1309d4","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:44:44.018Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:1a03a00712365c88a666236bad4eb93400e79b575c98fca579c9c48b1199a267\",\"sha256\":\"1a03a00712365c88a666236bad4eb93400e79b575c98fca579c9c48b1199a267\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-fdt-012\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=de5bea8c15bc3ecb60b19d7613594783099131162e3f6d4958a4a635f1755d45]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"**Input:** exact preflighted activation/admission, selected executor operation,\\nexisting grant, permitted tools/territory, material preconditions, effective\\ncontext/settings and selected attempt/resource/observation conditions.\\n**Output/checks:** invocation identity, actual supplied payload/settings,\\nacknowledgments, output/partial-output and effect/termination observations with\\nscope/time, retained attempts and decision-relevant return/exception/basis-change\\nnotifications. Check material bindings before the named effect and expose\\nchanged preconditions without silent rebase. **Limit:** the deterministic\\nwrapper does not make F_P output deterministic or semantic evidence of success.\\nRequests, delivery, evaluation, intended effects and their observed end remain\\nseparate under the selected method; timeout/cancel/interruption preserve its\\nunknown-effect semantics. Fallback observation is bounded by supplied conditions,\\nnot a mandatory polling controller. Owners: [ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act)\\n§1/3 Effects/5; [EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §6 if selected.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-008 — Capture and check a closed return\\n\\n**Input:** returned payload/transport evidence, original activation and return\\ncontract, expected consumer, exact subject/basis and supplied currentness,\\ndependency and independence predicates/evidence. **Output/checks:** preserved raw\\nreturn and provenance, deterministic binding/format/currentness findings and\\nthe exact declared evaluations, predicates, domain outcomes and residuals that\\nwere actually returned. Identify stale/wrong-subject/wrong-basis, missing,\\nduplicate and conflicting evidence without dropping it; expose non-consumable\\nsupport/gaps to the declared consumer. **Limit:** do not relabel a historical\\nverdict as a new verdict, manufacture a result for an unperformed evaluation or\\ntreat schema validity as semantic assessment/acceptance. A transport failure is\\nreported separately using the selected method contract. Owners:\\n[FOUND](fd-source-owner-map.md#found) Results/Conjunction of results;\\n[RF](fd-source-owner-map.md#rf) RF-012;\\n[ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §3/7;\\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §4.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-009 — Prepare independently acquirable review evidence\\n\\n**Input:** exact review claim/candidate and composition boundary, caller-selected\\nsource, comparison subjects, proof/evidence population and method-owned\\nindependence/exposure contract. **Output/checks:** independently resolvable raw\\nauthority/candidate/proof acquisition routes, acquired content where requested,\\nexact byte/record comparisons, and separate assertion/expected-result versus\\nexecution provenance. Support expectation recording before candidate exposure\\nand preserve the actual acquisition/exposure record under the supplied contract.\\nWorkers can acquire their implementation/proof context; Reviewers can inspect\\nthe actual candidate, tests/fixtures and source without author-only privileges.\\n**Limit:** diffs and trace/binding checks are not semantic findings, an independent\\nverdict or adoption of a review recommendation as disposition. Owners:\\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §1–4/6;\\n[ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §3/10/13–16;\\n[EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §9/10/17/19 if selected.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-010 — Execute declared checks and method-owned joins\\n\\n**Input:** exact subject/observations, selected executable or reproducible\\ndecidable predicate/proof contract and its provenance/domain/limits, or a\\nselected method-owned conjunction/translation with required coverage and inputs.\\n**Output/checks:** reproducible `F_D[v]` judgments for the properties actually\\nevaluated, counterexamples/gaps, and joins computed only under the supplied\\nqualified operator. Preserve source predicate, original domain outcomes,\\nnot-performed assessments, uncovered obligations and incompatibilities as the\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[121,179]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23\",\"selected_sha256\":\"c03aa14772d36641555020e6f9f77cb78b09fddc766ea41003413bbd867324eb\",\"size_bytes\":3883,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[121,179]},\"sha256\":\"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:1a03a00712365c88a666236bad4eb93400e79b575c98fca579c9c48b1199a267","sha256":"1a03a00712365c88a666236bad4eb93400e79b575c98fca579c9c48b1199a267"},"id":"p2-read-fdt-012","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=de5bea8c15bc3ecb60b19d7613594783099131162e3f6d4958a4a635f1755d45]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"**Input:** exact preflighted activation/admission, selected executor operation,\nexisting grant, permitted tools/territory, material preconditions, effective\ncontext/settings and selected attempt/resource/observation conditions.\n**Output/checks:** invocation identity, actual supplied payload/settings,\nacknowledgments, output/partial-output and effect/termination observations with\nscope/time, retained attempts and decision-relevant return/exception/basis-change\nnotifications. Check material bindings before the named effect and expose\nchanged preconditions without silent rebase. **Limit:** the deterministic\nwrapper does not make F_P output deterministic or semantic evidence of success.\nRequests, delivery, evaluation, intended effects and their observed end remain\nseparate under the selected method; timeout/cancel/interruption preserve its\nunknown-effect semantics. Fallback observation is bounded by supplied conditions,\nnot a mandatory polling controller. Owners: [ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act)\n§1/3 Effects/5; [EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §6 if selected.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-008 — Capture and check a closed return\n\n**Input:** returned payload/transport evidence, original activation and return\ncontract, expected consumer, exact subject/basis and supplied currentness,\ndependency and independence predicates/evidence. **Output/checks:** preserved raw\nreturn and provenance, deterministic binding/format/currentness findings and\nthe exact declared evaluations, predicates, domain outcomes and residuals that\nwere actually returned. Identify stale/wrong-subject/wrong-basis, missing,\nduplicate and conflicting evidence without dropping it; expose non-consumable\nsupport/gaps to the declared consumer. **Limit:** do not relabel a historical\nverdict as a new verdict, manufacture a result for an unperformed evaluation or\ntreat schema validity as semantic assessment/acceptance. A transport failure is\nreported separately using the selected method contract. Owners:\n[FOUND](fd-source-owner-map.md#found) Results/Conjunction of results;\n[RF](fd-source-owner-map.md#rf) RF-012;\n[ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §3/7;\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §4.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-009 — Prepare independently acquirable review evidence\n\n**Input:** exact review claim/candidate and composition boundary, caller-selected\nsource, comparison subjects, proof/evidence population and method-owned\nindependence/exposure contract. **Output/checks:** independently resolvable raw\nauthority/candidate/proof acquisition routes, acquired content where requested,\nexact byte/record comparisons, and separate assertion/expected-result versus\nexecution provenance. Support expectation recording before candidate exposure\nand preserve the actual acquisition/exposure record under the supplied contract.\nWorkers can acquire their implementation/proof context; Reviewers can inspect\nthe actual candidate, tests/fixtures and source without author-only privileges.\n**Limit:** diffs and trace/binding checks are not semantic findings, an independent\nverdict or adoption of a review recommendation as disposition. Owners:\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §1–4/6;\n[ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §3/10/13–16;\n[EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §9/10/17/19 if selected.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-010 — Execute declared checks and method-owned joins\n\n**Input:** exact subject/observations, selected executable or reproducible\ndecidable predicate/proof contract and its provenance/domain/limits, or a\nselected method-owned conjunction/translation with required coverage and inputs.\n**Output/checks:** reproducible `F_D[v]` judgments for the properties actually\nevaluated, counterexamples/gaps, and joins computed only under the supplied\nqualified operator. Preserve source predicate, original domain outcomes,\nnot-performed assessments, uncovered obligations and incompatibilities as the\n","coordinates":{"lines":[121,179]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23","selected_sha256":"c03aa14772d36641555020e6f9f77cb78b09f