{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YX23gk6H5VF2hhgoyTYdp3","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:a0f97e77f4506cd2a83bfe01d152d0e2de78f6acbe68b2ea76af2232b1becd53\",\"sha256\":\"a0f97e77f4506cd2a83bfe01d152d0e2de78f6acbe68b2ea76af2232b1becd53\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-rfb-001\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=6434fdeb01566ed9518a736203a22eb25a493adc6b33b862c1c4958668d2a457]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Construction Reference-Frame Basis\\n\\n## Project frame basis\\n\\nThe owner instruction in T-001 selects independent implementation of `a_c` with\\na Graphify build tenant. The operative builder is installed STDO 2.5.1 RC2,\\nmanifest `3d860ff4c1746f06ac25295a9e205cffb8e7725869615ac77cf2304b70ff2782`.\\nThis initial source configuration binds construction and evaluation; Product\\nacceptance and release remain with the owner.\\n\\nThe [T-007 owner clarification](../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-007-executive-lifecycle-tooling.md#owner-instruction)\\nadditionally selects Product/requirement authoring for deterministic tools\\nsupporting F_P Executives, Workers and Reviewers. The\\n[source-owner map](requirements/fd-source-owner-map.md) binds exact provisional\\nSTDO3.0 contract clauses for derivation. It does not adopt that candidate as an\\noperative builder/consumer method, make its optional Executive profile\\nmandatory, or change the installed construction basis above. Tool design,\\nimplementation and qualification remain unperformed in this increment.\\n\\n| Frame | Question and evidence | Result boundary |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| F-CONTRACT | Does the common WHAT conserve exact calculus ownership and distinguish the eight families, semantic interpretation, encoding and external judgments? Inspect the exact calculus and common source. | Semantic/contract assessment; no implementation acceptance. |\\n| F-REALIZATION | Does the tenant preserve its declared model fragment and refuse unsupported or incoherent inputs? Inspect design, code, positive cases and counterexamples. | Declared mechanical properties only. |\\n| F-INTEGRATION | Does the real pinned Graphify builder/reader preserve the generated representation and support the documented use path? Exercise actual upstream code and retain exact identity and outputs. | Tested boundary compatibility only. |\\n| F-USEFULNESS | Does actual task use preserve sufficient meaning while reducing total accepted-result cost? Compare matched tasks, acquisition and corrections. | Remains open without a matched semantic-use trial. |\\n| F-TOOL-CONTRACT | Do the additional common requirements define deterministic inputs/outputs/checked properties for all three F_P actors, tracing methodology decisions to exact STDO3.0 owners rather than duplicating them? Inspect the frozen authored source and provisional owner map. | Source-contract review only; no target-method adoption, executable behavior or qualification. |\\n\\nEach result names its exact subject/basis, evaluator, evidence, verdict,\\nresiduals and invalidators. Verdicts are satisfied, falsified, indeterminate,\\nout_of_frame or invalid_basis. A mechanical success cannot close F-USEFULNESS.\\n\\nThe coordinating Executive delegates bounded work and does not mutate. A Writer\\nor Worker has a named operation and territory. Nonauthor review assesses source\\nand code before closure; Jim retains Product acceptance and release.\\n\\nT-007's Writer owns only its named common source/ticket territory; its frozen\\nreturn is assessed by a nonauthor. This source increment establishes no new\\nconsumer frame set, lifecycle state, actor configuration or method-owned\\ndecision rule. Future tool checks bind the caller's exact selected contracts.\\n\\n## T-008 owner-selected RC9 execution configuration\\n\\nJim's [implementation instruction](../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-008-fd-tenant-implementation.md#owner-instruction)\\nselects Claude RC9 for the bounded Graphify-tenant implementation of the\\ncommitted deterministic-support WHAT. Source\\n`c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3`, custody\\n`3a2097137c3588ba44b98e3ea801ac7f2be1daf0` and standards tree\\n`98de394b352179c25dfa63b0b59a9b6bdd43632d` bind the exact work-scoped candidate.\\nThe [RC9 support binding](../build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-method-claude-rc9.json)\\nrecords exact member bytes and owner clauses. This explicit candidate dogfood\\nselects EXECUTIVE_BASELINE and DESIGN_MODULE for this engagement; it changes\\nno installed construction constitution, common derivation history, calculus\\nidentity, Product composition or release status.\\n\\nExecutive `/root` selects bounded dependency-ready work, consumes exact closed\\nreturns and records dispositions through an activated Writer. It mutates no\\ncandidate/Product/worktree bytes while Executive. Writer/Workers receive exact\\noperation/grant/territory and stop at return. Independent Reviewers acquire\\nsource/subject/proof themselves, record source-derived expectations before\\ncandidate exposure, edit no candidate and return to the Executive. A fresh\\nauthor context supplies no independence. All roles preserve RC9's existing\\nresult, admission, effects and return relations by reference; a_c defines no\\nreplacement lifecycle or role policy.\\n\\nThe T-008 design contract has a separately checked external bootstrap admission\\nreceipt bound to its exact digest and the owner's existing work instruction.\\nThis is bounded admission evidence, not qualification of the future public\\nadmission tool or admission of the upstream outcome. Each subsequent code,\\nreview, recording or checkpoint activation needs its own exact granted contract.\\nNo repeated human permission ceremony follows where current authority already\\ncovers the action. Jim retains scope, meaning, Product acceptance and release.\\n\\n| Work-scoped frame | Selected owner and bounded question | Result boundary |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Executive | Claude RC9 EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §§6/8/12/19; select/consume/dispose within T-008's implementation mandate and current source basis. | No Executive mutation or inferred owner acceptance. |\\n| Writer/Worker design/construction | RC9 §§9/12/19, ACTIVATION §§1–3/7 and DESIGN_MODULE §§5/7; construct the exact selected design/code/proof with a named operation and territory. | Candidate availability and separate performed-check results; stop at return. |\\n| Nonauthor review | RC9 §10/17/19, EVALUATION §§2–4 and ASSURANCE; source-first independent assessment of frozen exact design/runtime/proof within the supplied independence basis. | Evidence-bound findings; no repairs, priority, disposition or self-acceptance. |\\n\\nInitial design is a [candidate](../build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md).\\nImplementation and ordinary-use qualification are downstream of its required\\nassessment/disposition; benefit, full calculus conformance and release remain\\nunqualified. Deferred common requirements are not silently relabeled by this\\nwork-scoped configuration record.\\n\",\"coordinates\":null,\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"5cda45d1f267a3f221703c7fcc42b100c7997d3a98c015b7faf4f46b21222b8a\",\"selected_sha256\":\"5cda45d1f267a3f221703c7fcc42b100c7997d3a98c015b7faf4f46b21222b8a\",\"size_bytes\":6446,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"5cda45d1f267a3f221703c7fcc42b100c7997d