{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P5oQEgBvY84T4cUy9XdpTH","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:2662b33c9fb76f4fcf70ddf4c2113d71f48bae0e01a191e1dca578a1405850c5\",\"sha256\":\"2662b33c9fb76f4fcf70ddf4c2113d71f48bae0e01a191e1dca578a1405850c5\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-found-790\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=c9e96ec0630f2edb458379f555fc2b950aa8ef7e91632ac1a874bf0f35e60597]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### Results\\n\\nEvery performed evaluation returns one value of the core result algebra,\\ndirectly or as a refined value mapped into it (P5):\\n\\n| Value | Meaning |\\n|---|---|\\n| `satisfied` | the declared predicate holds on the exact basis |\\n| `falsified` | a declared counterexample defeats it |\\n| `indeterminate` | the available admissible evidence cannot decide it |\\n| `out_of_frame` | the evaluation requires an undeclared material relation or capability |\\n| `invalid_basis` | the subject or basis cannot support the evaluation |\\n\\nThis core is the only one. Results of constraints, judgments, frame\\nevaluations, stops, work steps and effects are stated in it or in a\\nrefinement mapped into it, so that results from any members combine under\\none rule ([Conjunction of results](#conjunction-of-results)). Purpose and\\nmaterial relation: no combination can report success while a failure, an\\nundecided question, an unperformed evaluation or an uncertain effect\\nremains, and none of these can be mistaken for another (P5, P6).\\n\\nRecording. A result records its core value together with the predicate\\nevaluated and the original domain outcome, which is the refined value\\nwhere a refinement produced it. A mapping into the core never owns domain\\nmeaning: the member, profile or adopting Product that defines the refined\\nvalue keeps it, and a consumer that needs the domain distinction reads the\\ndomain outcome, never the core value alone (P1, P6).\\n\\nStanding. The standing of a result is what it establishes about its\\npredicate; it is distinct from the standing of a commitment (§1). Only\\n`satisfied` establishes the predicate. `falsified` establishes that the\\npredicate fails and names the counterexample. `indeterminate`,\\n`out_of_frame` and `invalid_basis` establish neither, and each names what\\nwould decide: the evidence, the missing relation or capability with its\\nowner where the subject gives one, or the basis repair. By support for the\\npredicate, `satisfied` stands above each other value, and the other four\\nare not ordered among themselves.\\n\\nNo refinement or mapping raises a result's standing (P5, P6):\\n\\n- a falsified or failed result never maps to a satisfied or successful one;\\n- a result that admissible evidence cannot decide never maps to\\n  `satisfied`;\\n- an evaluation that was not performed stays distinct from one whose\\n  evidence cannot decide: it has no\\n  [closed result](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse), and it is never mapped\\n  to `indeterminate` or to any other core value;\\n- an effect whose completion is unknown never maps to no effect or to\\n  completed.\\n\\nNot performed. An evaluation that is required or planned and was not\\nperformed has no closed result; an actor cannot report an evaluation it\\ndid not perform (P6). Nothing is coerced to success: a failed,\\nindeterminate, out-of-frame, out-of-scope or invalid-basis result follows\\nthe declared result algebra and returns its own value under it, never\\n`satisfied`, and a missing result, being no result, enters every\\nconjunction over it as a gap: a planned assessment without a closed result\\nwhere an assessment was planned, and uncovered coverage where none was.\\nThis\\nconserves\\n[RF-012](stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md#rf-012-closed-results),\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[790,850]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\",\"selected_sha256\":\"434abc238d13a2587a0d82146898a1328fe080c25618e42f03a4ba87e4d4ce15\",\"size_bytes\":3253,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[790,850]},\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"5f05b0fc-673b-4ec3-b662-25d49cb4724a","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:45:37.466Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:2662b33c9fb76f4fcf70ddf4c2113d71f48bae0e01a191e1dca578a1405850c5\",\"sha256\":\"2662b33c9fb76f4fcf70ddf4c2113d71f48bae0e01a191e1dca578a1405850c5\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-found-790\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=c9e96ec0630f2edb458379f555fc2b950aa8ef7e91632ac1a874bf0f35e60597]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### Results\\n\\nEvery performed evaluation returns one value of the core result algebra,\\ndirectly or as a refined value mapped into it (P5):\\n\\n| Value | Meaning |\\n|---|---|\\n| `satisfied` | the declared predicate holds on the exact basis |\\n| `falsified` | a declared counterexample defeats it |\\n| `indeterminate` | the available admissible evidence cannot decide it |\\n| `out_of_frame` | the evaluation requires an undeclared material relation or capability |\\n| `invalid_basis` | the subject or basis cannot support the evaluation |\\n\\nThis core is the only one. Results of constraints, judgments, frame\\nevaluations, stops, work steps and effects are stated in it or in a\\nrefinement mapped into it, so that results from any members combine under\\none rule ([Conjunction of results](#conjunction-of-results)). Purpose and\\nmaterial relation: no combination can report success while a failure, an\\nundecided question, an unperformed evaluation or an uncertain effect\\nremains, and none of these can be mistaken for another (P5, P6).\\n\\nRecording. A result records its core value together with the predicate\\nevaluated and the original domain outcome, which is the refined value\\nwhere a refinement produced it. A mapping into the core never owns domain\\nmeaning: the member, profile or adopting Product that defines the refined\\nvalue keeps it, and a consumer that needs the domain distinction reads the\\ndomain outcome, never the core value alone (P1, P6).\\n\\nStanding. The standing of a result is what it establishes about its\\npredicate; it is distinct from the standing of a commitment (§1). Only\\n`satisfied` establishes the predicate. `falsified` establishes that the\\npredicate fails and names the counterexample. `indeterminate`,\\n`out_of_frame` and `invalid_basis` establish neither, and each names what\\nwould decide: the evidence, the missing relation or capability with its\\nowner where the subject gives one, or the basis repair. By support for the\\npredicate, `satisfied` stands above each other value, and the other four\\nare not ordered among themselves.\\n\\nNo refinement or mapping raises a result's standing (P5, P6):\\n\\n- a falsified or failed result never maps to a satisfied or successful one;\\n- a result that admissible evidence cannot decide never maps to\\n  `satisfied`;\\n- an evaluation that was not performed stays distinct from one whose\\n  evidence cannot decide: it has no\\n  [closed result](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse), and it is never mapped\\n  to `indeterminate` or to any other core value;\\n- an effect whose completion is unknown never maps to no effect or to\\n  completed.\\n\\nNot performed. An evaluation that is required or planned and was not\\nperformed has no closed result; an actor cannot report an evaluation it\\ndid not perform (P6). Nothing is coerced to success: a failed,\\nindeterminate, out-of-frame, out-of-scope or invalid-basis result follows\\nthe declared result algebra and returns its own value under it, never\\n`satisfied`, and a missing result, being no result, enters every\\nconjunction over it as a gap: a planned assessment without a closed result\\nwhere an assessment was planned, and uncovered coverage where none was.\\nThis\\nconserves\\n[RF-012](stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md#rf-012-closed-results),\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[790,850]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\",\"selected_sha256\":\"434abc238d13a2587a0d82146898a1328fe080c25618e42f03a4ba87e4d4ce15\",\"size_bytes\":3253,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[790,850]},\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:2662b33c9fb76f4fcf70ddf4c2113d71f48bae0e01a191e1dca578a1405850c5","sha256":"2662b33c9fb76f4fcf70ddf4c2113d71f48bae0e01a191e1dca578a1405850c5"},"id":"p2-read-found-790","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=c9e96ec0630f2edb458379f555fc2b950aa8ef7e91632ac1a874bf0f35e60597]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"### Results\n\nEvery performed evaluation returns one value of the core result algebra,\ndirectly or as a refined value mapped into it (P5):\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `satisfied` | the declared predicate holds on the exact basis |\n| `falsified` | a declared counterexample defeats it |\n| `indeterminate` | the available admissible evidence cannot decide it |\n| `out_of_frame` | the evaluation requires an undeclared material relation or capability |\n| `invalid_basis` | the subject or basis cannot support the evaluation |\n\nThis core is the only one. Results of constraints, judgments, frame\nevaluations, stops, work steps and effects are stated in it or in a\nrefinement mapped into it, so that results from any members combine under\none rule ([Conjunction of results](#conjunction-of-results)). Purpose and\nmaterial relation: no combination can report success while a failure, an\nundecided question, an unperformed evaluation or an uncertain effect\nremains, and none of these can be mistaken for another (P5, P6).\n\nRecording. A result records its core value together with the predicate\nevaluated and the original domain outcome, which is the refined value\nwhere a refinement produced it. A mapping into the core never owns domain\nmeaning: the member, profile or adopting Product that defines the refined\nvalue keeps it, and a consumer that needs the domain distinction reads the\ndomain outcome, never the core value alone (P1, P6).\n\nStanding. The standing of a result is what it establishes about its\npredicate; it is distinct from the standing of a commitment (§1). Only\n`satisfied` establishes the predicate. `falsified` establishes that the\npredicate fails and names the counterexample. `indeterminate`,\n`out_of_frame` and `invalid_basis` establish neither, and each names what\nwould decide: the evidence, the missing relation or capability with its\nowner where the subject gives one, or the basis repair. By support for the\npredicate, `satisfied` stands above each other value, and the other four\nare not ordered among themselves.\n\nNo refinement or mapping raises a result's standing (P5, P6):\n\n- a falsified or failed result never maps to a satisfied or successful one;\n- a result that admissible evidence cannot decide never maps to\n  `satisfied`;\n- an evaluation that was not performed stays distinct from one whose\n  evidence cannot decide: it has no\n  [closed result](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse), and it is never mapped\n  to `indeterminate` or to any other core value;\n- an effect whose completion is unknown never maps to no effect or to\n  completed.\n\nNot performed. An evaluation that is required or planned and was not\nperformed has no closed result; an actor cannot report an evaluation it\ndid not perform (P6). Nothing is coerced to success: a failed,\nindeterminate, out-of-frame, out-of-scope or invalid-basis result follows\nthe declared result algebra and returns its own value under it, never\n`satisfied`, and a missing result, being no result, enters every\nconjunction over it as a gap: a planned assessment without a closed result\nwhere an assessment was planned, and uncovered coverage where none was.\nThis\nconserves\n[RF-012](stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md#rf-012-closed-results),\n","coordinates":{"lines":[790,850]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f","selected_sha256":"434abc238d13a2587a0d82146898a1328fe080c25618e42f03a4ba87e4d4ce15","size_bytes":3253,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"FOUNDATIONS.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[790,850]},"sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P5oQEgBvY84T4cUy9XdpTH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
