{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EmwjL9pa1xwUzdtMyDgaRA","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:be3de0f068dba017578294970b3bdf045061a890d6c49f13dce739b7e449d5a3\",\"sha256\":\"be3de0f068dba017578294970b3bdf045061a890d6c49f13dce739b7e449d5a3\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-found-1008\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=a17a4f41f7e7250ac4eada9dc6172a35a8df58b71c6c2fa01e6e2386104f2d02]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### Conjunction of results\\n\\nConjunction combines results into one result for a composite predicate: a\\nclaim made of component claims, a decision over several evaluations, or\\nthe outer contract of composed steps. It is defined here once, over the\\ncore. A member or profile that combines results applies this rule and\\ndeclares only the choices it leaves open (P4a, P4b, P5, P6). Purpose and\\nmaterial relation: failure, undecidability, non-performance and uncertain\\neffects stay distinct after combination, so a composite can neither report\\nsuccess nor hide which kind of gap it has while one of them remains in\\nwhat it requires.\\n\\nA conjunction takes three inputs and keeps them apart:\\n\\n1. the closed results returned, each a core value with its predicate and\\n   domain outcome;\\n2. the planned assessments that have no closed result applicable to the\\n   composite: evaluations the composite requires that were not performed,\\n   or whose result is absent, stale, bound to another subject or basis, or\\n   incapable of establishing its claim;\\n3. the required coverage that no planned assessment addresses: for a\\n   required obligation set R and the coverage C that the planned\\n   assessments admit, the uncovered coverage R minus C.\\n\\nGaps. A conjunction with any item in the second or third input is never\\n`satisfied`. Its record names which kind of gap it has, not performed,\\nuncovered or both, and each item. An uncovered obligation is never\\nreported as satisfied or as an omitted planned assessment; a planned\\nassessment without a closed result is never reported as uncovered or as an\\n`indeterminate` component.\\n\\nStale results. A held result is stale for a composite when the basis it\\nbinds is not the basis the composite requires of that component, because\\na later state has superseded or advanced it or because it binds another\\nsubject or basis (§2, Basis). Two questions stay apart, so that one\\ncomposite has one reported value (P3, P5, P6):\\n\\n- an evaluation performed on a subject or basis that is stale, advanced,\\n  ambiguous or mismatched against the one it must bind returns\\n  `invalid_basis` for its own predicate, or is reactivated on the current\\n  basis; [RF-005](REFERENCE_FRAME.md#rf-005-exact-basis-and-coordinates)\\n  states this law over frames, and a conjunction that receives that\\n  `invalid_basis` holds it as a returned result;\\n- a component whose only held result is stale has no closed result\\n  applicable to the composite: on the basis the composite requires, its\\n  evaluation was not performed. It is a planned assessment without a\\n  closed result, in the second input, and a gap. Its stale value is\\n  neither counted as a returned result nor relabelled `invalid_basis` for\\n  the composite, and it stays in the record with its own basis;\\n- the declared basis relations disagree (Reported value below) only among\\n  returned results, each bound to the basis the composite requires of it,\\n  whose bases the declared rule requires to agree or to join in a coherent\\n  composite basis, and which do not.\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1008,1060]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\",\"selected_sha256\":\"b12f80c73b9bceeebdec290027851835d6cc3f9660fbed3edf633c30b1589ef0\",\"size_bytes\":3018,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1008,1060]},\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"a1d241a5-473a-4e22-8b80-b801904df7fd","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:45:40.653Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:be3de0f068dba017578294970b3bdf045061a890d6c49f13dce739b7e449d5a3\",\"sha256\":\"be3de0f068dba017578294970b3bdf045061a890d6c49f13dce739b7e449d5a3\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-found-1008\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=a17a4f41f7e7250ac4eada9dc6172a35a8df58b71c6c2fa01e6e2386104f2d02]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### Conjunction of results\\n\\nConjunction combines results into one result for a composite predicate: a\\nclaim made of component claims, a decision over several evaluations, or\\nthe outer contract of composed steps. It is defined here once, over the\\ncore. A member or profile that combines results applies this rule and\\ndeclares only the choices it leaves open (P4a, P4b, P5, P6). Purpose and\\nmaterial relation: failure, undecidability, non-performance and uncertain\\neffects stay distinct after combination, so a composite can neither report\\nsuccess nor hide which kind of gap it has while one of them remains in\\nwhat it requires.\\n\\nA conjunction takes three inputs and keeps them apart:\\n\\n1. the closed results returned, each a core value with its predicate and\\n   domain outcome;\\n2. the planned assessments that have no closed result applicable to the\\n   composite: evaluations the composite requires that were not performed,\\n   or whose result is absent, stale, bound to another subject or basis, or\\n   incapable of establishing its claim;\\n3. the required coverage that no planned assessment addresses: for a\\n   required obligation set R and the coverage C that the planned\\n   assessments admit, the uncovered coverage R minus C.\\n\\nGaps. A conjunction with any item in the second or third input is never\\n`satisfied`. Its record names which kind of gap it has, not performed,\\nuncovered or both, and each item. An uncovered obligation is never\\nreported as satisfied or as an omitted planned assessment; a planned\\nassessment without a closed result is never reported as uncovered or as an\\n`indeterminate` component.\\n\\nStale results. A held result is stale for a composite when the basis it\\nbinds is not the basis the composite requires of that component, because\\na later state has superseded or advanced it or because it binds another\\nsubject or basis (§2, Basis). Two questions stay apart, so that one\\ncomposite has one reported value (P3, P5, P6):\\n\\n- an evaluation performed on a subject or basis that is stale, advanced,\\n  ambiguous or mismatched against the one it must bind returns\\n  `invalid_basis` for its own predicate, or is reactivated on the current\\n  basis; [RF-005](REFERENCE_FRAME.md#rf-005-exact-basis-and-coordinates)\\n  states this law over frames, and a conjunction that receives that\\n  `invalid_basis` holds it as a returned result;\\n- a component whose only held result is stale has no closed result\\n  applicable to the composite: on the basis the composite requires, its\\n  evaluation was not performed. It is a planned assessment without a\\n  closed result, in the second input, and a gap. Its stale value is\\n  neither counted as a returned result nor relabelled `invalid_basis` for\\n  the composite, and it stays in the record with its own basis;\\n- the declared basis relations disagree (Reported value below) only among\\n  returned results, each bound to the basis the composite requires of it,\\n  whose bases the declared rule requires to agree or to join in a coherent\\n  composite basis, and which do not.\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1008,1060]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\",\"selected_sha256\":\"b12f80c73b9bceeebdec290027851835d6cc3f9660fbed3edf633c30b1589ef0\",\"size_bytes\":3018,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1008,1060]},\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:be3de0f068dba017578294970b3bdf045061a890d6c49f13dce739b7e449d5a3","sha256":"be3de0f068dba017578294970b3bdf045061a890d6c49f13dce739b7e449d5a3"},"id":"p2-read-found-1008","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=a17a4f41f7e7250ac4eada9dc6172a35a8df58b71c6c2fa01e6e2386104f2d02]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"### Conjunction of results\n\nConjunction combines results into one result for a composite predicate: a\nclaim made of component claims, a decision over several evaluations, or\nthe outer contract of composed steps. It is defined here once, over the\ncore. A member or profile that combines results applies this rule and\ndeclares only the choices it leaves open (P4a, P4b, P5, P6). Purpose and\nmaterial relation: failure, undecidability, non-performance and uncertain\neffects stay distinct after combination, so a composite can neither report\nsuccess nor hide which kind of gap it has while one of them remains in\nwhat it requires.\n\nA conjunction takes three inputs and keeps them apart:\n\n1. the closed results returned, each a core value with its predicate and\n   domain outcome;\n2. the planned assessments that have no closed result applicable to the\n   composite: evaluations the composite requires that were not performed,\n   or whose result is absent, stale, bound to another subject or basis, or\n   incapable of establishing its claim;\n3. the required coverage that no planned assessment addresses: for a\n   required obligation set R and the coverage C that the planned\n   assessments admit, the uncovered coverage R minus C.\n\nGaps. A conjunction with any item in the second or third input is never\n`satisfied`. Its record names which kind of gap it has, not performed,\nuncovered or both, and each item. An uncovered obligation is never\nreported as satisfied or as an omitted planned assessment; a planned\nassessment without a closed result is never reported as uncovered or as an\n`indeterminate` component.\n\nStale results. A held result is stale for a composite when the basis it\nbinds is not the basis the composite requires of that component, because\na later state has superseded or advanced it or because it binds another\nsubject or basis (§2, Basis). Two questions stay apart, so that one\ncomposite has one reported value (P3, P5, P6):\n\n- an evaluation performed on a subject or basis that is stale, advanced,\n  ambiguous or mismatched against the one it must bind returns\n  `invalid_basis` for its own predicate, or is reactivated on the current\n  basis; [RF-005](REFERENCE_FRAME.md#rf-005-exact-basis-and-coordinates)\n  states this law over frames, and a conjunction that receives that\n  `invalid_basis` holds it as a returned result;\n- a component whose only held result is stale has no closed result\n  applicable to the composite: on the basis the composite requires, its\n  evaluation was not performed. It is a planned assessment without a\n  closed result, in the second input, and a gap. Its stale value is\n  neither counted as a returned result nor relabelled `invalid_basis` for\n  the composite, and it stays in the record with its own basis;\n- the declared basis relations disagree (Reported value below) only among\n  returned results, each bound to the basis the composite requires of it,\n  whose bases the declared rule requires to agree or to join in a coherent\n  composite basis, and which do not.\n","coordinates":{"lines":[1008,1060]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f","selected_sha256":"b12f80c73b9bceeebdec290027851835d6cc3f9660fbed3edf633c30b1589ef0","size_bytes":3018,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"FOUNDATIONS.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[1008,1060]},"sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EmwjL9pa1xwUzdtMyDgaRA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
