{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VsAwqPH4cDDDM5ZZBbYm8p","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:49f86e9405faf8f42eba6b29eba5b55a17c7399e46df7af40ec3ba60e8304a2e\",\"sha256\":\"49f86e9405faf8f42eba6b29eba5b55a17c7399e46df7af40ec3ba60e8304a2e\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-eval-178\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=408390f12a0a114e966c7c8982bc6507ff84c294de10876aba29db1b7a9488bd]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"## 3. Independent assessment\\n\\nA constructor's self-review is construction output, not assessment. Where\\npromotion needs independent assessment, the assessor evaluates the exact\\nlive subject, authority paths, proof and installed state, not the\\nconstructor's summary (P6, and P0 with its premise that a step's output is\\na candidate until evaluated; instance premise (c) of §1 Foundation to law;\\nconserves\\n[UP-007](stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/TICKET_METHOD.md#execution-and-verification-authority-separation-stdo-up-007)).\\nThis section decides what counts as independent assessment. Which\\nboundaries require it is a policy choice of the Spec Method, owned by\\n[TICKETS §7 Execution and verification authority separation](TICKETS.md#execution-and-verification-authority-separation-up-007);\\na governing basis may add boundaries.\\n\\nProtocol: where method qualification applies\\n([§7 Method self-qualification](#method-self-qualification)), the subject is\\nfrozen by identity before material reference exposure; elsewhere it is\\nstabilised by an immutable identity or an equivalent exact-subject relation\\nsufficient for the claimed assessment. The assessor records its\\nexpectations from the governing source before opening the candidate; it\\nreads the subject at that identity or relation, never a mutable working\\ntree; it makes no repair; it does not assess its\\nown authorship. Reusing the constructor's judgment does not satisfy\\nindependence; shared mechanical evidence may be reused, judgment may not\\n(ACTIVATION §7). Binding a returned assessment to its producer, subject,\\nbasis and evidence authenticates the result; it establishes neither the\\nassertion provenance of its expected answer nor the execution provenance\\nof its run, which\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Parallel derivation and mutual assurance](FOUNDATIONS.md#parallel-derivation-and-mutual-assurance)\\nrequires separately (P6, P3). Membership in a plan authenticates nothing,\\nan unauthenticated result satisfies no required assessment, and a result\\nbound to another subject satisfies no planned assessment\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results));\\nno cryptographic or transport protocol is prescribed for the binding (P6). Any post-exposure revision is a declared intervention: it\\nis either a method constituent with its own qualification boundary or a new\\nqualification subject, and it cannot retroactively make the original\\nfrozen construction pass. This law prescribes no actor type or count,\\nreview-round count, engine, prompt or orchestration (UP-022).\\n\\nAuthor identity is the party responsible for the content of a realised\\nsubject. It is distinct from actor identity, whoever performs one\\noperation, which is an identity and not an authority\\n([FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds)).\\nAuthorship is one of the conditions on\\nwhich the independence of an assessment rests; the evidence conditions are\\nthe other (P6, P3; provenance: the definition moves here from the build\\nbinding terms of SPEC_METHOD §11, which refers to it).\\n\\nIndependence rests on authorship and on the evidence conditions above, not\\non a new context. The assessor may read the same governing sources as the\\nconstructor. A fresh context alone establishes no independence, and it\\nsupplies no review authority the author lacks: an author that opens a\\nfresh context to review its own candidate is still its author, and its\\nreview is self-review, which stays construction output and cannot be\\nrelabelled as independent assessment (P6; UP-007 applied to a fresh\\ncontext). A contribution received from another author stays that\\nauthor's wherever it is carried, and that author's reading of it supplies\\nno independent acceptance of it (P6).\\n\\nIndependence across actor families is declared, not assumed. Whether two\\nactivations of one model family are independent for a semantic judgment is a\\npolicy the governing basis states for the claim; the default where it is not\\nstated is that they are not independent.\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[178,241]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"14f8816b1eb9cd146dd58a29bac35ea47a62e4e4b093b20f9892330e44922991\",\"selected_sha256\":\"6071ebc20a92517bd4d5e12b3820ed918901fa9168679b4b98615b7dc422ce34\",\"size_bytes\":4002,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"EVALUATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[178,241]},\"sha256\":\"14f8816b1eb9cd146dd58a29bac35ea47a62e4e4b093b20f9892330e44922991\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"082378b6-6915-4433-998f-0e66e9856f20","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:45:47.681Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:49f86e9405faf8f42eba6b29eba5b55a17c7399e46df7af40ec3ba60e8304a2e\",\"sha256\":\"49f86e9405faf8f42eba6b29eba5b55a17c7399e46df7af40ec3ba60e8304a2e\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-eval-178\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=408390f12a0a114e966c7c8982bc6507ff84c294de10876aba29db1b7a9488bd]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"## 3. Independent assessment\\n\\nA constructor's self-review is construction output, not assessment. Where\\npromotion needs independent assessment, the assessor evaluates the exact\\nlive subject, authority paths, proof and installed state, not the\\nconstructor's summary (P6, and P0 with its premise that a step's output is\\na candidate until evaluated; instance premise (c) of §1 Foundation to law;\\nconserves\\n[UP-007](stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/TICKET_METHOD.md#execution-and-verification-authority-separation-stdo-up-007)).\\nThis section decides what counts as independent assessment. Which\\nboundaries require it is a policy choice of the Spec Method, owned by\\n[TICKETS §7 Execution and verification authority separation](TICKETS.md#execution-and-verification-authority-separation-up-007);\\na governing basis may add boundaries.\\n\\nProtocol: where method qualification applies\\n([§7 Method self-qualification](#method-self-qualification)), the subject is\\nfrozen by identity before material reference exposure; elsewhere it is\\nstabilised by an immutable identity or an equivalent exact-subject relation\\nsufficient for the claimed assessment. The assessor records its\\nexpectations from the governing source before opening the candidate; it\\nreads the subject at that identity or relation, never a mutable working\\ntree; it makes no repair; it does not assess its\\nown authorship. Reusing the constructor's judgment does not satisfy\\nindependence; shared mechanical evidence may be reused, judgment may not\\n(ACTIVATION §7). Binding a returned assessment to its producer, subject,\\nbasis and evidence authenticates the result; it establishes neither the\\nassertion provenance of its expected answer nor the execution provenance\\nof its run, which\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Parallel derivation and mutual assurance](FOUNDATIONS.md#parallel-derivation-and-mutual-assurance)\\nrequires separately (P6, P3). Membership in a plan authenticates nothing,\\nan unauthenticated result satisfies no required assessment, and a result\\nbound to another subject satisfies no planned assessment\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results));\\nno cryptographic or transport protocol is prescribed for the binding (P6). Any post-exposure revision is a declared intervention: it\\nis either a method constituent with its own qualification boundary or a new\\nqualification subject, and it cannot retroactively make the original\\nfrozen construction pass. This law prescribes no actor type or count,\\nreview-round count, engine, prompt or orchestration (UP-022).\\n\\nAuthor identity is the party responsible for the content of a realised\\nsubject. It is distinct from actor identity, whoever performs one\\noperation, which is an identity and not an authority\\n([FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds)).\\nAuthorship is one of the conditions on\\nwhich the independence of an assessment rests; the evidence conditions are\\nthe other (P6, P3; provenance: the definition moves here from the build\\nbinding terms of SPEC_METHOD §11, which refers to it).\\n\\nIndependence rests on authorship and on the evidence conditions above, not\\non a new context. The assessor may read the same governing sources as the\\nconstructor. A fresh context alone establishes no independence, and it\\nsupplies no review authority the author lacks: an author that opens a\\nfresh context to review its own candidate is still its author, and its\\nreview is self-review, which stays construction output and cannot be\\nrelabelled as independent assessment (P6; UP-007 applied to a fresh\\ncontext). A contribution received from another author stays that\\nauthor's wherever it is carried, and that author's reading of it supplies\\nno independent acceptance of it (P6).\\n\\nIndependence across actor families is declared, not assumed. Whether two\\nactivations of one model family are independent for a semantic judgment is a\\npolicy the governing basis states for the claim; the default where it is not\\nstated is that they are not independent.\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[178,241]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"14f8816b1eb9cd146dd58a29bac35ea47a62e4e4b093b20f9892330e44922991\",\"selected_sha256\":\"6071ebc20a92517bd4d5e12b3820ed918901fa9168679b4b98615b7dc422ce34\",\"size_bytes\":4002,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"EVALUATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[178,241]},\"sha256\":\"14f8816b1eb9cd146dd58a29bac35ea47a62e4e4b093b20f9892330e44922991\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:49f86e9405faf8f42eba6b29eba5b55a17c7399e46df7af40ec3ba60e8304a2e","sha256":"49f86e9405faf8f42eba6b29eba5b55a17c7399e46df7af40ec3ba60e8304a2e"},"id":"p2-read-eval-178","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=408390f12a0a114e966c7c8982bc6507ff84c294de10876aba29db1b7a9488bd]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"## 3. Independent assessment\n\nA constructor's self-review is construction output, not assessment. Where\npromotion needs independent assessment, the assessor evaluates the exact\nlive subject, authority paths, proof and installed state, not the\nconstructor's summary (P6, and P0 with its premise that a step's output is\na candidate until evaluated; instance premise (c) of §1 Foundation to law;\nconserves\n[UP-007](stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/TICKET_METHOD.md#execution-and-verification-authority-separation-stdo-up-007)).\nThis section decides what counts as independent assessment. Which\nboundaries require it is a policy choice of the Spec Method, owned by\n[TICKETS §7 Execution and verification authority separation](TICKETS.md#execution-and-verification-authority-separation-up-007);\na governing basis may add boundaries.\n\nProtocol: where method qualification applies\n([§7 Method self-qualification](#method-self-qualification)), the subject is\nfrozen by identity before material reference exposure; elsewhere it is\nstabilised by an immutable identity or an equivalent exact-subject relation\nsufficient for the claimed assessment. The assessor records its\nexpectations from the governing source before opening the candidate; it\nreads the subject at that identity or relation, never a mutable working\ntree; it makes no repair; it does not assess its\nown authorship. Reusing the constructor's judgment does not satisfy\nindependence; shared mechanical evidence may be reused, judgment may not\n(ACTIVATION §7). Binding a returned assessment to its producer, subject,\nbasis and evidence authenticates the result; it establishes neither the\nassertion provenance of its expected answer nor the execution provenance\nof its run, which\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Parallel derivation and mutual assurance](FOUNDATIONS.md#parallel-derivation-and-mutual-assurance)\nrequires separately (P6, P3). Membership in a plan authenticates nothing,\nan unauthenticated result satisfies no required assessment, and a result\nbound to another subject satisfies no planned assessment\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results));\nno cryptographic or transport protocol is prescribed for the binding (P6). Any post-exposure revision is a declared intervention: it\nis either a method constituent with its own qualification boundary or a new\nqualification subject, and it cannot retroactively make the original\nfrozen construction pass. This law prescribes no actor type or count,\nreview-round count, engine, prompt or orchestration (UP-022).\n\nAuthor identity is the party responsible for the content of a realised\nsubject. It is distinct from actor identity, whoever performs one\noperation, which is an identity and not an authority\n([FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds)).\nAuthorship is one of the conditions on\nwhich the independence of an assessment rests; the evidence conditions are\nthe other (P6, P3; provenance: the definition moves here from the build\nbinding terms of SPEC_METHOD §11, which refers to it).\n\nIndependence rests on authorship and on the evidence conditions above, not\non a new context. The assessor may read the same governing sources as the\nconstructor. A fresh context alone establishes no independence, and it\nsupplies no review authority the author lacks: an author that opens a\nfresh context to review its own candidate is still its author, and its\nreview is self-review, which stays construction output and cannot be\nrelabelled as independent assessment (P6; UP-007 applied to a fresh\ncontext). A contribution received from another author stays that\nauthor's wherever it is carried, and that author's reading of it supplies\nno independent acceptance of it (P6).\n\nIndependence across actor families is declared, not assumed. Whether two\nactivations of one model family are independent for a semantic judgment is a\npolicy the governing basis states for the claim; the default where it is not\nstated is that they are not independent.\n\n","coordinates":{"lines":[178,241]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"14f8816b1eb9cd146dd58a29bac35ea47a62e4e4b093b20f9892330e44922991","selected_sha256":"6071ebc20a92517bd4d5e12b3820ed918901fa9168679b4b98615b7dc422ce34","size_bytes":4002,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"EVALUATION.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[178,241]},"sha256":"14f8816b1eb9cd146dd58a29bac35ea47a62e4e4b093b20f9892330e44922991"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VsAwqPH4cDDDM5ZZBbYm8p","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAzEKfnYorEcBk2TzecD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E5tQYvawMmRRaZiMU1rFg4","name":"mcp__ac_review__source_read","input":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-eval-242","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"EVALUATION.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[242,309]},"sha256":"14f8816b1eb9cd146dd58a29bac35ea47a62e4e4b093b20f9892330e44922991"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6476,"cache_read_input_tokens":173341,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6476},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"a79153ed-4faf-44b9-94c1-5d7330fdbbf9","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:45:49.770Z","request_id":"req_011CgAzEKNvhFk5ANoo3Yu33","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01E5tQYvawMmRRaZiMU1rFg4":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-eval-242","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"EVALUATION.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[242,309]},"sha256":"14f8816b1eb9cd146dd58a29bac35ea47a62e4e4b093b20f9892330e44922991"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01E5tQYvawMmRRaZiMU1rFg4","display_name":"Source Read","server_display_name":"a_c.graphify.fd-support","tool_name":"source.read"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E5tQYvawMmRRaZiMU1rFg4","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:d77b6f60a2e633c2b0033f796366375e31407a632cf172a951c85bb58187522b\",\"sha256\":\"d77b6f60a2e633c2b0033f796366375e31407a632cf172a951c85bb58187522b\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-eval-242\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=cac43b43206209571f2888a45df3108b11b08e6aa50dfd2a8b6bd014198e1459]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"## 4. Review results\\n\\nA review returns one core result\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4, Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results)) for each declared\\npredicate it evaluated, with: the exact subject and basis, the evidence\\nconsulted, the findings ranked by consequence, each finding's evidence and\\nthe smallest bounded correction, the residual uncertainty, and the\\ninvalidation conditions. A declared predicate the review planned and did\\nnot evaluate has no result (FOUNDATIONS §4, Results). The review names it\\nas not performed and reports no core value for it, neither\\n`indeterminate` nor `falsified`, so that conjunction keeps it apart from\\nan undecided predicate and from required coverage that no planned\\nassessment addresses\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4, Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results);\\nP5, P6). It may recommend a disposition\\n([ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#3-step-results-and-disposition)), which is\\nevidence only and never a disposition; it does not apply one. A finding\\nwithout evidence a consumer can chase is commentary.\\n\\n### Result and triage projection\\n\\nWhere a review returns findings with technical triage, the triage is the\\nassessor's evidence-bound assessment of each finding against the exact\\nevaluated claim and basis. Severity, the assessor's grade of consequence,\\nis evaluation evidence. Priority, the effect on the current promotion\\nboundary and the disposition are the decision owner's (ACTIVATION §1,\\nRoles and delegation; when a finding can block is\\n[§5, When a finding blocks promotion](#when-a-finding-blocks-promotion))\\nand stay distinct values even where a\\nProduct-defined policy maps one to another. A recommended disposition\\nis evidence for the decision owner: it is not a disposition, a\\npriority or a boundary effect, and it is never adopted mechanically (P6,\\nRF-007). The fields of a triage are declared by the profile that adopts it, and\\nthe scales it uses are bound by the adopting Product (P2, P6; provenance\\n[reviewer result and triage projection](stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#reviewer-result-and-triage-projection)).\\n\\nThe projection of the finding-level triage payload is total over the core\\nvalues of [FOUNDATIONS §4, Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results). A predicate\\nnot performed has no result and so no triage payload; the payload class\\n`indeterminate` never stands for it. The payload classes `complete`,\\n`indeterminate` and `not_applicable` classify the triage only; they are\\nnot new results, dispositions, priorities or lifecycle states (P5, P1).\\n\\n| Core result | Finding and triage payload | Decision-owner consumption constraint |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| satisfied | an explicit no-finding state; triage `not_applicable`; evidence, residuals and invalidation stay present | priority and boundary effect are `not_applicable` to this result unless another exact consumed result supplies a finding |\\n| falsified | one or more exact findings; triage `complete` where supported, keeping `indeterminate` fields where evidence cannot close them | apply the Product-owned priority and boundary policy without mapping severity mechanically to a disposition |\\n| indeterminate | a partial finding or observation state; triage `indeterminate`; the exact evidence gaps and residual uncertainty | keep the uncertainty or reactivate a capable evaluation; do not consume it as satisfaction or as a closed finding |\\n| out_of_frame | the evaluated claim needs an undeclared material relation or evaluator capability; triage `indeterminate`; the missing relation or capability and the exact reconfiguration pressure are named | refine or reconfigure a capable activation and keep the claim unresolved; do not consume the result as satisfaction or falsification |\\n| invalid_basis | a basis failure; triage `not_applicable`; invalidation evidence and basis-repair pressure | refuse to consume the result and return through the declared basis re-entry relation |\\n\\nAn adjacent observation outside the evaluated claim does not replace the\\nclaim-relative result. The assessor returns it separately, with triage\\n`not_applicable` to that claim and the exact repricing or re-entry\\npressure; the decision owner returns it to its declared owner without\\ncreating a claim-relative block, or another review round, from its\\nseverity alone (P6, P2).\\n\\nThe assessor returns to the decision owner, not to the constructor. It does\\nnot edit the candidate, direct the repair or authorise continuation (P6,\\n§3).\\n\\nPurpose and material relation of this projection's generality: the\\npredecessor stated it for the Reviewer and the Executive only. Stating it\\nfor any assessor and decision owner gives every configuration the same\\nseparation of severity, priority, boundary effect and disposition, and\\nEXECUTIVE_BASELINE keeps the Reviewer and Executive instance (P6).\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[242,309]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"14f8816b1eb9cd146dd58a29bac35ea47a62e4e4b093b20f9892330e44922991\",\"selected_sha256\":\"b19acbc01df2a64aeb91c274750a47ba212e1024790c4c5d380e066dde3d4219\",\"size_bytes\":4801,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"EVALUATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[242,309]},\"sha256\":\"14f8816b1eb9cd146dd58a29bac35ea47a62e4e4b093b20f9892330e44922991\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"efc7fc8c-7210-4ce0-9488-5e62739239b6","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:45:50.250Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:d77b6f60a2e633c2b0033f796366375e31407a632cf172a951c85bb58187522b\",\"sha256\":\"d77b6f60a2e633c2b0033f796366375e31407a632cf172a951c85bb58187522b\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-eval-242\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=cac43b43206209571f2888a45df3108b11b08e6aa50dfd2a8b6bd014198e1459]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"## 4. Review results\\n\\nA review returns one core result\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4, Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results)) for each declared\\npredicate it evaluated, with: the exact subject and basis, the evidence\\nconsulted, the findings ranked by consequence, each finding's evidence and\\nthe smallest bounded correction, the residual uncertainty, and the\\ninvalidation conditions. A declared predicate the review planned and did\\nnot evaluate has no result (FOUNDATIONS §4, Results). The review names it\\nas not performed and reports no core value for it, neither\\n`indeterminate` nor `falsified`, so that conjunction keeps it apart from\\nan undecided predicate and from required coverage that no planned\\nassessment addresses\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4, Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results);\\nP5, P6). It may recommend a disposition\\n([ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#3-step-results-and-disposition)), which is\\nevidence only and never a disposition; it does not apply one. A finding\\nwithout evidence a consumer can chase is commentary.\\n\\n### Result and triage projection\\n\\nWhere a review returns findings with technical triage, the triage is the\\nassessor's evidence-bound assessment of each finding against the exact\\nevaluated claim and basis. Severity, the assessor's grade of consequence,\\nis evaluation evidence. Priority, the effect on the current promotion\\nboundary and the disposition are the decision owner's (ACTIVATION §1,\\nRoles and delegation; when a finding can block is\\n[§5, When a finding blocks promotion](#when-a-finding-blocks-promotion))\\nand stay distinct values even where a\\nProduct-defined policy maps one to another. A recommended disposition\\nis evidence for the decision owner: it is not a disposition, a\\npriority or a boundary effect, and it is never adopted mechanically (P6,\\nRF-007). The fields of a triage are declared by the profile that adopts it, and\\nthe scales it uses are bound by the adopting Product (P2, P6; provenance\\n[reviewer result and triage projection](stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#reviewer-result-and-triage-projection)).\\n\\nThe projection of the finding-level triage payload is total over the core\\nvalues of [FOUNDATIONS §4, Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results). A predicate\\nnot performed has no result and so no triage payload; the payload class\\n`indeterminate` never stands for it. The payload classes `complete`,\\n`indeterminate` and `not_applicable` classify the triage only; they are\\nnot new results, dispositions, priorities or lifecycle states (P5, P1).\\n\\n| Core result | Finding and triage payload | Decision-owner consumption constraint |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| satisfied | an explicit no-finding state; triage `not_applicable`; evidence, residuals and invalidation stay present | priority and boundary effect are `not_applicable` to this result unless another exact consumed result supplies a finding |\\n| falsified | one or more exact findings; triage `complete` where supported, keeping `indeterminate` fields where evidence cannot close them | apply the Product-owned priority and boundary policy without mapping severity mechanically to a disposition |\\n| indeterminate | a partial finding or observation state; triage `indeterminate`; the exact evidence gaps and residual uncertainty | keep the uncertainty or reactivate a capable evaluation; do not consume it as satisfaction or as a closed finding |\\n| out_of_frame | the evaluated claim needs an undeclared material relation or evaluator capability; triage `indeterminate`; the missing relation or capability and the exact reconfiguration pressure are named | refine or reconfigure a capable activation and keep the claim unresolved; do not consume the result as satisfaction or falsification |\\n| invalid_basis | a basis failure; triage `not_applicable`; invalidation evidence and basis-repair pressure | refuse to consume the result and return through the declared basis re-entry relation |\\n\\nAn adjacent observation outside the evaluated claim does not replace the\\nclaim-relative result. The assessor returns it separately, with triage\\n`not_applicable` to that claim and the exact repricing or re-entry\\npressure; the decision owner returns it to its declared owner without\\ncreating a claim-relative block, or another review round, from its\\nseverity alone (P6, P2).\\n\\nThe assessor returns to the decision owner, not to the constructor. It does\\nnot edit the candidate, direct the repair or authorise continuation (P6,\\n§3).\\n\\nPurpose and material relation of this projection's generality: the\\npredecessor stated it for the Reviewer and the Executive only. Stating it\\nfor any assessor and decision owner gives every configuration the same\\nseparation of severity, priority, boundary effect and disposition, and\\nEXECUTIVE_BASELINE keeps the Reviewer and Executive instance (P6).\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[242,309]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"14f8816b1eb9cd146dd58a29bac35ea47a62e4e4b093b20f9892330e44922991\",\"selected_sha256\":\"b19acbc01df2a64aeb91c274750a47ba212e1024790c4c5d380e066dde3d4219\",\"size_bytes\":4801,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"EVALUATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[242,309]},\"sha256\":\"14f8816b1eb9cd146dd58a29bac35ea47a62e4e4b093b20f9892330e44922991\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:d77b6f60a2e633c2b0033f796366375e31407a632cf172a951c85bb58187522b","sha256":"d77b6f60a2e633c2b0033f796366375e31407a632cf172a951c85bb58187522b"},"id":"p2-read-eval-242","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=cac43b43206209571f2888a45df3108b11b08e6aa50dfd2a8b6bd014198e1459]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"## 4. Review results\n\nA review returns one core result\n([FOUNDATIONS §4, Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results)) for each declared\npredicate it evaluated, with: the exact subject and basis, the evidence\nconsulted, the findings ranked by consequence, each finding's evidence and\nthe smallest bounded correction, the residual uncertainty, and the\ninvalidation conditions. A declared predicate the review planned and did\nnot evaluate has no result (FOUNDATIONS §4, Results). The review names it\nas not performed and reports no core value for it, neither\n`indeterminate` nor `falsified`, so that conjunction keeps it apart from\nan undecided predicate and from required coverage that no planned\nassessment addresses\n([FOUNDATIONS §4, Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results);\nP5, P6). It may recommend a disposition\n([ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#3-step-results-and-disposition)), which is\nevidence only and never a disposition; it does not apply one. A finding\nwithout evidence a consumer can chase is commentary.\n\n### Result and triage projection\n\nWhere a review returns findings with technical triage, the triage is the\nassessor's evidence-bound assessment of each finding against the exact\nevaluated claim and basis. Severity, the assessor's grade of consequence,\nis evaluation evidence. Priority, the effect on the current promotion\nboundary and the disposition are the decision owner's (ACTIVATION §1,\nRoles and delegation; when a finding can block is\n[§5, When a finding blocks promotion](#when-a-finding-blocks-promotion))\nand stay distinct values even where a\nProduct-defined policy maps one to another. A recommended disposition\nis evidence for the decision owner: it is not a disposition, a\npriority or a boundary effect, and it is never adopted mechanically (P6,\nRF-007). The fields of a triage are declared by the profile that adopts it, and\nthe scales it uses are bound by the adopting Product (P2, P6; provenance\n[reviewer result and triage projection](stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#reviewer-result-and-triage-projection)).\n\nThe projection of the finding-level triage payload is total over the core\nvalues of [FOUNDATIONS §4, Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results). A predicate\nnot performed has no result and so no triage payload; the payload class\n`indeterminate` never stands for it. The payload classes `complete`,\n`indeterminate` and `not_applicable` classify the triage only; they are\nnot new results, dispositions, priorities or lifecycle states (P5, P1).\n\n| Core result | Finding and triage payload | Decision-owner consumption constraint |\n|---|---|---|\n| satisfied | an explicit no-finding state; triage `not_applicable`; evidence, residuals and invalidation stay present | priority and boundary effect are `not_applicable` to this result unless another exact consumed result supplies a finding |\n| falsified | one or more exact findings; triage `complete` where supported, keeping `indeterminate` fields where evidence cannot close them | apply the Product-owned priority and boundary policy without mapping severity mechanically to a disposition |\n| indeterminate | a partial finding or observation state; triage `indeterminate`; the exact evidence gaps and residual uncertainty | keep the uncertainty or reactivate a capable evaluation; do not consume it as satisfaction or as a closed finding |\n| out_of_frame | the evaluated claim needs an undeclared material relation or evaluator capability; triage `indeterminate`; the missing relation or capability and the exact reconfiguration pressure are named | refine or reconfigure a capable activation and keep the claim unresolved; do not consume the result as satisfaction or falsification |\n| invalid_basis | a basis failure; triage `not_applicable`; invalidation evidence and basis-repair pressure | refuse to consume the result and return through the declared basis re-entry relation |\n\nAn adjacent observation outside the evaluated claim does not replace the\nclaim-relative result. The assessor returns it separately, with triage\n`not_applicable` to that claim and the exact repricing or re-entry\npressure; the decision owner returns it to its declared owner without\ncreating a claim-relative block, or another review round, from its\nseverity alone (P6, P2).\n\nThe assessor returns to the decision owner, not to the constructor. It does\nnot edit the candidate, direct the repair or authorise continuation (P6,\n§3).\n\nPurpose and material relation of this projection's generality: the\npredecessor stated it for the Reviewer and the Executive only. Stating it\nfor any assessor and decision owner gives every configuration the same\nseparation of severity, priority, boundary effect and disposition, and\nEXECUTIVE_BASELINE keeps the Reviewer and Executive instance (P6).\n\n","coordinates":{"lines":[242,309]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"14f8816b1eb9cd146dd58a29bac35ea47a62e4e4b093b20f9892330e44922991","selected_sha256":"b19acbc01df2a64aeb91c274750a47ba212e1024790c4c5d380e066dde3d4219","size_bytes":4801,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"EVALUATION.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[242,309]},"sha256":"14f8816b1eb9cd146dd58a29bac35ea47a62e4e4b093b20f9892330e44922991"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01E5tQYvawMmRRaZiMU1rFg4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
