ssary-condition pass cannot satisfy a stronger predicate; unsupported operations refuse. | FD-001,004,008,010; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-012 Existing state and authorized records | Project the named work/evidence carrier and apply one already-authorized actor/owner record through its Writer interface with preimage/grant checks. Preserve original ruling versus interpretation; a recommendation/commit/review event supplies no automatic disposition/closure/release, and generated views do not own work state. | FD-011; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-013 Refresh and fresh-actor handoff | Edit material source/frame inputs and compute affected support under supplied impact/reuse rules. Preserve originals/frozen studies and demonstrably valid survivors; incomplete dependencies leave uncertainty. A fresh actor resumes from current named sources without replay or blind retry of unreconciled effects. | FD-002,004,012; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-014 Notifications and resource evidence | Deliver return/exception/basis-change/checkpoint events and test declared bounded fallback when notifications fail. Retain failed/partial/retried attempts, units, unknown backend usage, elapsed versus summed intervals and selected limit checks without double counting or universal quotas. | FD-007,013; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-015 Matched usefulness | Compare matched tasks with/without support and retain bounded source/semantic/accepted-outcome and total cost evidence, including acquisition/authoring/refresh/repair/review and unknowns. Report actual results without extrapolating savings from fewer calls. | FD-013; FDV-003 |\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[51,84]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf\",\"selected_sha256\":\"798aa73dbc103f3928ef0f110e7af1eb693a107c262b93b06dff1e39ef9c2381\",\"size_bytes\":6458,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/requirements/fd-support-verification.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[51,84]},\"sha256\":\"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:3706145b82b5f801c7c6c9bbe1c263b9fcf977e03758146175b348dcffe937c1","sha256":"3706145b82b5f801c7c6c9bbe1c263b9fcf977e03758146175b348dcffe937c1"},"id":"p2-read-fdv-002","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=f8f9bbf9b4c095fea9adf2c6ac3c356e3cd85ca60cb138f0d576c8f06eec1007]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"context preparation, refresh, invocation, failed attempts/retries, repair,\nreview and decision effort, with measurement boundaries and unknowns. Report\nobserved differences and limitations rather than inferring a general benefit\nfrom count, graph size, fit or structural success. Owners:\n[ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §6;\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §1;\n[FOUND](fd-source-owner-map.md#found) Assertions and observation/Change impact\nand evidence reuse.\n\n## Scenario and requirement trace\n\nThe following is written test-case authority, not executed evidence. FD-nnn\nexpands to `REQ-AC-FD-nnn`; FDV-nnn expands to `REQ-AC-FDV-nnn`. Each case supplies\nthe exact applicable upstream contract; the table does not redefine its states,\nrole duties, result values, applicability or admission policy.\n\n| Scenario | Supplied input/variation and required observable tool response | Trace |\n|---|---|---|\n| SC-AC-FD-001 Real actor use | One actual bounded task uses ordinary documented operations for Executive preparation/dispatch, Worker source/proof acquisition and Reviewer independent candidate/source/proof access, then captures supplied actor/owner results through the selected carrier. All effective inputs and effect evidence are traceable; no tool-generated semantic/owner verdict appears. | FD-001..013; FDV-001 |\n| SC-AC-FD-002 Contract discovery/bases | Exact supported request returns its contract/checked fragment. Unknown operation, unsupported method/profile and ambiguous Product selection refuse with reasons. Tool builder, consumer method and represented v3 subject stay distinct; equal model labels do not create a join. | FD-001,002,004; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-003 Dirty current state | Relevant dirty/untracked bytes or dependency/configuration change after observation without changing HEAD. A dependent preflight detects the changed supplied precondition; a branch/commit match cannot hide it or silently rebase the request. | FD-002,006,007; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-004 Grounding and incomplete coverage | Give exact source/record references plus a missing mapping, inferred code edge and methodology-only model. Return actual payload/content or a named gap and coverage boundaries. No inferred governing relation, complete-workspace claim or unaffectedness conclusion follows. | FD-003,004; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-005 Supplied conditional predicates | Evaluate a declared supported applicability predicate on true, false and missing-premise inputs, plus missing/wrong-subject prerequisite evidence. Preserve the method's exact distinction and F_P judgments separately; no semantic frontier/re-entry choice is made by the query. | FD-004,008,010; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-006 Context and envelope | Supply locator-only versus acquired records/source, governing closure with qualifications/residuals, exact permitted late reads, denied acquisition, exceeded capacity and unknown host context. Assemble/check the selected packet, measure only the declared boundary and preserve gaps/owner refusals without silent trimming or sufficiency claims. | FD-003,005; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-007 Admission and grants | Candidate packet/ticket/role without the selected admission evidence or granted effect refuses dispatch. Exact Product-bound mechanism/allowed override and supplied grant permit only the named tools/territory. Unauthorized recording/Executive or Reviewer mutation refuses under the selected role contract. | FD-006,007,011; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-008 Transport and uncertain effect | Distinguish receipt, schema-valid output, F_P return, observed effect and observed end. Lost response/timeout/cancel/interruption with partial write preserves upstream unknown-effect evidence and material retry preconditions. A termination request never proves completion/rollback. | FD-007,008,012,013; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-009 Closed return binding | Capture exact valid, stale, wrong-subject/basis, duplicate and conflicting returns. Preserve raw original predicates/domain outcomes; report consumer-binding errors and gaps without rewriting old verdicts, counting duplicate independence or fabricating unperformed results. | FD-008,010; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-010 Independent review acquisition | Under supplied exposure/independence conditions, record source-derived expectations before candidate exposure and permit a nonauthor Reviewer to acquire exact candidate, tests/fixtures, governing source and comparisons directly. Author summary/new session is not certified independent. The tool returns acquisition/diff facts, never review severity or disposition. | FD-003,005,009; FDV-001,002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-011 Declared checks/conjunction | Execute a qualified supplied structural/proof predicate and method-owned operator. Preserve wrong-basis inputs, missing planned assessments, uncovered obligations, original domain outcomes and conflicts exactly. A necessary-condition pass cannot satisfy a stronger predicate; unsupported operations refuse. | FD-001,004,008,010; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-012 Existing state and authorized records | Project the named work/evidence carrier and apply one already-authorized actor/owner record through its Writer interface with preimage/grant checks. Preserve original ruling versus interpretation; a recommendation/commit/review event supplies no automatic disposition/closure/release, and generated views do not own work state. | FD-011; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-013 Refresh and fresh-actor handoff | Edit material source/frame inputs and compute affected support under supplied impact/reuse rules. Preserve originals/frozen studies and demonstrably valid survivors; incomplete dependencies leave uncertainty. A fresh actor resumes from current named sources without replay or blind retry of unreconciled effects. | FD-002,004,012; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-014 Notifications and resource evidence | Deliver return/exception/basis-change/checkpoint events and test declared bounded fallback when notifications fail. Retain failed/partial/retried attempts, units, unknown backend usage, elapsed versus summed intervals and selected limit checks without double counting or universal quotas. | FD-007,013; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-015 Matched usefulness | Compare matched tasks with/without support and retain bounded source/semantic/accepted-outcome and total cost evidence, including acquisition/authoring/refresh/repair/review and unknowns. Report actual results without extrapolating savings from fewer calls. | FD-013; FDV-003 |\n\n","coordinates":{"lines":[51,84]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf","selected_sha256":"798aa73dbc103f3928ef0f110e7af1eb693a107c262b93b06dff1e39ef9c2381","size_bytes":6458,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"specification/requirements/fd-support-verification.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[51,84]},"sha256":"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013Fhm9X1iBf3vLL6MRUEUWr","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAzEqmXofX2yF1rvVriH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P5guA5cHsgCSWwqBHE4uoD","name":"mcp__ac_review__source_read","input":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-assure-680","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"ASSURANCE.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[680,756]},"sha256":"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5091,"cache_read_input_tokens":179817,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5091},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"33f78ed3-876c-48ea-a2dc-cc1c25779699","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:46:01.410Z","request_id":"req_011CgAzEqUR1urJPvnVhVK2v","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01P5guA5cHsgCSWwqBHE4uoD":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-assure-680","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"ASSURANCE.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[680,756]},"sha256":"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P5guA5cHsgCSWwqBHE4uoD","display_name":"Source Read","server_display_name":"a_c.graphify.fd-support","tool_name":"source.read"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P5guA5cHsgCSWwqBHE4uoD","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:b251cbc0716e13eb1eeb06b5144a42afe19c959ac7bc95784a92f5821ab46762\",\"sha256\":\"b251cbc0716e13eb1eeb06b5144a42afe19c959ac7bc95784a92f5821ab46762\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-assure-680\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=d177ed601c6094d3e88a4d56ac50764e6d9d15caea5be0653d27ca66aeb94f1f]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"## 11. Assurance subject acquisition and evaluation\\n\\nAcquiring the assurance subject and evaluating it are distinct relations\\n(P6, P1; provenance #assurance-subject-acquisition-and-evaluation). Where a\\nclaim depends on owner-issued Product, runtime, lifecycle, admission,\\nreplay or projection truth, the testing frame acquires that truth through\\nthe exact runnable owner surface, validator, projection, receipt or\\nreconstruction relation. A harness, fixture, expected-value builder, proof\\nscript, assurance evaluator or assessor does not reconstruct a parallel\\nowner state from raw payloads, events, logs, filenames, labels or\\nimplementation fragments and then evaluate that self-authored state as if\\nit were the Product subject. Where the acquired observation cannot\\nseparate two admissible subjects on which the assessed predicate takes\\nopposite truth values, the frame returns further evidence, a justified\\nnarrower scope or `indeterminate`. The binding of the\\nobservation itself needs support\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Assertions and observation](FOUNDATIONS.md#assertions-and-observation),\\nObservation sufficiency) (P1, P6).\\n\\nAfter lawful acquisition, an independently derived oracle may evaluate the\\ngoverning claim. Generic assurance mechanics may compute bytes, digests,\\nordering, equality, set membership, completeness and conjunction over\\nowner-issued evidence. Those mechanics stay evidence evaluators: they\\ncannot mint owner carriers, choose the current history, select the\\nauthoritative path, interpret domain lifecycle or admission meaning, or\\nbecome a runtime fallback (P6; EVALUATION §2).\\n\\nThe rule does not require an evaluator to trust the implementation under\\ntest as its semantic oracle; the oracle derives from Product, requirement\\nand accepted-design law. It requires the assurance subject to be the actual\\nowner-issued subject rather than a second implementation of the owner's\\nruntime meaning. If the required owner projection or observable seam is\\nabsent, the result keeps a named assurance or design gap; the proof harness\\ndoes not fill it with rival semantics (P6, P5).\\n\\n## 12. Counterexample localisation\\n\\nA testing counterexample is returned to its earliest supported causal\\nfrontier on the declared path. The frontier holds the causally minimal\\nviolated owner relations or seam coordinates the evidence establishes;\\nearliest means minimal under the declared causal relation, not first in log\\nor clock order (P5, P6; provenance #counterexample-localization).\\n\\nThe localisation result represents exactly one of (P5, P1):\\n\\n- one unique violated locus;\\n- a jointly established set of incomparable earliest violated loci whose\\n  combined violation is necessary to the supported causal explanation;\\n- unresolved alternative frontiers, when the evidence supports several\\n  possible causal explanations but cannot establish which occurred; or\\n- `indeterminate`, when the evidence cannot support a bounded frontier.\\n\\nThe four forms are a refinement of the core under the rule of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), for the predicate \\\"the\\nevidence establishes the counterexample's earliest violated loci on the\\ndeclared path\\\". One unique violated locus and a jointly established set\\nmap to `satisfied`. Unresolved alternative frontiers map to\\n`indeterminate`, naming the alternatives that further evidence must\\ndecide between. The fourth form is the core value `indeterminate` itself,\\nnaming the evidence a bounded frontier needs. The form travels with the\\nvalue as the domain outcome, so a joint set stays distinct from a unique\\nlocus and unresolved alternatives stay distinct from an unbounded\\nfrontier. Purpose and material relation: a localisation combines with\\nother results in the one core, and an unresolved causal explanation is\\nnever read as an established one (P5, P1, P6).\\n\\nLocalisation records the subject, basis, frontier form and members, causal\\nevidence, expected relations, the observed counterexample and the\\ndownstream claims it invalidates. It does not collapse a jointly\\nestablished set into one arbitrary owner, and it does not report\\nunresolved alternatives as a joint cause (P5, P4b).\\n\\nA localised frontier does not itself authorise broader test expansion,\\ncompatibility repair, another controller or a reinterpretation of unchanged\\nupstream meaning. A resulting scope or design change follows the existing\\nre-entry relation (SPEC_METHOD §4; P6).\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[680,756]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf\",\"selected_sha256\":\"25be90aa160d0bef429091772d88e3f099c9acee5cf177c9356af01758b1aa6d\",\"size_bytes\":4400,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"ASSURANCE.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[680,756]},\"sha256\":\"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"4c0402dc-38b3-464b-b2fd-54f7c6869c2c","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:46:01.882Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:b251cbc0716e13eb1eeb06b5144a42afe19c959ac7bc95784a92f5821ab46762\",\"sha256\":\"b251cbc0716e13eb1eeb06b5144a42afe19c959ac7bc95784a92f5821ab46762\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-assure-680\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=d177ed601c6094d3e88a4d56ac50764e6d9d15caea5be0653d27ca66aeb94f1f]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"## 11. Assurance subject acquisition and evaluation\\n\\nAcquiring the assurance subject and evaluating it are distinct relations\\n(P6, P1; provenance #assurance-subject-acquisition-and-evaluation). Where a\\nclaim depends on owner-issued Product, runtime, lifecycle, admission,\\nreplay or projection truth, the testing frame acquires that truth through\\nthe exact runnable owner surface, validator, projection, receipt or\\nreconstruction relation. A harness, fixture, expected-value builder, proof\\nscript, assurance evaluator or assessor does not reconstruct a parallel\\nowner state from raw payloads, events, logs, filenames, labels or\\nimplementation fragments and then evaluate that self-authored state as if\\nit were the Product subject. Where the acquired observation cannot\\nseparate two admissible subjects on which the assessed predicate takes\\nopposite truth values, the frame returns further evidence, a justified\\nnarrower scope or `indeterminate`. The binding of the\\nobservation itself needs support\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Assertions and observation](FOUNDATIONS.md#assertions-and-observation),\\nObservation sufficiency) (P1, P6).\\n\\nAfter lawful acquisition, an independently derived oracle may evaluate the\\ngoverning claim. Generic assurance mechanics may compute bytes, digests,\\nordering, equality, set membership, completeness and conjunction over\\nowner-issued evidence. Those mechanics stay evidence evaluators: they\\ncannot mint owner carriers, choose the current history, select the\\nauthoritative path, interpret domain lifecycle or admission meaning, or\\nbecome a runtime fallback (P6; EVALUATION §2).\\n\\nThe rule does not require an evaluator to trust the implementation under\\ntest as its semantic oracle; the oracle derives from Product, requirement\\nand accepted-design law. It requires the assurance subject to be the actual\\nowner-issued subject rather than a second implementation of the owner's\\nruntime meaning. If the required owner projection or observable seam is\\nabsent, the result keeps a named assurance or design gap; the proof harness\\ndoes not fill it with rival semantics (P6, P5).\\n\\n## 12. Counterexample localisation\\n\\nA testing counterexample is returned to its earliest supported causal\\nfrontier on the declared path. The frontier holds the causally minimal\\nviolated owner relations or seam coordinates the evidence establishes;\\nearliest means minimal under the declared causal relation, not first in log\\nor clock order (P5, P6; provenance #counterexample-localization).\\n\\nThe localisation result represents exactly one of (P5, P1):\\n\\n- one unique violated locus;\\n- a jointly established set of incomparable earliest violated loci whose\\n  combined violation is necessary to the supported causal explanation;\\n- unresolved alternative frontiers, when the evidence supports several\\n  possible causal explanations but cannot establish which occurred; or\\n- `indeterminate`, when the evidence cannot support a bounded frontier.\\n\\nThe four forms are a refinement of the core under the rule of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), for the predicate \\\"the\\nevidence establishes the counterexample's earliest violated loci on the\\ndeclared path\\\". One unique violated locus and a jointly established set\\nmap to `satisfied`. Unresolved alternative frontiers map to\\n`indeterminate`, naming the alternatives that further evidence must\\ndecide between. The fourth form is the core value `indeterminate` itself,\\nnaming the evidence a bounded frontier needs. The form travels with the\\nvalue as the domain outcome, so a joint set stays distinct from a unique\\nlocus and unresolved alternatives stay distinct from an unbounded\\nfrontier. Purpose and material relation: a localisation combines with\\nother results in the one core, and an unresolved causal explanation is\\nnever read as an established one (P5, P1, P6).\\n\\nLocalisation records the subject, basis, frontier form and members, causal\\nevidence, expected relations, the observed counterexample and the\\ndownstream claims it invalidates. It does not collapse a jointly\\nestablished set into one arbitrary owner, and it does not report\\nunresolved alternatives as a joint cause (P5, P4b).\\n\\nA localised frontier does not itself authorise broader test expansion,\\ncompatibility repair, another controller or a reinterpretation of unchanged\\nupstream meaning. A resulting scope or design change follows the existing\\nre-entry relation (SPEC_METHOD §4; P6).\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[680,756]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf\",\"selected_sha256\":\"25be90aa160d0bef429091772d88e3f099c9acee5cf177c9356af01758b1aa6d\",\"size_bytes\":4400,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"ASSURANCE.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[680,756]},\"sha256\":\"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:b251cbc0716e13eb1eeb06b5144a42afe19c959ac7bc95784a92f5821ab46762","sha256":"b251cbc0716e13eb1eeb06b5144a42afe19c959ac7bc95784a92f5821ab46762"},"id":"p2-read-assure-680","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=d177ed601c6094d3e88a4d56ac50764e6d9d15caea5be0653d27ca66aeb94f1f]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"## 11. Assurance subject acquisition and evaluation\n\nAcquiring the assurance subject and evaluating it are distinct relations\n(P6, P1; provenance #assurance-subject-acquisition-and-evaluation). Where a\nclaim depends on owner-issued Product, runtime, lifecycle, admission,\nreplay or projection truth, the testing frame acquires that truth through\nthe exact runnable owner surface, validator, projection, receipt or\nreconstruction relation. A harness, fixture, expected-value builder, proof\nscript, assurance evaluator or assessor does not reconstruct a parallel\nowner state from raw payloads, events, logs, filenames, labels or\nimplementation fragments and then evaluate that self-authored state as if\nit were the Product subject. Where the acquired observation cannot\nseparate two admissible subjects on which the assessed predicate takes\nopposite truth values, the frame returns further evidence, a justified\nnarrower scope or `indeterminate`. The binding of the\nobservation itself needs support\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Assertions and observation](FOUNDATIONS.md#assertions-and-observation),\nObservation sufficiency) (P1, P6).\n\nAfter lawful acquisition, an independently derived oracle may evaluate the\ngoverning claim. Generic assurance mechanics may compute bytes, digests,\nordering, equality, set membership, completeness and conjunction over\nowner-issued evidence. Those mechanics stay evidence evaluators: they\ncannot mint owner carriers, choose the current history, select the\nauthoritative path, interpret domain lifecycle or admission meaning, or\nbecome a runtime fallback (P6; EVALUATION §2).\n\nThe rule does not require an evaluator to trust the implementation under\ntest as its semantic oracle; the oracle derives from Product, requirement\nand accepted-design law. It requires the assurance subject to be the actual\nowner-issued subject rather than a second implementation of the owner's\nruntime meaning. If the required owner projection or observable seam is\nabsent, the result keeps a named assurance or design gap; the proof harness\ndoes not fill it with rival semantics (P6, P5).\n\n## 12. Counterexample localisation\n\nA testing counterexample is returned to its earliest supported causal\nfrontier on the declared path. The frontier holds the causally minimal\nviolated owner relations or seam coordinates the evidence establishes;\nearliest means minimal under the declared causal relation, not first in log\nor clock order (P5, P6; provenance #counterexample-localization).\n\nThe localisation result represents exactly one of (P5, P1):\n\n- one unique violated locus;\n- a jointly established set of incomparable earliest violated loci whose\n  combined violation is necessary to the supported causal explanation;\n- unresolved alternative frontiers, when the evidence supports several\n  possible causal explanations but cannot establish which occurred; or\n- `indeterminate`, when the evidence cannot support a bounded frontier.\n\nThe four forms are a refinement of the core under the rule of\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), for the predicate \"the\nevidence establishes the counterexample's earliest violated loci on the\ndeclared path\". One unique violated locus and a jointly established set\nmap to `satisfied`. Unresolved alternative frontiers map to\n`indeterminate`, naming the alternatives that further evidence must\ndecide between. The fourth form is the core value `indeterminate` itself,\nnaming the evidence a bounded frontier needs. The form travels with the\nvalue as the domain outcome, so a joint set stays distinct from a unique\nlocus and unresolved alternatives stay distinct from an unbounded\nfrontier. Purpose and material relation: a localisation combines with\nother results in the one core, and an unresolved causal explanation is\nnever read as an established one (P5, P1, P6).\n\nLocalisation records the subject, basis, frontier form and members, causal\nevidence, expected relations, the observed counterexample and the\ndownstream claims it invalidates. It does not collapse a jointly\nestablished set into one arbitrary owner, and it does not report\nunresolved alternatives as a joint cause (P5, P4b).\n\nA localised frontier does not itself authorise broader test expansion,\ncompatibility repair, another controller or a reinterpretation of unchanged\nupstream meaning. A resulting scope or design change follows the existing\nre-entry relation (SPEC_METHOD §4; P6).\n\n","coordinates":{"lines":[680,756]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf","selected_sha256":"25be90aa160d0bef429091772d88e3f099c9acee5cf177c9356af01758b1aa6d","size_bytes":4400,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"ASSURANCE.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[680,756]},"sha256":"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P5guA5cHsgCSWwqBHE4uoD","p