{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jy3y9KVxPyR4AK2AQ2wiz3","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:1b3438d11175ea8b28cb5cbc7188d1b3efc48e9395dacec40de74f6632f34388\",\"sha256\":\"1b3438d11175ea8b28cb5cbc7188d1b3efc48e9395dacec40de74f6632f34388\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-rf-281\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=863c1d183cde85ba7cf61604c93343f8e119bae648d4d0b68129616fab517b65]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### RF-001 Evaluation relativity\\n\\nEvery frame declares the evaluation family it supports. A frame with no\\ndeclared evaluation family has no testable sufficiency boundary (P2; rc.2\\n#rf-001-evaluation-relativity).\\n\\n### RF-002 Finite attention\\n\\nAn activated frame contains a finite attention surface that fits the\\nselected actor's declared capability envelope. A frame that needs\\nundeclared ambient memory, conversation history or an effectively global\\nworkspace context is not reconstructable for that actor (P0; rc.2\\n#rf-002-finite-attention). The fit is tested in\\n[ACTIVATION §2](ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope),\\nwhich owns the measurement of the context's size and when it applies.\\nWhether the actor attends adequately to a frame that fits is a separate\\nquestion, answered by actual-use evidence under\\n[EVALUATION §7](EVALUATION.md#frame-qualification); a size measurement\\ndoes not answer it (P0, P6).\\n\\n### RF-003 Material sufficiency\\n\\nEvery known relation whose lawful change can alter the evaluation result,\\nthe validity of the basis, the sufficiency of evidence, operation authority\\nor decision authority appears in the frame or enters through a declared\\nauthoritative input. Omitting a material relation makes the frame\\ninsufficient. The law does not require proving that no undiscovered\\nmaterial relation exists (P2; P0 with the open-world premise; rc.2\\n#rf-003-material-sufficiency).\\n\\n### RF-004 Irrelevance exclusion\\n\\nRelations that cannot affect the declared evaluation stay outside active\\nattention unless they are needed to establish that irrelevance. A frame\\ndoes not expand because adjacent workspace material exists (P2; rc.2\\n#rf-004-irrelevance-exclusion).\\n\\n### RF-005 Exact basis and coordinates\\n\\nEvery result binds its exact subject, basis, coordinates and evidence\\nscope. A stale, advanced, ambiguous or mismatched basis returns\\n`invalid_basis` or requires reactivation. Apparent equality never\\nsubstitutes for declared coordinate equality (P3, P1; rc.2\\n#rf-005-exact-basis-and-coordinates).\\n\\n### RF-006 Authority conservation\\n\\nA frame carries and applies admitted authority. It does not mint, widen,\\ntransfer or reconstruct semantic, evaluation, operation or decision\\nauthority from anything that creates none. That list is\\n[FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds)'; its\\ninstances in a frame include actor identity, available capability,\\nevidence shape, implementation reachability and frame selection (P6;\\nrc.2 #rf-006-authority-conservation).\\n\\n### RF-007 Semantic, evidence and verdict separation\\n\\nThe separation of semantic law, evidence, the evaluator's application\\nand the disposing decision authority is\\n[EVALUATION §2](EVALUATION.md#2-separation)'s. This law binds it to a\\nframe: a frame declaration keeps these roles distinguishable even when\\none actor lawfully performs several of them, and where the evaluation\\nperforms a material operation, the existing operation owner supplies the\\nexact grant as a further role the declaration keeps apart (P6; rc.2\\n#rf-007-semantic-evidence-and-verdict-separation).\\n\\n### RF-008 Overlap without identity collapse\\n\\nFrames may share entities, variables, evidence or coordinates. Shared\\nmaterial establishes neither identical meaning nor identical basis,\\nauthority or result. Every cross-frame equality or translation an\\nevaluation uses is declared where it is used (P1, P3; rc.2\\n#rf-008-overlap-without-identity-collapse).\\n\\n### RF-009 No assumed hierarchy\\n\\nFrames may relate through disjointness, overlap, refinement, restriction,\\ntranslation, temporal succession, composition or governance (§7). Parent\\nand child relations apply only where explicitly declared. Functional\\ndecomposition, communication, authority precedence, frame configuration,\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[281,360]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"d64ee5c05aaefac346116c2e43eabf193dd84123f1d461070ecd378ce5e9b551\",\"selected_sha256\":\"ebe1a2dccb1fd3e129dad142730dd0de456a36099808d194dd65a8e6c6dee3f4\",\"size_bytes\":3762,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[281,360]},\"sha256\":\"d64ee5c05aaefac346116c2e43eabf193dd84123f1d461070ecd378ce5e9b551\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"fe31bf2d-8a54-4266-b9d6-35f5af0a7969","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:46:08.410Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:1b3438d11175ea8b28cb5cbc7188d1b3efc48e9395dacec40de74f6632f34388\",\"sha256\":\"1b3438d11175ea8b28cb5cbc7188d1b3efc48e9395dacec40de74f6632f34388\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-rf-281\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=863c1d183cde85ba7cf61604c93343f8e119bae648d4d0b68129616fab517b65]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### RF-001 Evaluation relativity\\n\\nEvery frame declares the evaluation family it supports. A frame with no\\ndeclared evaluation family has no testable sufficiency boundary (P2; rc.2\\n#rf-001-evaluation-relativity).\\n\\n### RF-002 Finite attention\\n\\nAn activated frame contains a finite attention surface that fits the\\nselected actor's declared capability envelope. A frame that needs\\nundeclared ambient memory, conversation history or an effectively global\\nworkspace context is not reconstructable for that actor (P0; rc.2\\n#rf-002-finite-attention). The fit is tested in\\n[ACTIVATION §2](ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope),\\nwhich owns the measurement of the context's size and when it applies.\\nWhether the actor attends adequately to a frame that fits is a separate\\nquestion, answered by actual-use evidence under\\n[EVALUATION §7](EVALUATION.md#frame-qualification); a size measurement\\ndoes not answer it (P0, P6).\\n\\n### RF-003 Material sufficiency\\n\\nEvery known relation whose lawful change can alter the evaluation result,\\nthe validity of the basis, the sufficiency of evidence, operation authority\\nor decision authority appears in the frame or enters through a declared\\nauthoritative input. Omitting a material relation makes the frame\\ninsufficient. The law does not require proving that no undiscovered\\nmaterial relation exists (P2; P0 with the open-world premise; rc.2\\n#rf-003-material-sufficiency).\\n\\n### RF-004 Irrelevance exclusion\\n\\nRelations that cannot affect the declared evaluation stay outside active\\nattention unless they are needed to establish that irrelevance. A frame\\ndoes not expand because adjacent workspace material exists (P2; rc.2\\n#rf-004-irrelevance-exclusion).\\n\\n### RF-005 Exact basis and coordinates\\n\\nEvery result binds its exact subject, basis, coordinates and evidence\\nscope. A stale, advanced, ambiguous or mismatched basis returns\\n`invalid_basis` or requires reactivation. Apparent equality never\\nsubstitutes for declared coordinate equality (P3, P1; rc.2\\n#rf-005-exact-basis-and-coordinates).\\n\\n### RF-006 Authority conservation\\n\\nA frame carries and applies admitted authority. It does not mint, widen,\\ntransfer or reconstruct semantic, evaluation, operation or decision\\nauthority from anything that creates none. That list is\\n[FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds)'; its\\ninstances in a frame include actor identity, available capability,\\nevidence shape, implementation reachability and frame selection (P6;\\nrc.2 #rf-006-authority-conservation).\\n\\n### RF-007 Semantic, evidence and verdict separation\\n\\nThe separation of semantic law, evidence, the evaluator's application\\nand the disposing decision authority is\\n[EVALUATION §2](EVALUATION.md#2-separation)'s. This law binds it to a\\nframe: a frame declaration keeps these roles distinguishable even when\\none actor lawfully performs several of them, and where the evaluation\\nperforms a material operation, the existing operation owner supplies the\\nexact grant as a further role the declaration keeps apart (P6; rc.2\\n#rf-007-semantic-evidence-and-verdict-separation).\\n\\n### RF-008 Overlap without identity collapse\\n\\nFrames may share entities, variables, evidence or coordinates. Shared\\nmaterial establishes neither identical meaning nor identical basis,\\nauthority or result. Every cross-frame equality or translation an\\nevaluation uses is declared where it is used (P1, P3; rc.2\\n#rf-008-overlap-without-identity-collapse).\\n\\n### RF-009 No assumed hierarchy\\n\\nFrames may relate through disjointness, overlap, refinement, restriction,\\ntranslation, temporal succession, composition or governance (§7). Parent\\nand child relations apply only where explicitly declared. Functional\\ndecomposition, communication, authority precedence, frame configuration,\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[281,360]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"d64ee5c05aaefac346116c2e43eabf193dd84123f1d461070ecd378ce5e9b551\",\"selected_sha256\":\"ebe1a2dccb1fd3e129dad142730dd0de456a36099808d194dd65a8e6c6dee3f4\",\"size_bytes\":3762,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[281,360]},\"sha256\":\"d64ee5c05aaefac346116c2e43eabf193dd84123f1d461070ecd378ce5e9b551\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:1b3438d11175ea8b28cb5cbc7188d1b3efc48e9395dacec40de74f6632f34388","sha256":"1b3438d11175ea8b28cb5cbc7188d1b3efc48e9395dacec40de74f6632f34388"},"id":"p2-read-rf-281","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=863c1d183cde85ba7cf61604c93343f8e119bae648d4d0b68129616fab517b65]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"### RF-001 Evaluation relativity\n\nEvery frame declares the evaluation family it supports. A frame with no\ndeclared evaluation family has no testable sufficiency boundary (P2; rc.2\n#rf-001-evaluation-relativity).\n\n### RF-002 Finite attention\n\nAn activated frame contains a finite attention surface that fits the\nselected actor's declared capability envelope. A frame that needs\nundeclared ambient memory, conversation history or an effectively global\nworkspace context is not reconstructable for that actor (P0; rc.2\n#rf-002-finite-attention). The fit is tested in\n[ACTIVATION §2](ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope),\nwhich owns the measurement of the context's size and when it applies.\nWhether the actor attends adequately to a frame that fits is a separate\nquestion, answered by actual-use evidence under\n[EVALUATION §7](EVALUATION.md#frame-qualification); a size measurement\ndoes not answer it (P0, P6).\n\n### RF-003 Material sufficiency\n\nEvery known relation whose lawful change can alter the evaluation result,\nthe validity of the basis, the sufficiency of evidence, operation authority\nor decision authority appears in the frame or enters through a declared\nauthoritative input. Omitting a material relation makes the frame\ninsufficient. The law does not require proving that no undiscovered\nmaterial relation exists (P2; P0 with the open-world premise; rc.2\n#rf-003-material-sufficiency).\n\n### RF-004 Irrelevance exclusion\n\nRelations that cannot affect the declared evaluation stay outside active\nattention unless they are needed to establish that irrelevance. A frame\ndoes not expand because adjacent workspace material exists (P2; rc.2\n#rf-004-irrelevance-exclusion).\n\n### RF-005 Exact basis and coordinates\n\nEvery result binds its exact subject, basis, coordinates and evidence\nscope. A stale, advanced, ambiguous or mismatched basis returns\n`invalid_basis` or requires reactivation. Apparent equality never\nsubstitutes for declared coordinate equality (P3, P1; rc.2\n#rf-005-exact-basis-and-coordinates).\n\n### RF-006 Authority conservation\n\nA frame carries and applies admitted authority. It does not mint, widen,\ntransfer or reconstruct semantic, evaluation, operation or decision\nauthority from anything that creates none. That list is\n[FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds)'; its\ninstances in a frame include actor identity, available capability,\nevidence shape, implementation reachability and frame selection (P6;\nrc.2 #rf-006-authority-conservation).\n\n### RF-007 Semantic, evidence and verdict separation\n\nThe separation of semantic law, evidence, the evaluator's application\nand the disposing decision authority is\n[EVALUATION §2](EVALUATION.md#2-separation)'s. This law binds it to a\nframe: a frame declaration keeps these roles distinguishable even when\none actor lawfully performs several of them, and where the evaluation\nperforms a material operation, the existing operation owner supplies the\nexact grant as a further role the declaration keeps apart (P6; rc.2\n#rf-007-semantic-evidence-and-verdict-separation).\n\n### RF-008 Overlap without identity collapse\n\nFrames may share entities, variables, evidence or coordinates. Shared\nmaterial establishes neither identical meaning nor identical basis,\nauthority or result. Every cross-frame equality or translation an\nevaluation uses is declared where it is used (P1, P3; rc.2\n#rf-008-overlap-without-identity-collapse).\n\n### RF-009 No assumed hierarchy\n\nFrames may relate through disjointness, overlap, refinement, restriction,\ntranslation, temporal succession, composition or governance (§7). Parent\nand child relations apply only where explicitly declared. Functional\ndecomposition, communication, authority precedence, frame configuration,\n","coordinates":{"lines":[281,360]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"d64ee5c05aaefac346116c2e43eabf193dd84123f1d461070ecd378ce5e9b551","selected_sha256":"ebe1a2dccb1fd3e129dad142730dd0de456a36099808d194dd65a8e6c6dee3f4","size_bytes":3762,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"REFERENCE_FRAME.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[281,360]},"sha256":"d64ee5c05aaefac346116c2e43eabf193dd84123f1d461070ecd378ce5e9b551"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Jy3y9KVxPyR4AK2AQ2wiz3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
