{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Woqyjsv4DhyKYRC9HErGYU","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:beb1217f0bc49ece8938e3035334411e27497c58b4a4bce36b2db41a700c7d83\",\"sha256\":\"beb1217f0bc49ece8938e3035334411e27497c58b4a4bce36b2db41a700c7d83\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-rf-361\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=f00a56503f4aa031ceb832ba6e12e852d09fec266ea8173a657f0ce9586c9298]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"subject topology and evaluation dependency are distinct relation\\nstructures; a consumer may align them where the governed subject warrants\\nit and may not silently treat them as one hierarchy (P3, P1; rc.2\\n#rf-009-no-assumed-hierarchy). Communication is the exchange of\\ninformation between frames, or between the actors activated on them. An\\nexchange by itself grants no authority, an instance of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds), What\\ncreates no authority, and establishes neither a decomposition nor an\\nevaluation dependency (P6, P1). Communication is new\\nin this list. Purpose and material relation: a configuration assigns\\ninformation exchanges as well as responsibilities\\n([ACTIVATION §1](ACTIVATION.md#configuration)), and an exchange read as a\\ngrant or as a dependency would move authority or change a result without a\\ndeclared relation.\\n\\n### RF-010 Composition on demand\\n\\nUsing several frames does not require composing their internal manifolds.\\nComposition law is required only when the governing evaluation combines\\ntheir internal variables, transports evidence or values across them, or\\ntreats their operations as one material execution relation. Independently\\nactivated evaluations may instead return closed results to one declared\\nconjunction or decision rule (P4a; §6; rc.2\\n#rf-010-composition-on-demand).\\n\\n### RF-011 Topology mutation and recharting\\n\\nAn activated frame declares the topology changes capable of invalidating\\nits coordinates or its materiality judgment. A detected material topology\\nmutation causes reevaluation, frame revision or recharting before the\\nprevious result is reused. Material revision of the frame itself\\ninvalidates for reuse every result bound to the prior revision coordinate;\\n§10 Revision actions states that rule (P3, P4b; rc.2\\n#rf-011-topology-mutation-and-recharting).\\n\\n### RF-012 Closed results\\n\\nEvery performed evaluation of a frame returns one closed result in the\\nframe's declared result algebra: the core algebra of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), or a refinement mapped\\ninto it under that section. That section owns the five core values\\n(`satisfied`, `falsified`, `indeterminate`, `out_of_frame` and\\n`invalid_basis`), their meanings and the rules over them: that nothing is\\ncoerced to success; that a refinement adds no core value, keeps\\nindeterminate, out-of-frame and invalid-basis pressure explicit and raises\\nno result's standing; and that an evaluation not performed has no result,\\nits stop state being\\n[ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#3-step-results-and-disposition). This law\\napplies them to every frame and defines none of them (P5; rc.2\\n#rf-012-closed-results).\\n\\n### RF-013 Reconstructable activation\\n\\nA fresh competent actor inside the declared capability envelope can\\nreconstruct the activated evaluation from the frame declaration, the exact\\nsubject, the basis and the admissible inputs, without undocumented\\nconversational or historical context (P0 with the actor-change premise;\\nrc.2 #rf-013-reconstructable-activation).\\n\\n### RF-014 Capability fit\\n\\nFrame adequacy includes actor usability. When the material manifold\\nexceeds an actor's capability envelope, the remedies are those of\\n[ACTIVATION §2](ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope)\\nstep 3, which owns the list: among them selecting another actor, refining\\nthe frame into steps, sequencing activations and a lawful compression\\n(RF-017). Choosing among them is human authority's, exercised directly or\\nin advance through the grant; ACTIVATION §2 says which of them a step\\nselects itself and which re-enter the grant's owner. The actor may not\\nsilently omit material relations to fit its context (P0, P5; rc.2\\n#rf-014-capability-fit).\\n\\n### RF-015 Residual uncertainty\\n\\nCoverage and evaluation results retain known uncertainty. Unresolved\\nrelations, uncovered evaluations, contested evidence and unknown capability\\nstay explicit. Absence of a recorded counterexample is not evidence of\\nuniversal completeness (P4b, P6; open-world premise; rc.2\\n#rf-015-residual-uncertainty).\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[361,440]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"d64ee5c05aaefac346116c2e43eabf193dd84123f1d461070ecd378ce5e9b551\",\"selected_sha256\":\"88ae16a5bd6a4e267c0ea23bc8ed8715f464e54b446bdd7bfe39cab16e793d92\",\"size_bytes\":4069,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[361,440]},\"sha256\":\"d64ee5c05aaefac346116c2e43eabf193dd84123f1d461070ecd378ce5e9b551\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"a30cc51e-0038-40a9-b689-31edbf1d8abd","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:46:10.382Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:beb1217f0bc49ece8938e3035334411e27497c58b4a4bce36b2db41a700c7d83\",\"sha256\":\"beb1217f0bc49ece8938e3035334411e27497c58b4a4bce36b2db41a700c7d83\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-rf-361\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=f00a56503f4aa031ceb832ba6e12e852d09fec266ea8173a657f0ce9586c9298]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"subject topology and evaluation dependency are distinct relation\\nstructures; a consumer may align them where the governed subject warrants\\nit and may not silently treat them as one hierarchy (P3, P1; rc.2\\n#rf-009-no-assumed-hierarchy). Communication is the exchange of\\ninformation between frames, or between the actors activated on them. An\\nexchange by itself grants no authority, an instance of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds), What\\ncreates no authority, and establishes neither a decomposition nor an\\nevaluation dependency (P6, P1). Communication is new\\nin this list. Purpose and material relation: a configuration assigns\\ninformation exchanges as well as responsibilities\\n([ACTIVATION §1](ACTIVATION.md#configuration)), and an exchange read as a\\ngrant or as a dependency would move authority or change a result without a\\ndeclared relation.\\n\\n### RF-010 Composition on demand\\n\\nUsing several frames does not require composing their internal manifolds.\\nComposition law is required only when the governing evaluation combines\\ntheir internal variables, transports evidence or values across them, or\\ntreats their operations as one material execution relation. Independently\\nactivated evaluations may instead return closed results to one declared\\nconjunction or decision rule (P4a; §6; rc.2\\n#rf-010-composition-on-demand).\\n\\n### RF-011 Topology mutation and recharting\\n\\nAn activated frame declares the topology changes capable of invalidating\\nits coordinates or its materiality judgment. A detected material topology\\nmutation causes reevaluation, frame revision or recharting before the\\nprevious result is reused. Material revision of the frame itself\\ninvalidates for reuse every result bound to the prior revision coordinate;\\n§10 Revision actions states that rule (P3, P4b; rc.2\\n#rf-011-topology-mutation-and-recharting).\\n\\n### RF-012 Closed results\\n\\nEvery performed evaluation of a frame returns one closed result in the\\nframe's declared result algebra: the core algebra of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), or a refinement mapped\\ninto it under that section. That section owns the five core values\\n(`satisfied`, `falsified`, `indeterminate`, `out_of_frame` and\\n`invalid_basis`), their meanings and the rules over them: that nothing is\\ncoerced to success; that a refinement adds no core value, keeps\\nindeterminate, out-of-frame and invalid-basis pressure explicit and raises\\nno result's standing; and that an evaluation not performed has no result,\\nits stop state being\\n[ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#3-step-results-and-disposition). This law\\napplies them to every frame and defines none of them (P5; rc.2\\n#rf-012-closed-results).\\n\\n### RF-013 Reconstructable activation\\n\\nA fresh competent actor inside the declared capability envelope can\\nreconstruct the activated evaluation from the frame declaration, the exact\\nsubject, the basis and the admissible inputs, without undocumented\\nconversational or historical context (P0 with the actor-change premise;\\nrc.2 #rf-013-reconstructable-activation).\\n\\n### RF-014 Capability fit\\n\\nFrame adequacy includes actor usability. When the material manifold\\nexceeds an actor's capability envelope, the remedies are those of\\n[ACTIVATION §2](ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope)\\nstep 3, which owns the list: among them selecting another actor, refining\\nthe frame into steps, sequencing activations and a lawful compression\\n(RF-017). Choosing among them is human authority's, exercised directly or\\nin advance through the grant; ACTIVATION §2 says which of them a step\\nselects itself and which re-enter the grant's owner. The actor may not\\nsilently omit material relations to fit its context (P0, P5; rc.2\\n#rf-014-capability-fit).\\n\\n### RF-015 Residual uncertainty\\n\\nCoverage and evaluation results retain known uncertainty. Unresolved\\nrelations, uncovered evaluations, contested evidence and unknown capability\\nstay explicit. Absence of a recorded counterexample is not evidence of\\nuniversal completeness (P4b, P6; open-world premise; rc.2\\n#rf-015-residual-uncertainty).\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[361,440]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"d64ee5c05aaefac346116c2e43eabf193dd84123f1d461070ecd378ce5e9b551\",\"selected_sha256\":\"88ae16a5bd6a4e267c0ea23bc8ed8715f464e54b446bdd7bfe39cab16e793d92\",\"size_bytes\":4069,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[361,440]},\"sha256\":\"d64ee5c05aaefac346116c2e43eabf193dd84123f1d461070ecd378ce5e9b551\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:beb1217f0bc49ece8938e3035334411e27497c58b4a4bce36b2db41a700c7d83","sha256":"beb1217f0bc49ece8938e3035334411e27497c58b4a4bce36b2db41a700c7d83"},"id":"p2-read-rf-361","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=f00a56503f4aa031ceb832ba6e12e852d09fec266ea8173a657f0ce9586c9298]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"subject topology and evaluation dependency are distinct relation\nstructures; a consumer may align them where the governed subject warrants\nit and may not silently treat them as one hierarchy (P3, P1; rc.2\n#rf-009-no-assumed-hierarchy). Communication is the exchange of\ninformation between frames, or between the actors activated on them. An\nexchange by itself grants no authority, an instance of\n[FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds), What\ncreates no authority, and establishes neither a decomposition nor an\nevaluation dependency (P6, P1). Communication is new\nin this list. Purpose and material relation: a configuration assigns\ninformation exchanges as well as responsibilities\n([ACTIVATION §1](ACTIVATION.md#configuration)), and an exchange read as a\ngrant or as a dependency would move authority or change a result without a\ndeclared relation.\n\n### RF-010 Composition on demand\n\nUsing several frames does not require composing their internal manifolds.\nComposition law is required only when the governing evaluation combines\ntheir internal variables, transports evidence or values across them, or\ntreats their operations as one material execution relation. Independently\nactivated evaluations may instead return closed results to one declared\nconjunction or decision rule (P4a; §6; rc.2\n#rf-010-composition-on-demand).\n\n### RF-011 Topology mutation and recharting\n\nAn activated frame declares the topology changes capable of invalidating\nits coordinates or its materiality judgment. A detected material topology\nmutation causes reevaluation, frame revision or recharting before the\nprevious result is reused. Material revision of the frame itself\ninvalidates for reuse every result bound to the prior revision coordinate;\n§10 Revision actions states that rule (P3, P4b; rc.2\n#rf-011-topology-mutation-and-recharting).\n\n### RF-012 Closed results\n\nEvery performed evaluation of a frame returns one closed result in the\nframe's declared result algebra: the core algebra of\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), or a refinement mapped\ninto it under that section. That section owns the five core values\n(`satisfied`, `falsified`, `indeterminate`, `out_of_frame` and\n`invalid_basis`), their meanings and the rules over them: that nothing is\ncoerced to success; that a refinement adds no core value, keeps\nindeterminate, out-of-frame and invalid-basis pressure explicit and raises\nno result's standing; and that an evaluation not performed has no result,\nits stop state being\n[ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#3-step-results-and-disposition). This law\napplies them to every frame and defines none of them (P5; rc.2\n#rf-012-closed-results).\n\n### RF-013 Reconstructable activation\n\nA fresh competent actor inside the declared capability envelope can\nreconstruct the activated evaluation from the frame declaration, the exact\nsubject, the basis and the admissible inputs, without undocumented\nconversational or historical context (P0 with the actor-change premise;\nrc.2 #rf-013-reconstructable-activation).\n\n### RF-014 Capability fit\n\nFrame adequacy includes actor usability. When the material manifold\nexceeds an actor's capability envelope, the remedies are those of\n[ACTIVATION §2](ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope)\nstep 3, which owns the list: among them selecting another actor, refining\nthe frame into steps, sequencing activations and a lawful compression\n(RF-017). Choosing among them is human authority's, exercised directly or\nin advance through the grant; ACTIVATION §2 says which of them a step\nselects itself and which re-enter the grant's owner. The actor may not\nsilently omit material relations to fit its context (P0, P5; rc.2\n#rf-014-capability-fit).\n\n### RF-015 Residual uncertainty\n\nCoverage and evaluation results retain known uncertainty. Unresolved\nrelations, uncovered evaluations, contested evidence and unknown capability\nstay explicit. Absence of a recorded counterexample is not evidence of\nuniversal completeness (P4b, P6; open-world premise; rc.2\n#rf-015-residual-uncertainty).\n\n","coordinates":{"lines":[361,440]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"d64ee5c05aaefac346116c2e43eabf193dd84123f1d461070ecd378ce5e9b551","selected_sha256":"88ae16a5bd6a4e267c0ea23bc8ed8715f464e54b446bdd7bfe39cab16e793d92","size_bytes":4069,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"REFERENCE_FRAME.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[361,440]},"sha256":"d64ee5c05aaefac346116c2e43eabf193dd84123f1d461070ecd378ce5e9b551"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Woqyjsv4DhyKYRC9HErGYU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
