is not an Ontology); whole-family Prime contraction where every candidate atom kind enters one contraction, each accepted atom declares an admitted domain, and every realisation unit maps explicitly to atoms (e.g. whether separately named operations contract to parameterised atoms); three distinct views (Mermaid classDiagram, sequenceDiagram, stateDiagram-v2) derived from the Ontology, not one flowchart; a cross-view axiom table with pass/fail/not_applicable mapped to core values and gap owners; decision-completeness of M(B) incl. failure/refusal routes, effect/closure laws, public contracts and module mappings. Implementation-introduced material semantic decisions or contradictory projections mean underconstrained. Also: F_D[v] judgments distinct from named acquisition/context/dispatch/write operations; builder STDO 2.5.1-rc.2, consumer RC9 profile and represented subject bases distinct with no label/co-location join; no second lifecycle/ledger/frame or next-action selection; method meaning by reference to owner clauses. Falsified by a named element violating these; indeterminate where cited evidence cannot decide. Design acceptance is not Reviewer authority.\n\nS2 implementation-conservation (adds to E2): FD013 complete: attempt/cost records with units, measured scope, elapsed vs summed actor intervals, usage/cache counters, partial/failed calls, unknown counters and limit-check result; reproducible aggregation without double counting; anticipated separate from observed; unavailable backend usage stays unknown; no benefit inference. Joins follow FOUNDATIONS Conjunction: returned, planned-without-closed-result and uncovered inputs kept apart; any gap never satisfied; stale results are planned-without-result, not relabelled; not-performed carries no core value (EVALUATION s4). ASSURANCE s11: proof must acquire owner-issued subject via runnable surface.\n\nS3 guide-task-criteria: TASK 1-6 as E3; additionally the guide must not present tool output as a semantic verdic