r field, participates. Its acquired raw parent SourceRef/hash, the Context\\nand Preflight artifact hashes, and frame/subject/basis coordinates remain\\nseparate. No caller replacement hash is accepted. The coordinate is published\\nas `activation_identity` in the ordinary Context summary and in its rendered\\n`boundaries`, so an actor can construct the return through the public surface.\\nThis derived coordinate adds no packet field and has no self-hash recursion.\\n\\nEach performed evaluation has exactly `id`, `predicate`, `domain_outcome`,\\n`core_value`, `evidence`, `residuals` and `invalidators`. `predicate` is its exact\\nsource identity or explicitly supplied predicate body bound to the activation;\\n`core_value` uses the source-owned five-value vocabulary. Domain outcome is the\\noriginal JSON value, not a rewritten success flag. `not_performed` lists planned\\nevaluation ids and contains no verdict. `work_result` is null for a return not\\nasserting construction availability; otherwise it contains exactly `value`,\\n`cause`, `candidate`, `evidence` and `residuals`, preserving RC9 ACTIVATION's\\nvalue/cause relation. `candidate_ready` must resolve its exact candidate and\\ntransition evidence. The parser reports a wrong mapping without inventing the\\nWorker's answer. The original bytes always survive invalid format or binding.\\n\\nThis is a serialization of the selected method-owned relations, not an\\nadditional result algebra or requirement that F_P judgment be deterministic.\\nRegistered return-contract SourceRefs resolve the exact ReturnContract content\\nschema and role-specific proof obligations in Closed acquired content contracts\\nbelow; no arbitrary body or hidden proof convention is accepted. Unsupported return carriers remain retained\\nraw output with an explicit unsupported-format gap.\\n\\n### Packet carrier\\n\\nThe `packet` object is a tenant serialization of REFERENCE_FRAME §11's minimum\\nbinding, with exactly the following source-owned groups, not a second packet\\nlaw. The RC9 profile supplies each group's owner route. Group values are closed\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[281,340]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"e937013144570c9b27f5f5c7e9af7ea6cb3a88c3d8ccfeaa90aeff6e31e45259\",\"size_bytes\":3649,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[281,340]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:420f6387a80d0c8b6605db309ea48fe773d620995476de6df9762ef9bc1f729b","sha256":"420f6387a80d0c8b6605db309ea48fe773d620995476de6df9762ef9bc1f729b"},"id":"p2-read-how-005","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=9e50d74753292c03d678275f9b083a7ea4a82a3328ed228ad94525ce588ec7ea]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"acquisition routes; the caller chooses whether to acquire them.\n\nThe exact ordinary CLI entry is:\n\n```sh\npython3 code/ac_support.py --policy POLICY.json --policy-sha256 POLICY_SHA256 --principal EXECUTIVE_ID call --request REQUEST.json\npython3 code/ac_support.py --policy POLICY.json --policy-sha256 POLICY_SHA256 --principal REVIEWER_ID mcp\n```\n\n`--request -` reads one JSON object from stdin. CLI emits exactly one response\nobject on stdout and exits 0 for `ok`, 2 for `refused`, 1 for an external/internal\n`error`; diagnostics belong on stderr. `mcp` serves the protocol below. There\nis one internal fixed supervisor entry, inaccessible through public operation\narguments. No interface changes the operator's host/global configuration.\n\n### Returned actor payload\n\nThe supported closed-return carrier is `a_c.fd-support.closed-return/1`.\nIts exact keys are `schema`, `id`, `frame`, `activation`, `subject`, `basis`,\n`actor`, `consumer`, `evaluations`, `not_performed`, `work_result`, `residuals`\nand `invalidators`. Frame is id/revision; activation is id/SHA-256; subject is\nid/SHA-256; basis is the exact method-profile id/digest plus Observation refs;\nactor is id/family/authorship identity. These coordinates are checked against\nthe original activation and protected identity bindings, never accepted merely\nbecause the answer asserts them.\n\nThe expected activation coordinate is derived only after full packet acquisition\nand validation: `{\"id\": packet.activation.id, \"sha256\": SHA256(canonical(packet))}`.\nThe complete canonical packet body, including revision/configuration and every\nother field, participates. Its acquired raw parent SourceRef/hash, the Context\nand Preflight artifact hashes, and frame/subject/basis coordinates remain\nseparate. No caller replacement hash is accepted. The coordinate is published\nas `activation_identity` in the ordinary Context summary and in its rendered\n`boundaries`, so an actor can construct the return through the public surface.\nThis derived coordinate adds no packet field and has no self-hash recursion.\n\nEach performed evaluation has exactly `id`, `predicate`, `domain_outcome`,\n`core_value`, `evidence`, `residuals` and `invalidators`. `predicate` is its exact\nsource identity or explicitly supplied predicate body bound to the activation;\n`core_value` uses the source-owned five-value vocabulary. Domain outcome is the\noriginal JSON value, not a rewritten success flag. `not_performed` lists planned\nevaluation ids and contains no verdict. `work_result` is null for a return not\nasserting construction availability; otherwise it contains exactly `value`,\n`cause`, `candidate`, `evidence` and `residuals`, preserving RC9 ACTIVATION's\nvalue/cause relation. `candidate_ready` must resolve its exact candidate and\ntransition evidence. The parser reports a wrong mapping without inventing the\nWorker's answer. The original bytes always survive invalid format or binding.\n\nThis is a serialization of the selected method-owned relations, not an\nadditional result algebra or requirement that F_P judgment be deterministic.\nRegistered return-contract SourceRefs resolve the exact ReturnContract content\nschema and role-specific proof obligations in Closed acquired content contracts\nbelow; no arbitrary body or hidden proof convention is accepted. Unsupported return carriers remain retained\nraw output with an explicit unsupported-format gap.\n\n### Packet carrier\n\nThe `packet` object is a tenant serialization of REFERENCE_FRAME §11's minimum\nbinding, with exactly the following source-owned groups, not a second packet\nlaw. The RC9 profile supplies each group's owner route. Group values are closed\n","coordinates":{"lines":[281,340]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005","selected_sha256":"e937013144570c9b27f5f5c7e9af7ea6cb3a88c3d8ccfeaa90aeff6e31e45259","size_bytes":3649,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[281,340]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Rpvc597rVRkAJR6DSx1Bcc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
