{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAzbx9M668rGrSVZNzUZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016481QGaWBmoFGtWMfjsJt3","name":"mcp__ac_review__source_read","input":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-how-007","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[401,460]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9607,"cache_read_input_tokens":257871,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9607},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"3b41be09-7ac2-4d4f-9992-8ca843836d76","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:50:45.959Z","request_id":"req_011CgAzbwqFRVHpKi3rcTmhW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016481QGaWBmoFGtWMfjsJt3":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-how-007","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[401,460]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016481QGaWBmoFGtWMfjsJt3","display_name":"Source Read","server_display_name":"a_c.graphify.fd-support","tool_name":"source.read"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016481QGaWBmoFGtWMfjsJt3","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:82cec947efdd33de95265b66ae4df29c8c58dcb863b9444c950306e505c7357b\",\"sha256\":\"82cec947efdd33de95265b66ae4df29c8c58dcb863b9444c950306e505c7357b\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-007\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=01a49628f0138f9f8c62128b55b6cf9a9c877669e79b97a1815b4d3d6d82a8a6]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"Every dependent effect compares a new observation over the same scope to the\\nretained one, including path population, before its effect begins. Git HEAD and\\nstatus are useful metadata, not authority for current bytes. Stable scope can\\ncoexist with unrelated dirty files outside it; those files are preserved.\\nRead-modify-write operations acquire an exclusive per-target tool lock and\\nrecheck the target inside that lock. The declared threat model excludes a\\nhostile non-tool filesystem swap between check and effect; this limitation is\\nrecorded rather than mislabeled atomic isolation.\\n\\nAcquisition supports regular workspace files, exact Git blobs and protected\\nretained evidence. Whole-content digest and selected payload digest are both\\nreturned. Line reads retain original inclusive coordinates; JSON pointers are\\nexact, and a missing pointer refuses rather than returns null. UTF-8 decoding\\nfailure is explicit; base64 returns actual binary content when requested.\\nMissing mappings and source grounding do not become inferred mappings.\\n\\n`ModelRef` verification uses `ac_graph.validate` or `decode(GraphCarrier)` and\\nchecks exact model and raw carrier coordinates. Existing `find`, `inspect`,\\n`project_many` and carrier identity are reused without editing their model\\nschemas or dependency semantics. A model can be methodology-only; its declared\\nsubject/coverage are always returned. No operation calls it a complete Product\\nworkspace map. Composite/cross-model querying needs an explicit supported\\nidentity/translation rule; this first fragment refuses it.\\n\\n`relations.query` acquires the exact integer-only RelationDeclarations JSON\\nbody and returns the closed RelationQueryResult below. Both schemas are in the\\nshared content catalog/tools.describe; this paragraph supplies no looser\\nalternative. The same validated model, represented subject, native calculus\\nbasis and selected execution-method coordinates bind the declaration and every\\nusable applicability judgment. source -> target means dependent -> prerequisite.\\nOnly explicitly governing, not-authentically-excluded edges participate;\\nunresolved conditions are included conservatively and qualified as unknown.\\nCoverage is raw seed-scoped declared-support mapping, never semantic covered,\\nsatisfied, unaffectedness, F_P frontier selection or automatic re-entry.\\nNative codec closure/governing semantics and all other public contracts remain\\nunchanged; this authored graph is not an alternate authority or activation path.\\n\\n## Product-bound admission and exact dispatch\\n\\nOwner policy has schema `a_c.fd-support.policy/1`, with closed top-level keys\\n`id`, `product`, `method_profile`, `sources`, `principals`, `grants`,\\n`predicates`, `operators`, `executors`, `event_sinks`, `independence_policy`,\\n`evidence_root`, `limits` and `authority_sources`. Operator startup supplies its path and expected digest;\\nthere is no public registration/write operation for it.\\n\\n- `product` binds definition id, exact definition SourceRef and work/outcome\\n  source records. `sources` registers exact local roots/repositories, allowed\\n  read scopes and immutable-source aliases.\\n- `principals` binds startup requester principal to actor id, role, authorship/family\\n  metadata and allowed operations. A request cannot change these values.\\n- Each `grant` names id, existing owner/delegation SourceRefs, exact outcome,\\n  permitted requester principals and activated targets, operations/tools/executors/territory, required material\\n  preconditions, admission mechanism/conditions and `notification_sink` selecting\\n  an existing sink id (or null only for a non-dispatch grant). The operator verifies the\\n  source owners; the tool checks these registered bindings, not the truth of\\n  arbitrary supplied authority prose.\\n- Each `predicate` names id, exact source contract, subject/domain/basis and\\n  supported expression; each `operator` names the exact source-owned\\n  conjunction and selected declared rule, coverage/basis and decision-owner\\n  requirements. These cannot be chosen by an unregistered request definition.\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[401,460]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"888427d69b13404e3dfb3488bd28d7e9e0e1c5f6bda8c014acd2b280c33ddb11\",\"size_bytes\":4060,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[401,460]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"4f0f712b-0da6-4b85-badb-1a38185a547f","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:50:46.664Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:82cec947efdd33de95265b66ae4df29c8c58dcb863b9444c950306e505c7357b\",\"sha256\":\"82cec947efdd33de95265b66ae4df29c8c58dcb863b9444c950306e505c7357b\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-007\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=01a49628f0138f9f8c62128b55b6cf9a9c877669e79b97a1815b4d3d6d82a8a6]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"Every dependent effect compares a new observation over the same scope to the\\nretained one, including path population, before its effect begins. Git HEAD and\\nstatus are useful metadata, not authority for current bytes. Stable scope can\\ncoexist with unrelated dirty files outside it; those files are preserved.\\nRead-modify-write operations acquire an exclusive per-target tool lock and\\nrecheck the target inside that lock. The declared threat model excludes a\\nhostile non-tool filesystem swap between check and effect; this limitation is\\nrecorded rather than mislabeled atomic isolation.\\n\\nAcquisition supports regular workspace files, exact Git blobs and protected\\nretained evidence. Whole-content digest and selected payload digest are both\\nreturned. Line reads retain original inclusive coordinates; JSON pointers are\\nexact, and a missing pointer refuses rather than returns null. UTF-8 decoding\\nfailure is explicit; base64 returns actual binary content when requested.\\nMissing mappings and source grounding do not become inferred mappings.\\n\\n`ModelRef` verification uses `ac_graph.validate` or `decode(GraphCarrier)` and\\nchecks exact model and raw carrier coordinates. Existing `find`, `inspect`,\\n`project_many` and carrier identity are reused without editing their model\\nschemas or dependency semantics. A model can be methodology-only; its declared\\nsubject/coverage are always returned. No operation calls it a complete Product\\nworkspace map. Composite/cross-model querying needs an explicit supported\\nidentity/translation rule; this first fragment refuses it.\\n\\n`relations.query` acquires the exact integer-only RelationDeclarations JSON\\nbody and returns the closed RelationQueryResult below. Both schemas are in the\\nshared content catalog/tools.describe; this paragraph supplies no looser\\nalternative. The same validated model, represented subject, native calculus\\nbasis and selected execution-method coordinates bind the declaration and every\\nusable applicability judgment. source -> target means dependent -> prerequisite.\\nOnly explicitly governing, not-authentically-excluded edges participate;\\nunresolved conditions are included conservatively and qualified as unknown.\\nCoverage is raw seed-scoped declared-support mapping, never semantic covered,\\nsatisfied, unaffectedness, F_P frontier selection or automatic re-entry.\\nNative codec closure/governing semantics and all other public contracts remain\\nunchanged; this authored graph is not an alternate authority or activation path.\\n\\n## Product-bound admission and exact dispatch\\n\\nOwner policy has schema `a_c.fd-support.policy/1`, with closed top-level keys\\n`id`, `product`, `method_profile`, `sources`, `principals`, `grants`,\\n`predicates`, `operators`, `executors`, `event_sinks`, `independence_policy`,\\n`evidence_root`, `limits` and `authority_sources`. Operator startup supplies its path and expected digest;\\nthere is no public registration/write operation for it.\\n\\n- `product` binds definition id, exact definition SourceRef and work/outcome\\n  source records. `sources` registers exact local roots/repositories, allowed\\n  read scopes and immutable-source aliases.\\n- `principals` binds startup requester principal to actor id, role, authorship/family\\n  metadata and allowed operations. A request cannot change these values.\\n- Each `grant` names id, existing owner/delegation SourceRefs, exact outcome,\\n  permitted requester principals and activated targets, operations/tools/executors/territory, required material\\n  preconditions, admission mechanism/conditions and `notification_sink` selecting\\n  an existing sink id (or null only for a non-dispatch grant). The operator verifies the\\n  source owners; the tool checks these registered bindings, not the truth of\\n  arbitrary supplied authority prose.\\n- Each `predicate` names id, exact source contract, subject/domain/basis and\\n  supported expression; each `operator` names the exact source-owned\\n  conjunction and selected declared rule, coverage/basis and decision-owner\\n  requirements. These cannot be chosen by an unregistered request definition.\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[401,460]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"888427d69b13404e3dfb3488bd28d7e9e0e1c5f6bda8c014acd2b280c33ddb11\",\"size_bytes\":4060,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[401,460]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:82cec947efdd33de95265b66ae4df29c8c58dcb863b9444c950306e505c7357b","sha256":"82cec947efdd33de95265b66ae4df29c8c58dcb863b9444c950306e505c7357b"},"id":"p2-read-how-007","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=01a49628f0138f9f8c62128b55b6cf9a9c877669e79b97a1815b4d3d6d82a8a6]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"Every dependent effect compares a new observation over the same scope to the\nretained one, including path population, before its effect begins. Git HEAD and\nstatus are useful metadata, not authority for current bytes. Stable scope can\ncoexist with unrelated dirty files outside it; those files are preserved.\nRead-modify-write operations acquire an exclusive per-target tool lock and\nrecheck the target inside that lock. The declared threat model excludes a\nhostile non-tool filesystem swap between check and effect; this limitation is\nrecorded rather than mislabeled atomic isolation.\n\nAcquisition supports regular workspace files, exact Git blobs and protected\nretained evidence. Whole-content digest and selected payload digest are both\nreturned. Line reads retain original inclusive coordinates; JSON pointers are\nexact, and a missing pointer refuses rather than returns null. UTF-8 decoding\nfailure is explicit; base64 returns actual binary content when requested.\nMissing mappings and source grounding do not become inferred mappings.\n\n`ModelRef` verification uses `ac_graph.validate` or `decode(GraphCarrier)` and\nchecks exact model and raw carrier coordinates. Existing `find`, `inspect`,\n`project_many` and carrier identity are reused without editing their model\nschemas or dependency semantics. A model can be methodology-only; its declared\nsubject/coverage are always returned. No operation calls it a complete Product\nworkspace map. Composite/cross-model querying needs an explicit supported\nidentity/translation rule; this first fragment refuses it.\n\n`relations.query` acquires the exact integer-only RelationDeclarations JSON\nbody and returns the closed RelationQueryResult below. Both schemas are in the\nshared content catalog/tools.describe; this paragraph supplies no looser\nalternative. The same validated model, represented subject, native calculus\nbasis and selected execution-method coordinates bind the declaration and every\nusable applicability judgment. source -> target means dependent -> prerequisite.\nOnly explicitly governing, not-authentically-excluded edges participate;\nunresolved conditions are included conservatively and qualified as unknown.\nCoverage is raw seed-scoped declared-support mapping, never semantic covered,\nsatisfied, unaffectedness, F_P frontier selection or automatic re-entry.\nNative codec closure/governing semantics and all other public contracts remain\nunchanged; this authored graph is not an alternate authority or activation path.\n\n## Product-bound admission and exact dispatch\n\nOwner policy has schema `a_c.fd-support.policy/1`, with closed top-level keys\n`id`, `product`, `method_profile`, `sources`, `principals`, `grants`,\n`predicates`, `operators`, `executors`, `event_sinks`, `independence_policy`,\n`evidence_root`, `limits` and `authority_sources`. Operator startup supplies its path and expected digest;\nthere is no public registration/write operation for it.\n\n- `product` binds definition id, exact definition SourceRef and work/outcome\n  source records. `sources` registers exact local roots/repositories, allowed\n  read scopes and immutable-source aliases.\n- `principals` binds startup requester principal to actor id, role, authorship/family\n  metadata and allowed operations. A request cannot change these values.\n- Each `grant` names id, existing owner/delegation SourceRefs, exact outcome,\n  permitted requester principals and activated targets, operations/tools/executors/territory, required material\n  preconditions, admission mechanism/conditions and `notification_sink` selecting\n  an existing sink id (or null only for a non-dispatch grant). The operator verifies the\n  source owners; the tool checks these registered bindings, not the truth of\n  arbitrary supplied authority prose.\n- Each `predicate` names id, exact source contract, subject/domain/basis and\n  supported expression; each `operator` names the exact source-owned\n  conjunction and selected declared rule, coverage/basis and decision-owner\n  requirements. These cannot be chosen by an unregistered request definition.\n","coordinates":{"lines":[401,460]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005","selected_sha256":"888427d69b13404e3dfb3488bd28d7e9e0e1c5f6bda8c014acd2b280c33ddb11","size_bytes":4060,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[401,460]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016481QGaWBmoFGtWMfjsJt3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
