{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ge7eSgarBP2CrxBaDvP8LV","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:8cbacdc529aa4a0403578180e5113c6fbcbc5ad4e2caa6b2534ed573315bb5fb\",\"sha256\":\"8cbacdc529aa4a0403578180e5113c6fbcbc5ad4e2caa6b2534ed573315bb5fb\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-008\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=fd3a518d4328ec729e7acd374761030e9cb8a0096ab8e8e4c7811066c660252e]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"- Each `executor` names a fixed executable and argv, dependency/configuration\\n  SourceRefs, cwd, allowlisted environment, effective actor/settings, input and\\n  stdout decoders, available tools, permitted local-effect contract and\\n  termination/effect observation capabilities. Public requests choose its id.\\n  No shell parsing, arbitrary executable, argument suffix, cwd or environment\\n  injection is accepted.\\n- `limits` names selected enumeration, message, attempt, observation and resource\\n  bounds with their units/scope. They are this deployment's controls, not\\n  universal method quotas. `authority_sources` names the trusted operator/owner\\n  records; their hashes establish bytes, not author authenticity.\\n\\n`contract.preflight` re-acquires policy/definition/method/grant material and\\nselected current observations, validates the exact packet and registered\\npredicate premises, checks role/effects/tools/territory/result surface and\\nexecutor dependencies, and binds the draft to the exact context digest.\\nOnly `grant.admission.required_predicates` are evaluated for admission, on the\\nactivation subject `packet.subject_basis.subject` and selected execution Basis.\\nThe optional reconciliation selection below is not evaluated on that subject\\nor folded into admission; preflight still validates its closed carrier.\\nIf the protected mechanism's conditions hold it records its actual admission\\nreceipt: mechanism id/digest, authority source, exact contract digest, decision,\\nevidence and predicates actually evaluated. An optional existing admission or\\nowner override is usable only when resolved through the trusted policy's\\nregistered source and exact contract binding. Caller-created receipt JSON,\\na ticket title or successful schema validation cannot substitute.\\n\\nThe admitted artifact is not an indefinitely valid bearer token. Dispatch\\nrechecks all material preimages and authority binding. Drift refuses before\\nlaunch, names which premise changed and retains the historical receipt. It\\nnever silently substitutes new context or settings. Missing basis, authority,\\nclosure or capability is routed through the selected RC9 owners and is not\\nreported as a Worker result.\\n\\nThe following concrete registry carriers close the public policy seams. Registry\\npopulations are id-keyed objects; duplicate ids/unknown fields refuse. Source\\nreferences use the grammar above. The policy's `method_profile` is the exact\\nid/digest plus SourceRef of the shipped binding. Each local source root has\\nexactly `path`, `read_scope`, `kind` (`workspace` or `git`), and `writable`;\\nroot paths are trusted startup configuration, never request fields.\\n\\n| Registry record | Exact fields |\\n|---|---|\\n| Principal | `actor_id`, `role`, `family`, `authorship`, `operations`, `role_binding`, `role_transition` |\\n| Grant | `id`, `authority_sources`, `outcome`, `principals`, `targets`, `operations`, `tools`, `executors`, `territory`, `preconditions`, `admission`, `notification_sink` |\\n| Admission selection | Required: `mechanism_id`, `mechanism_source`, `authority_source`, `required_predicates`, `allowed_override_sources`; optional: `required_reconciliation_predicates` |\\n| Executor | `id`, `executable`, `argv`, `dependencies`, `cwd`, `environment`, `actor_id`, `settings`, `tools`, `effect_scope`, `stdin_mode`, `stdout_decoder`, `observers` |\\n| Predicate | `id`, `source`, `subject`, `basis`, `input_names`, `expression`, `limits` |\\n| Conjunction operator | `id`, `source`, `decision_authority`, `rule`, `plan_source`, `qualification` |\\n\\n`outcome` is id plus exact source; `territory` is a list of registered-root and\\nrelative file/directory scopes. `preconditions` are exact SourceRefs and retained\\nObservation refs. `admission` may reference only the implemented finite\\nmechanism `product-policy-preflight/1`: all source/identity, scope, role, effect,\\nresult-surface and selected registered predicate checks above. It is a real\\nProduct-bound mechanism under the protected policy, not mere shape validation.\\nAn unsupported mechanism id refuses. The mechanism's implementation and policy\\nremain distinct provenance. An override source must be separately registered\\nby the operator and explicitly bind the exact contract; the request cannot add\\none to that registry. No authority is inferred from the words in `outcome`.\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[461,520]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"71607316c84bcd5a77ef517f6ca7048c3f853d85b8240a8d16cc8f17e864aa1e\",\"size_bytes\":4305,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[461,520]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"98d93a7a-cc93-415c-904d-a198afc9c0f8","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:50:51.705Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:8cbacdc529aa4a0403578180e5113c6fbcbc5ad4e2caa6b2534ed573315bb5fb\",\"sha256\":\"8cbacdc529aa4a0403578180e5113c6fbcbc5ad4e2caa6b2534ed573315bb5fb\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-008\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=fd3a518d4328ec729e7acd374761030e9cb8a0096ab8e8e4c7811066c660252e]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"- Each `executor` names a fixed executable and argv, dependency/configuration\\n  SourceRefs, cwd, allowlisted environment, effective actor/settings, input and\\n  stdout decoders, available tools, permitted local-effect contract and\\n  termination/effect observation capabilities. Public requests choose its id.\\n  No shell parsing, arbitrary executable, argument suffix, cwd or environment\\n  injection is accepted.\\n- `limits` names selected enumeration, message, attempt, observation and resource\\n  bounds with their units/scope. They are this deployment's controls, not\\n  universal method quotas. `authority_sources` names the trusted operator/owner\\n  records; their hashes establish bytes, not author authenticity.\\n\\n`contract.preflight` re-acquires policy/definition/method/grant material and\\nselected current observations, validates the exact packet and registered\\npredicate premises, checks role/effects/tools/territory/result surface and\\nexecutor dependencies, and binds the draft to the exact context digest.\\nOnly `grant.admission.required_predicates` are evaluated for admission, on the\\nactivation subject `packet.subject_basis.subject` and selected execution Basis.\\nThe optional reconciliation selection below is not evaluated on that subject\\nor folded into admission; preflight still validates its closed carrier.\\nIf the protected mechanism's conditions hold it records its actual admission\\nreceipt: mechanism id/digest, authority source, exact contract digest, decision,\\nevidence and predicates actually evaluated. An optional existing admission or\\nowner override is usable only when resolved through the trusted policy's\\nregistered source and exact contract binding. Caller-created receipt JSON,\\na ticket title or successful schema validation cannot substitute.\\n\\nThe admitted artifact is not an indefinitely valid bearer token. Dispatch\\nrechecks all material preimages and authority binding. Drift refuses before\\nlaunch, names which premise changed and retains the historical receipt. It\\nnever silently substitutes new context or settings. Missing basis, authority,\\nclosure or capability is routed through the selected RC9 owners and is not\\nreported as a Worker result.\\n\\nThe following concrete registry carriers close the public policy seams. Registry\\npopulations are id-keyed objects; duplicate ids/unknown fields refuse. Source\\nreferences use the grammar above. The policy's `method_profile` is the exact\\nid/digest plus SourceRef of the shipped binding. Each local source root has\\nexactly `path`, `read_scope`, `kind` (`workspace` or `git`), and `writable`;\\nroot paths are trusted startup configuration, never request fields.\\n\\n| Registry record | Exact fields |\\n|---|---|\\n| Principal | `actor_id`, `role`, `family`, `authorship`, `operations`, `role_binding`, `role_transition` |\\n| Grant | `id`, `authority_sources`, `outcome`, `principals`, `targets`, `operations`, `tools`, `executors`, `territory`, `preconditions`, `admission`, `notification_sink` |\\n| Admission selection | Required: `mechanism_id`, `mechanism_source`, `authority_source`, `required_predicates`, `allowed_override_sources`; optional: `required_reconciliation_predicates` |\\n| Executor | `id`, `executable`, `argv`, `dependencies`, `cwd`, `environment`, `actor_id`, `settings`, `tools`, `effect_scope`, `stdin_mode`, `stdout_decoder`, `observers` |\\n| Predicate | `id`, `source`, `subject`, `basis`, `input_names`, `expression`, `limits` |\\n| Conjunction operator | `id`, `source`, `decision_authority`, `rule`, `plan_source`, `qualification` |\\n\\n`outcome` is id plus exact source; `territory` is a list of registered-root and\\nrelative file/directory scopes. `preconditions` are exact SourceRefs and retained\\nObservation refs. `admission` may reference only the implemented finite\\nmechanism `product-policy-preflight/1`: all source/identity, scope, role, effect,\\nresult-surface and selected registered predicate checks above. It is a real\\nProduct-bound mechanism under the protected policy, not mere shape validation.\\nAn unsupported mechanism id refuses. The mechanism's implementation and policy\\nremain distinct provenance. An override source must be separately registered\\nby the operator and explicitly bind the exact contract; the request cannot add\\none to that registry. No authority is inferred from the words in `outcome`.\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[461,520]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"71607316c84bcd5a77ef517f6ca7048c3f853d85b8240a8d16cc8f17e864aa1e\",\"size_bytes\":4305,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[461,520]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:8cbacdc529aa4a0403578180e5113c6fbcbc5ad4e2caa6b2534ed573315bb5fb","sha256":"8cbacdc529aa4a0403578180e5113c6fbcbc5ad4e2caa6b2534ed573315bb5fb"},"id":"p2-read-how-008","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=fd3a518d4328ec729e7acd374761030e9cb8a0096ab8e8e4c7811066c660252e]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"- Each `executor` names a fixed executable and argv, dependency/configuration\n  SourceRefs, cwd, allowlisted environment, effective actor/settings, input and\n  stdout decoders, available tools, permitted local-effect contract and\n  termination/effect observation capabilities. Public requests choose its id.\n  No shell parsing, arbitrary executable, argument suffix, cwd or environment\n  injection is accepted.\n- `limits` names selected enumeration, message, attempt, observation and resource\n  bounds with their units/scope. They are this deployment's controls, not\n  universal method quotas. `authority_sources` names the trusted operator/owner\n  records; their hashes establish bytes, not author authenticity.\n\n`contract.preflight` re-acquires policy/definition/method/grant material and\nselected current observations, validates the exact packet and registered\npredicate premises, checks role/effects/tools/territory/result surface and\nexecutor dependencies, and binds the draft to the exact context digest.\nOnly `grant.admission.required_predicates` are evaluated for admission, on the\nactivation subject `packet.subject_basis.subject` and selected execution Basis.\nThe optional reconciliation selection below is not evaluated on that subject\nor folded into admission; preflight still validates its closed carrier.\nIf the protected mechanism's conditions hold it records its actual admission\nreceipt: mechanism id/digest, authority source, exact contract digest, decision,\nevidence and predicates actually evaluated. An optional existing admission or\nowner override is usable only when resolved through the trusted policy's\nregistered source and exact contract binding. Caller-created receipt JSON,\na ticket title or successful schema validation cannot substitute.\n\nThe admitted artifact is not an indefinitely valid bearer token. Dispatch\nrechecks all material preimages and authority binding. Drift refuses before\nlaunch, names which premise changed and retains the historical receipt. It\nnever silently substitutes new context or settings. Missing basis, authority,\nclosure or capability is routed through the selected RC9 owners and is not\nreported as a Worker result.\n\nThe following concrete registry carriers close the public policy seams. Registry\npopulations are id-keyed objects; duplicate ids/unknown fields refuse. Source\nreferences use the grammar above. The policy's `method_profile` is the exact\nid/digest plus SourceRef of the shipped binding. Each local source root has\nexactly `path`, `read_scope`, `kind` (`workspace` or `git`), and `writable`;\nroot paths are trusted startup configuration, never request fields.\n\n| Registry record | Exact fields |\n|---|---|\n| Principal | `actor_id`, `role`, `family`, `authorship`, `operations`, `role_binding`, `role_transition` |\n| Grant | `id`, `authority_sources`, `outcome`, `principals`, `targets`, `operations`, `tools`, `executors`, `territory`, `preconditions`, `admission`, `notification_sink` |\n| Admission selection | Required: `mechanism_id`, `mechanism_source`, `authority_source`, `required_predicates`, `allowed_override_sources`; optional: `required_reconciliation_predicates` |\n| Executor | `id`, `executable`, `argv`, `dependencies`, `cwd`, `environment`, `actor_id`, `settings`, `tools`, `effect_scope`, `stdin_mode`, `stdout_decoder`, `observers` |\n| Predicate | `id`, `source`, `subject`, `basis`, `input_names`, `expression`, `limits` |\n| Conjunction operator | `id`, `source`, `decision_authority`, `rule`, `plan_source`, `qualification` |\n\n`outcome` is id plus exact source; `territory` is a list of registered-root and\nrelative file/directory scopes. `preconditions` are exact SourceRefs and retained\nObservation refs. `admission` may reference only the implemented finite\nmechanism `product-policy-preflight/1`: all source/identity, scope, role, effect,\nresult-surface and selected registered predicate checks above. It is a real\nProduct-bound mechanism under the protected policy, not mere shape validation.\nAn unsupported mechanism id refuses. The mechanism's implementation and policy\nremain distinct provenance. An override source must be separately registered\nby the operator and explicitly bind the exact contract; the request cannot add\none to that registry. No authority is inferred from the words in `outcome`.\n\n","coordinates":{"lines":[461,520]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005","selected_sha256":"71607316c84bcd5a77ef517f6ca7048c3f853d85b8240a8d16cc8f17e864aa1e","size_bytes":4305,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[461,520]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Ge7eSgarBP2CrxBaDvP8LV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAzchAiZT1vUFDzJnLK1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qb9kNeLqa3NaNztowrcA8B","name":"mcp__ac_review__source_read","input":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-how-009","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[521,580]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7725,"cache_read_input_tokens":267478,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7725},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"0440685e-24b6-4c0a-a0d6-a4990bca2961","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:50:54.030Z","request_id":"req_011CgAzcgs72N4kK3Heqjc5G","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Qb9kNeLqa3NaNztowrcA8B":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-how-009","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[521,580]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Qb9kNeLqa3NaNztowrcA8B","display_name":"Source Read","server_display_name":"a_c.graphify.fd-support","tool_name":"source.read"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qb9kNeLqa3NaNztowrcA8B","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:2c0772a50dbdda40bf7ad6f748040fd7eda89cb51a7b87dd68590d98159cc03b\",\"sha256\":\"2c0772a50dbdda40bf7ad6f748040fd7eda89cb51a7b87dd68590d98159cc03b\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-009\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=f9ee920518527b2109ee4ddd520d89715b38afb836e1bd29f511541ca1ca5a9f]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"This provisional policy/1 refinement permits exactly one additional optional\\nAdmission-selection key, `required_reconciliation_predicates`. It has the same\\nfinite nonempty-string id-list grammar as `required_predicates`, naming only\\nregistered predicates. Other unknown keys, null/non-array values and malformed\\nids refuse under the existing closed policy boundary. Absence means an empty\\nreconciliation selection, not a default predicate or retry permission. Old\\ngrants without an explicit nonempty selection cannot retry. The two lists have\\ndistinct domains: required_predicates is activation-subject admission only;\\nrequired_reconciliation_predicates is predecessor-Attempt/current-Basis\\nreconciliation only. Neither is a source from which the other is inferred or\\nclassified by predicate name, role or matching subject. This adds no public\\noperation, request argument, method law or shared-content schema definition.\\n\\nExecutor `executable` is an exact absolute regular-file path/digest chosen by\\nthe operator; `argv` is its complete fixed string array including argv[0].\\nDependencies/configuration are SourceRefs rechecked before launch; environment\\nis a complete explicit string map, not inherited arbitrary caller variables.\\nThe tool retains any required host/environment unknowns. `stdin_mode` is\\n`context-utf8`; its byte payload is exactly the saved Context rendering, with no\\nunmeasured appended prompt. `stdout_decoder` has exactly `format` (`json` or\\n`utf8`), `pointer` (JSON pointer or null), and `decode_json_string` (Boolean).\\nThis permits a provider's JSON envelope containing the actual answer as a JSON\\nstring to be unwrapped reproducibly. Missing/invalid decoding retains raw output\\nand a format gap. No decoder executes code. Observers are `process-end` and\\n`file-postimages` with exact selected scope/expected hashes; they establish only\\ntheir named predicates, not semantic task success. File completion/end is\\nclaimed only where the registered effect contract and actual observer establish\\nboth; otherwise external effects/descendants remain unknown. `effect_scope`\\ndeclares the expected local-effect and unsupported enforcement boundary.\\n\\n`work.write.record` is exactly `{\\\"text\\\":\\\"literal UTF-8 bytes as text\\\",\\n\\\"provenance\\\":SourceRef}`. Append adds precisely that UTF-8 text, with no\\nimplicit newline or method prose; replace supplies the whole target body.\\n`interpretation` is null or `{\\\"text\\\":\\\"...\\\",\\\"author\\\":SourceRef}` and is\\nretained separately in operation evidence, not silently inserted as an owner\\nruling in the target. New absent targets and existing targets both use explicit\\ngrant/territory and expected preimages as described above.\\n\\n### Attempts, notifications and uncertain effects\\n\\n`dispatch.start` atomically reserves a unique request/activation key under the\\nprotected evidence root before launching a small per-attempt supervisor. This\\nis process supervision for one named invocation, not task scheduling or\\nmethod-workflow control. The supervisor rechecks admission/preimages again at\\nthe actual effect edge, starts the fixed executable with exact retained stdin,\\nrecords acknowledgments, stdout/stderr, events, timestamps and observed process\\nend, and writes the named result surface. Provider/actor settings are retained\\nexactly; provider usage absent from its actual result stays unknown.\\n\\nA repeated exact request returns the existing attempt and its observations;\\na conflicting use of the key refuses. If the caller loses a response or a\\nsupervisor dies during the launch interval, the reservation remains and no\\nautomatic second launch occurs. A fresh actor can acquire the named attempt,\\nreconcile observed effects/end, and supply an explicit already-authorized retry\\nwith predecessor/reconciliation evidence. `retry_of` is required for another\\nattempt of the same activation. The same applicable protected Grant must\\nexplicitly select at least one registered predicate in\\n`admission.required_reconciliation_predicates`; `required_predicates` is never\\nthe retry selector. Every selected reconciliation predicate must declare the\\ncomplete predecessor Attempt id/digest as its exact subject and the selected\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[521,580]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"577fd00e2cb9cfcb5a0fe83d1d7c40be6abe606d9fd719c6cf60b4225e63de6b\",\"size_bytes\":4154,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[521,580]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"223cbca7-9cdc-4b14-8cfc-24d419c7cba7","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:50:54.236Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:2c0772a50dbdda40bf7ad6f748040fd7eda89cb51a7b87dd68590d98159cc03b\",\"sha256\":\"2c0772a50dbdda40bf7ad6f748040fd7eda89cb51a7b87dd68590d98159cc03b\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-009\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=f9ee920518527b2109ee4ddd520d89715b38afb836e1bd29f511541ca1ca5a9f]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"This provisional policy/1 refinement permits exactly one additional optional\\nAdmission-selection key, `required_reconciliation_predicates`. It has the same\\nfinite nonempty-string id-list grammar as `required_predicates`, naming only\\nregistered predicates. Other unknown keys, null/non-array values and malformed\\nids refuse under the existing closed policy boundary. Absence means an empty\\nreconciliation selection, not a default predicate or retry permission. Old\\ngrants without an explicit nonempty selection cannot retry. The two lists have\\ndistinct domains: required_predicates is activation-subject admission only;\\nrequired_reconciliation_predicates is predecessor-Attempt/current-Basis\\nreconciliation only. Neither is a source from which the other is inferred or\\nclassified by predicate name, role or matching subject. This adds no public\\noperation, request argument, method law or shared-content schema definition.\\n\\nExecutor `executable` is an exact absolute regular-file path/digest chosen by\\nthe operator; `argv` is its complete fixed string array including argv[0].\\nDependencies/configuration are SourceRefs rechecked before launch; environment\\nis a complete explicit string map, not inherited arbitrary caller variables.\\nThe tool retains any required host/environment unknowns. `stdin_mode` is\\n`context-utf8`; its byte payload is exactly the saved Context rendering, with no\\nunmeasured appended prompt. `stdout_decoder` has exactly `format` (`json` or\\n`utf8`), `pointer` (JSON pointer or null), and `decode_json_string` (Boolean).\\nThis permits a provider's JSON envelope containing the actual answer as a JSON\\nstring to be unwrapped reproducibly. Missing/invalid decoding retains raw output\\nand a format gap. No decoder executes code. Observers are `process-end` and\\n`file-postimages` with exact selected scope/expected hashes; they establish only\\ntheir named predicates, not semantic task success. File completion/end is\\nclaimed only where the registered effect contract and actual observer establish\\nboth; otherwise external effects/descendants remain unknown. `effect_scope`\\ndeclares the expected local-effect and unsupported enforcement boundary.\\n\\n`work.write.record` is exactly `{\\\"text\\\":\\\"literal UTF-8 bytes as text\\\",\\n\\\"provenance\\\":SourceRef}`. Append adds precisely that UTF-8 text, with no\\nimplicit newline or method prose; replace supplies the whole target body.\\n`interpretation` is null or `{\\\"text\\\":\\\"...\\\",\\\"author\\\":SourceRef}` and is\\nretained separately in operation evidence, not silently inserted as an owner\\nruling in the target. New absent targets and existing targets both use explicit\\ngrant/territory and expected preimages as described above.\\n\\n### Attempts, notifications and uncertain effects\\n\\n`dispatch.start` atomically reserves a unique request/activation key under the\\nprotected evidence root before launching a small per-attempt supervisor. This\\nis process supervision for one named invocation, not task scheduling or\\nmethod-workflow control. The supervisor rechecks admission/preimages again at\\nthe actual effect edge, starts the fixed executable with exact retained stdin,\\nrecords acknowledgments, stdout/stderr, events, timestamps and observed process\\nend, and writes the named result surface. Provider/actor settings are retained\\nexactly; provider usage absent from its actual result stays unknown.\\n\\nA repeated exact request returns the existing attempt and its observations;\\na conflicting use of the key refuses. If the caller loses a response or a\\nsupervisor dies during the launch interval, the reservation remains and no\\nautomatic second launch occurs. A fresh actor can acquire the named attempt,\\nreconcile observed effects/end, and supply an explicit already-authorized retry\\nwith predecessor/reconciliation evidence. `retry_of` is required for another\\nattempt of the same activation. The same applicable protected Grant must\\nexplicitly select at least one registered predicate in\\n`admission.required_reconciliation_predicates`; `required_predicates` is never\\nthe retry selector. Every selected reconciliation predicate must declare the\\ncomplete predecessor Attempt id/digest as its exact subject and the selected\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[521,580]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"577fd00e2cb9cfcb5a0fe83d1d7c40be6abe606d9fd719c6cf60b4225e63de6b\",\"size_bytes\":4154,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[521,580]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:2c0772a50dbdda40bf7ad6f748040fd7eda89cb51a7b87dd68590d98159cc03b","sha256":"2c0772a50dbdda40bf7ad6f748040fd7eda89cb51a7b87dd68590d98159cc03b"},"id":"p2-read-how-009","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=f9ee920518527b2109ee4ddd520d89715b38afb836e1bd29f511541ca1ca5a9f]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"This provisional policy/1 refinement permits exactly one additional optional\nAdmission-selection key, `required_reconciliation_predicates`. It has the same\nfinite nonempty-string id-list grammar as `required_predicates`, naming only\nregistered predicates. Other unknown keys, null/non-array values and malformed\nids refuse under the existing closed policy boundary. Absence means an empty\nreconciliation selection, not a default predicate or retry permission. Old\ngrants without an explicit nonempty selection cannot retry. The two lists have\ndistinct domains: required_predicates is activation-subject admission only;\nrequired_reconciliation_predicates is predecessor-Attempt/current-Basis\nreconciliation only. Neither is a source from which the other is inferred or\nclassified by predicate name, role or matching subject. This adds no public\noperation, request argument, method law or shared-content schema definition.\n\nExecutor `executable` is an exact absolute regular-file path/digest chosen by\nthe operator; `argv` is its complete fixed string array including argv[0].\nDependencies/configuration are SourceRefs rechecked before launch; environment\nis a complete explicit string map, not inherited arbitrary caller variables.\nThe tool retains any required host/environment unknowns. `stdin_mode` is\n`context-utf8`; its byte payload is exactly the saved Context rendering, with no\nunmeasured appended prompt. `stdout_decoder` has exactly `format` (`json` or\n`utf8`), `pointer` (JSON pointer or null), and `decode_json_string` (Boolean).\nThis permits a provider's JSON envelope containing the actual answer as a JSON\nstring to be unwrapped reproducibly. Missing/invalid decoding retains raw output\nand a format gap. No decoder executes code. Observers are `process-end` and\n`file-postimages` with exact selected scope/expected hashes; they establish only\ntheir named predicates, not semantic task success. File completion/end is\nclaimed only where the registered effect contract and actual observer establish\nboth; otherwise external effects/descendants remain unknown. `effect_scope`\ndeclares the expected local-effect and unsupported enforcement boundary.\n\n`work.write.record` is exactly `{\"text\":\"literal UTF-8 bytes as text\",\n\"provenance\":SourceRef}`. Append adds precisely that UTF-8 text, with no\nimplicit newline or method prose; replace supplies the whole target body.\n`interpretation` is null or `{\"text\":\"...\",\"author\":SourceRef}` and is\nretained separately in operation evidence, not silently inserted as an owner\nruling in the target. New absent targets and existing targets both use explicit\ngrant/territory and expected preimages as described above.\n\n### Attempts, notifications and uncertain effects\n\n`dispatch.start` atomically reserves a unique request/activation key under the\nprotected evidence root before launching a small per-attempt supervisor. This\nis process supervision for one named invocation, not task scheduling or\nmethod-workflow control. The supervisor rechecks admission/preimages again at\nthe actual effect edge, starts the fixed executable with exact retained stdin,\nrecords acknowledgments, stdout/stderr, events, timestamps and observed process\nend, and writes the named result surface. Provider/actor settings are retained\nexactly; provider usage absent from its actual result stays unknown.\n\nA repeated exact request returns the existing attempt and its observations;\na conflicting use of the key refuses. If the caller loses a response or a\nsupervisor dies during the launch interval, the reservation remains and no\nautomatic second launch occurs. A fresh actor can acquire the named attempt,\nreconcile observed effects/end, and supply an explicit already-authorized retry\nwith predecessor/reconciliation evidence. `retry_of` is required for another\nattempt of the same activation. The same applicable protected Grant must\nexplicitly select at least one registered predicate in\n`admission.required_reconciliation_predicates`; `required_predicates` is never\nthe retry selector. Every selected reconciliation predicate must declare the\ncomplete predecessor Attempt id/digest as its exact subject and the selected\n","coordinates":{"lines":[521,580]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005","selected_sha256":"577fd00e2cb9cfcb5a0fe83d1d7c40be6abe606d9fd719c6cf60b4225e63de6b","size_bytes":4154,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[521,580]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Qb9kNeLqa3NaNztowrcA8B","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
