partial output\nor another stdout fragment is not an additional closed return. Multiple distinct\nperformed predicates within one actor return are independently keyed by their\nevaluation ids. Each keeps its predicate, domain outcome, subject/basis and\nproducer/run provenance. Matching bytes across distinct genuine keys remain\ndistinct evaluations. Stale/wrong-subject held results remain original evidence\nand create gaps for current planned assessments; they are not relabeled new\ninvalid_basis returns.\n\nThe declared rule selects the first non-satisfied **mandatory applicable returned\nresult in the plan's explicit assessment order**. There is no universal priority\namong the four non-satisfied values. All failures/counterexamples, original domain\noutcomes, provenance conflicts and both gap sets survive. When there is no such\nmandatory non-satisfied return, incoherent required basis relations report\ninvalid_basis; otherwise any planned/uncovered gap reports indeterminate;\notherwise a counterexample to a plan-declared required constraint falsifies the\ncomposite whichever contributor found it; otherwise satisfied is reported.\nNonmandatory results are record-only except such exact required-constraint\ncounterexamples. Required-constraint identity is source/plan-bound; tooling does\nnot infer semantic materiality. Nested joins union inherited failures and\nplanned gaps, recompute uncovered obligations and cannot hide them by wrapping\na prior conjunction as a single satisfied component.\n\nThe exact RF §5 output is computed **after** that core value: satisfied maps to\n`decision(holds)`; falsified maps to `conflict` only when mandatory evaluations\nfor the same exact claim include both satisfied and falsified, otherwise to\n`decision(fails)`; indeterminate maps to `indeterminate`; out_of_frame and\ninvalid_basis are returned directly as those core values. The RF `conflict`\ncause is conditional on the conjunction already reporting falsified. A later\nfalsified return never overrides a different earlier non-satisfied mandatory\nvalue merely to manufacture conflict. Disagreement metadata and counterexamples\nremain present whichever core value the declared rule reports. Gaps are records\nbeside this result, never synthesized component values. This entire method\nresult is distinct from the tool operation's output-availability outcome.\n\n","coordinates":{"lines":[701,760]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005","selected_sha256":"fc65554c3decd4dd11f056ca6b33ea8ba88fde264137c8425b39e5359e3b0fa6","size_bytes":4060,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[701,760]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AdFk9Cg9McBPi1zLWBSANg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAzdSSDwayoVJjaHeYZ7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y4TYCpSwedg88AWEoGVY8C","name":"mcp__ac_review__source_read","input":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-how-013","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[761,820]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7529,"cache_read_input_tokens":275203,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7529},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"76ca27d0-8f86-493c-85b5-034814775347","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:51:05.965Z","request_id":"req_011CgAzdS3A5eAdrTT9emgGv","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Y4TYCpSwedg88AWEoGVY8C":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-how-013","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[761,820]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Y4TYCpSwedg88AWEoGVY8C","display_name":"Source Read","server_display_name":"a_c.graphify.fd-support","tool_name":"source.read"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y4TYCpSwedg88AWEoGVY8C","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:13e9de070d16c59489bf33a1c4845f8bf87db13ce82f402bd6077c6ac3bc33d0\",\"sha256\":\"13e9de070d16c59489bf33a1c4845f8bf87db13ce82f402bd6077c6ac3bc33d0\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-013\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=35cf412f9254645eb0c0b4eab45b7d99fe108666a82715fa4965316cdf9ea665]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"\\n## Existing records, refresh and accounting\\n\\n`work.project` supports exact JSON-pointer and Markdown-heading projections of\\nnamed authoritative carriers, keeping raw original content and source identity.\\nIt does not derive a work-state value from incidental prose. `work.write` is a\\nnamed interface for an already-authorized Writer record. It checks fixed\\ncurrent caller Worker role and named Writer operation grant, exact target territory/preimage and\\nmaterial observations, acquires a per-target lock, rechecks them and writes\\ncomplete exact bytes only under the qualified same-directory atomic publication\\ncontract below; an unsupported filesystem refuses before the effect. Appending\\npreserves original bytes; replacing requires the explicit selected update grant.\\nAbsent-file creation publishes a fully written/fsynced temporary file by\\nexclusive atomic link; any conflicting writer or unexpected target refuses\\nrather than overwrites or exposes partial target bytes. Symlink and protected-policy/\\nevidence aliases refuse. Caller record wording and optional interpretation\\nremain separate; it neither invents an owner ruling nor adopts a recommendation.\\nActual postimage and observed write end are retained before returning.\\n\\n`refresh.prepare` compares actual observations and declared transitive evidence\\ndependencies. Affected support is the intersection of declared dependency\\nclosure and the supplied conservative impact cover. It retains missing\\ncoverage/invalidator premises as unknowns, names new obligations and mandatory\\ngates, and does not prove non-influence from absent edges. Retention on a new\\nsubject requires the registered applicability/preservation evidence; originals\\nremain bound to old subjects. Unchanged applicable support survives role/session\\nchanges. Handoff names exact current work carriers, original/successor results,\\nvalid-support relations, source routes, residuals and unreconciled attempts;\\nit needs no hidden conversation or replay of unaffected work. Frozen studies\\nare never refresh targets.\\n\\n`resources.aggregate` accepts only actually retained attempt/operation records.\\nIt rejects conflicting records for the same evidence identity and deduplicates\\nreplays of that same attempt/counter identity. Equal counter values from distinct\\nattempts remain distinct contributions. Original failures, partial outputs, repair/retry/review/acquisition\\nattempts and unknown usage remain visible. Integer nanoseconds represent time;\\nprovider counters keep units and raw source. Counter identity is attempt plus\\nprovider/counter id, unit and measurement scope; repeated cumulative snapshots\\nof one counter are not additive. Select a supported authoritative snapshot or\\nretain ambiguity; equal content alone is not a deduplication key. Cache/reasoning subsets are marked\\nas subsets and never added twice to totals. Wall elapsed is the union/enclosing\\nboundary declared by the accounting contract; summed actor duration is reported\\nseparately and overlapping intervals are explicit. Known-subtotal and unknown\\npopulation are both reported; missing usage is not zero. Unsupported pricing\\nor a counter's undocumented scope is not guessed. Selected limit checks are\\nfinite declared predicates. No accounting result claims accepted-result benefit.\\n\\n### Closed acquired content contracts (repair-004)\\n\\nThe SourceRefs in relations.query.declarations, results.conjoin.plan,\\nrefresh.prepare.declarations and invalidators, resources.aggregate.accounting\\nand return.capture.return_contract, plus the structured review.prepare.claim route,\\nresolve **actual UTF-8 JSON bodies**, parsed with the same integer-only,\\nduplicate-key-refusing grammar as public requests. They are not merely manifests\\nor arbitrary dictionaries. Their exact keys/types are the following shared\\ncontent schemas. `tools.describe` returns these `content_schemas` with the\\noperation contract, including referenced definitions; request_schema describes\\nthe full request envelope and its SourceRef arguments, while core validates the\\nacquired body against the same published content definition. No private builder\\nor unstated implementation default supplies semantics. Unknown fields/schema\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[761,820]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"b3bb837a600edb7f7d172317e45d53e94102dd6a894768ee9d5ec18f16edaf01\",\"size_bytes\":4177,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[761,820]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"464b6c52-aca4-4613-941a-39d9ba53773d","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:51:06.106Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:13e9de070d16c59489bf33a1c4845f8bf87db13ce82f402bd6077c6ac3bc33d0\",\"sha256\":\"13e9de070d16c59489bf33a1c4845f8bf87db13ce82f402bd6077c6ac3bc33d0\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-013\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=35cf412f9254645eb0c0b4eab45b7d99fe108666a82715fa4965316cdf9ea665]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"\\n## Existing records, refresh and accounting\\n\\n`work.project` supports exact JSON-pointer and Markdown-heading projections of\\nnamed authoritative carriers, keeping raw original content and source identity.\\nIt does not derive a work-state value from incidental prose. `work.write` is a\\nnamed interface for an already-authorized Writer record. It checks fixed\\ncurrent caller Worker role and named Writer operation grant, exact target territory/preimage and\\nmaterial observations, acquires a per-target lock, rechecks them and writes\\ncomplete exact bytes only under the qualified same-directory atomic publication\\ncontract below; an unsupported filesystem refuses before the effect. Appending\\npreserves original bytes; replacing requires the explicit selected update grant.\\nAbsent-file creation publishes a fully written/fsynced temporary file by\\nexclusive atomic link; any conflicting writer or unexpected target refuses\\nrather than overwrites or exposes partial target bytes. Symlink and protected-policy/\\nevidence aliases refuse. Caller record wording and optional interpretation\\nremain separate; it neither invents an owner ruling nor adopts a recommendation.\\nActual postimage and observed write end are retained before returning.\\n\\n`refresh.prepare` compares actual observations and declared transitive evidence\\ndependencies. Affected support is the intersection of declared dependency\\nclosure and the supplied conservative impact cover. It retains missing\\ncoverage/invalidator premises as unknowns, names new obligations and mandatory\\ngates, and does not prove non-influence from absent edges. Retention on a new\\nsubject requires the registered applicability/preservation evidence; originals\\nremain bound to old subjects. Unchanged applicable support survives role/session\\nchanges. Handoff names exact current work carriers, original/successor results,\\nvalid-support relations, source routes, residuals and unreconciled attempts;\\nit needs no hidden conversation or replay of unaffected work. Frozen studies\\nare never refresh targets.\\n\\n`resources.aggregate` accepts only actually retained attempt/operation records.\\nIt rejects conflicting records for the same evidence identity and deduplicates\\nreplays of that same attempt/counter identity. Equal counter values from distinct\\nattempts remain distinct contributions. Original failures, partial outputs, repair/retry/review/acquisition\\nattempts and unknown usage remain visible. Integer nanoseconds represent time;\\nprovider counters keep units and raw source. Counter identity is attempt plus\\nprovider/counter id, unit and measurement scope; repeated cumulative snapshots\\nof one counter are not additive. Select a supported authoritative snapshot or\\nretain ambiguity; equal content alone is not a deduplication key. Cache/reasoning subsets are marked\\nas subsets and never added twice to totals. Wall elapsed is the union/enclosing\\nboundary declared by the accounting contract; summed actor duration is reported\\nseparately and overlapping intervals are explicit. Known-subtotal and unknown\\npopulation are both reported; missing usage is not zero. Unsupported pricing\\nor a counter's undocumented scope is not guessed. Selected limit checks are\\nfinite declared predicates. No accounting result claims accepted-result benefit.\\n\\n### Closed acquired content contracts (repair-004)\\n\\nThe SourceRefs in relations.query.declarations, results.conjoin.plan,\\nrefresh.prepare.declarations and invalidators, resources.aggregate.accounting\\nand return.capture.return_contract, plus the structured review.prepare.claim route,\\nresolve **actual UTF-8 JSON bodies**, parsed with the same integer-only,\\nduplicate-key-refusing grammar as public requests. They are not merely manifests\\nor arbitrary dictionaries. Their exact keys/types are the following shared\\ncontent schemas. `tools.describe` returns these `content_schemas` with the\\noperation contract, including referenced definitions; request_schema describes\\nthe full request envelope and its SourceRef arguments, while core validates the\\nacquired body against the same published content definition. No private builder\\nor unstated implementation default supplies semantics. Unknown fields/schema\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[761,820]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"b3bb837a600edb7f7d172317e45d53e94102dd6a894768ee9d5ec18f16edaf01\",\"size_bytes\":4177,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[761,820]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:13e9de070d16c59489bf33a1c4845f8bf87db13ce82f402bd6077c6ac3bc33d0","sha256":"13e9de070d16c59489bf33a1c4845f8bf87db13ce82f402bd6077c6ac3bc33d0"},"id":"p2-read-how-013","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=35cf412f9254645eb0c0b4eab45b7d99fe108666a82715fa4965316cdf9ea665]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"\n## Existing records, refresh and accounting\n\n`work.project` supports exact JSON-pointer and Markdown-heading projections of\nnamed authoritative carriers, keeping raw original content and source identity.\nIt does not derive a work-state value from incidental prose. `work.write` is a\nnamed interface for an already-authorized Writer record. It checks fixed\ncurrent caller Worker role and named Writer operation grant, exact target territory/preimage and\nmaterial observations, acquires a per-target lock, rechecks them and writes\ncomplete exact bytes only under the qualified same-directory atomic publication\ncontract below; an unsupported filesystem refuses before the effect. Appending\npreserves original bytes; replacing requires the explicit selected update grant.\nAbsent-file creation publishes a fully written/fsynced temporary file by\nexclusive atomic link; any conflicting writer or unexpected target refuses\nrather than overwrites or exposes partial target bytes. Symlink and protected-policy/\nevidence aliases refuse. Caller record wording and optional interpretation\nremain separate; it neither invents an owner ruling nor adopts a recommendation.\nActual postimage and observed write end are retained before returning.\n\n`refresh.prepare` compares actual observations and declared transitive evidence\ndependencies. Affected support is the intersection of declared dependency\nclosure and the supplied conservative impact cover. It retains missing\ncoverage/invalidator premises as unknowns, names new obligations and mandatory\ngates, and does not prove non-influence from absent edges. Retention on a new\nsubject requires the registered applicability/preservation evidence; originals\nremain bound to old subjects. Unchanged applicable support survives role/session\nchanges. Handoff names exact current work carriers, original/successor results,\nvalid-support relations, source routes, residuals and unreconciled attempts;\nit needs no hidden conversation or replay of unaffected work. Frozen studies\nare never refresh targets.\n\n`resources.aggregate` accepts only actually retained attempt/operation records.\nIt rejects conflicting records for the same evidence identity and deduplicates\nreplays of that same attempt/counter identity. Equal counter values from distinct\nattempts remain distinct contributions. Original failures, partial outputs, repair/retry/review/acquisition\nattempts and unknown usage remain visible. Integer nanoseconds represent time;\nprovider counters keep units and raw source. Counter identity is attempt plus\nprovider/counter id, unit and measurement scope; repeated cumulative snapshots\nof one counter are not additive. Select a supported authoritative snapshot or\nretain ambiguity; equal content alone is not a deduplication key. Cache/reasoning subsets are marked\nas subsets and never added twice to totals. Wall elapsed is the union/enclosing\nboundary declared by the accounting contract; summed actor duration is reported\nseparately and overlapping intervals are explicit. Known-subtotal and unknown\npopulation are both reported; missing usage is not zero. Unsupported pricing\nor a counter's undocumented scope is not guessed. Selected limit checks are\nfinite declared predicates. No accounting result claims accepted-result benefit.\n\n### Closed acquired content contracts (repair-004)\n\nThe SourceRefs in relations.query.declarations, results.conjoin.plan,\nrefresh.prepare.declarations and invalidators, resources.aggregate.accounting\nand return.capture.return_contract, plus the structured review.prepare.claim route,\nresolve **actual UTF-8 JSON bodies**, parsed with the same integer-only,\nduplicate-key-refusing grammar as public requests. They are not merely manifests\nor arbitrary dictionaries. Their exact keys/types are the following shared\ncontent schemas. `tools.describe` returns these `content_schemas` with the\noperation contract, including referenced definitions; request_schema describes\nthe full request envelope and its SourceRef arguments, while core validates the\nacquired body against the same published content definition. No private builder\nor unstated implementation default supplies semantics. Unknown fields/schema\n","coordinates":{"lines":[761,820]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005","selected_sha256":"b3bb837a600edb7f7d172317e45d53e94102dd6a894768ee9d5ec18f16edaf01","size_bytes":4177,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[761,820]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Y4TYCpSwedg88AWEoGVY8C","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAze8KLNQRwCThjDPshJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017YfTkG2H68aJdhGP9brCcy","name":"mcp__ac_review__source_read","input":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-how-014","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[821,880]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7212,"cache_read_input_tokens":282732,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7212},"output_tokens":26,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"cd89f0da-11b4-4d7c-9000-56d1f7b10f2e","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:51:10.509Z","request_id":"req_011CgAze7yW2UkQGvd6dScxu","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017YfTkG2H68aJdhGP9brCcy":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-how-014","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[821,880]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017YfTkG2H68aJdhGP9brCcy","display_name":"Source Read","server_display_name":"a_c.graphify.fd-support","tool_name":"source.read"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017YfTkG2H68aJdhGP9brCcy","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:3fe832295eb2997004e12101b0745608774faa74434c0d8e3cb8798c80c55f44\",\"sha256\":\"3fe832295eb2997004e12101b0745608774faa74434c0d8e3cb8798c80c55f44\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-014\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=b976c48d169838a8fc2925cde04f43d83c062c4d4c449fc355a977fdef3f0ba2]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"revisions refuse unsupported_contract/contract_violation as appropriate; an\\nunreadable or mismatched source retains the applicable basis gap. Policy bounds\\nfinite populations. Source/body validity supplies no semantic authority.\\n\\nThe normative schema below is JSON Schema 2020-12 with closed object keys.\\nThe strict JSON parser additionally rejects all decimal/exponent number tokens\\n(including 1.0), duplicate keys and nonfinite values before schema validation;\\nJSON Schema's mathematical integer test alone does not enforce that lexical\\nrule. All quantities are integers, exact integer ratios or explicit null; an\\ninteger is never a Boolean. No implicit null/empty/default substitution occurs.\\nId is a nonempty string; Sha256 is lowercase 64-hex. ArtifactRef.id must equal\\n`sha256:` plus its sha256, beyond the shape check. SourceRef engine spellings\\nare those already pinned in the unchanged method profile. Its object is a full\\n40/64-hex Git object only for immutable-git-blob and null otherwise; selectors,\\nregular-blob/path/read-scope and parent-hash laws above still apply. The schema\\nis a finite serialization, not a replacement method or arbitrary schema engine.\\n\\nJudgmentRef names an exact pointer from the complete envelope root into an actually produced,\\nverified retained record: an authenticated Return's original performed evaluation, or this tool's\\nactual OperationEvidence result.value.judgment. Imported/caller-authored JSON\\nwith the same shape cannot satisfy it. The selected predicate, subject/basis,\\noriginal domain outcome and provenance are checked; no pointer to an arbitrary\\nBoolean is a judgment. ProofCondition.evaluation null means missing evidence,\\nnever a satisfied condition. Applicability null means the source-qualified plan\\nstates an unconditional obligation/assessment. A nonnull Applicability has an\\nexact applicability predicate and actual judgment: satisfied requires it;\\nfalsified excludes it under ACT §1; unresolved/missing/other values leave it\\nrequired and unresolved. Its exclusion is a state, not a result of the skipped\\nobligation. This only serializes ACT Applicability, whose result is preserved.\\n\\n#### Review claim population and exposure scope\\n\\nThe public review.prepare.claim argument remains a SourceRef. Its acquired\\nstructured body is exactly ReviewClaim: `{\\\"id\\\": Id, \\\"candidate_sources\\\":\\n[SourceRef,...]}`. The finite unique list is the F_P supplier's explicitly\\ncomplete declared candidate-source population; that claim of scope is not a\\ntool-inferred semantic mapping. The claim parent's identity is distinct from\\nthese member parents. Exact shape/ref validation rejects duplicate declared\\nrefs, ambiguous whole-parent hashes, dangling/out-of-scope/wrong-parent bindings\\nunder the existing boundary codes. Adding the explicit candidate to the\\npopulation uses exact union, not a second copy of the same ref. Before candidate\\nphase, member locators/hashes can be inspected without reading candidate bytes.\\n\\nAll declared refs plus the explicit candidate participate in historical\\nexposure overlap and actual-delivery checks, including earlier test/fixture\\nmember acquisitions. Matching retains source/parent/selection identity and\\nuncertain overlaps. Opaque prose is retained verbatim; its extra population is\\nunknown, so no clean source-first/independence conclusion covers a broader unseen\\npopulation. Missing or opaque declarations can yield truthful unknown output;\\nactual qualification selects a structured complete population. Candidate-phase\\nproof must bind the same claim/source identity and check the full historical\\npopulation, not merely its manifest file. SourceRef validity, supplied scope and\\nobserved delivery remain distinct from semantic independence.\\n\\nPositive: an exact structured unique population includes both implementation\\nand fixture parents; a prior fixture read is detected for that claim. Adverse:\\nduplicate/dangling/competing-parent refs refuse or retain their precise basis\\ngap, never infer a mapping. Unknown: opaque or absent extra scope cannot certify\\nclean exposure, and an unobserved external acquisition remains unknown. These\\nare uses of review.prepare and existing reads, not a new method sequence.\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[821,880]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"9856eb588b416380c9a8f660ed95dd2c5114d66c29308ac9728e6887632800c6\",\"size_bytes\":4192,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[821,880]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"f4297e5a-d55a-43bb-a772-796a323da2ac","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:51:11.243Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:3fe832295eb2997004e12101b0745608774faa74434c0d8e3cb8798c80c55f44\",\"sha256\":\"3fe832295eb2997004e12101b0745608774faa74434c0d8e3cb8798c80c55f44\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-014\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=b976c48d169838a8fc2925cde04f43d83c062c4d4c449fc355a977fdef3f0ba2]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"revisions refuse unsupported_contract/contract_violation as appropriate; an\\nunreadable or mismatched source retains the applicable basis gap. Policy bounds\\nfinite populations. Source/body validity supplies no semantic authority.\\n\\nThe normative schema below is JSON Schema 2020-12 with closed object keys.\\nThe strict JSON parser additionally rejects all decimal/exponent number tokens\\n(including 1.0), duplicate keys and nonfinite values before schema validation;\\nJSON Schema's mathematical integer test alone does not enforce that lexical\\nrule. All quantities are integers, exact integer ratios or explicit null; an\\ninteger is never a Boolean. No implicit null/empty/default substitution occurs.\\nId is a nonempty string; Sha256 is lowercase 64-hex. ArtifactRef.id must equal\\n`sha256:` plus its sha256, beyond the shape check. SourceRef engine spellings\\nare those already pinned in the unchanged method profile. Its object is a full\\n40/64-hex Git object only for immutable-git-blob and null otherwise; selectors,\\nregular-blob/path/read-scope and parent-hash laws above still apply. The schema\\nis a finite serialization, not a replacement method or arbitrary schema engine.\\n\\nJudgmentRef names an exact pointer from the complete envelope root into an actually produced,\\nverified retained record: an authenticated Return's original performed evaluation, or this tool's\\nactual OperationEvidence result.value.judgment. Imported/caller-authored JSON\\nwith the same shape cannot satisfy it. The selected predicate, subject/basis,\\noriginal domain outcome and provenance are checked; no pointer to an arbitrary\\nBoolean is a judgment. ProofCondition.evaluation null means missing evidence,\\nnever a satisfied condition. Applicability null means the source-qualified plan\\nstates an unconditional obligation/assessment. A nonnull Applicability has an\\nexact applicability predicate and actual judgment: satisfied requires it;\\nfalsified excludes it under ACT §1; unresolved/missing/other values leave it\\nrequired and unresolved. Its exclusion is a state, not a result of the skipped\\nobligation. This only serializes ACT Applicability, whose result is preserved.\\n\\n#### Review claim population and exposure scope\\n\\nThe public review.prepare.claim argument remains a SourceRef. Its acquired\\nstructured body is exactly ReviewClaim: `{\\\"id\\\": Id, \\\"candidate_sources\\\":\\n[SourceRef,...]}`. The finite unique list is the F_P supplier's explicitly\\ncomplete declared candidate-source population; that claim of scope is not a\\ntool-inferred semantic mapping. The claim parent's identity is distinct from\\nthese member parents. Exact shape/ref validation rejects duplicate declared\\nrefs, ambiguous whole-parent hashes, dangling/out-of-scope/wrong-parent bindings\\nunder the existing boundary codes. Adding the explicit candidate to the\\npopulation uses exact union, not a second copy of the same ref. Before candidate\\nphase, member locators/hashes can be inspected without reading candidate bytes.\\n\\nAll declared refs plus the explicit candidate participate in historical\\nexposure overlap and actual-delivery checks, including earlier test/fixture\\nmember acquisitions. Matching retains source/parent/selection identity and\\nuncertain overlaps. Opaque prose is retained verbatim; its extra population is\\nunknown, so no clean source-first/independence conclusion covers a broader unseen\\npopulation. Missing or opaque declarations can yield truthful unknown output;\\nactual qualification selects a structured complete population. Candidate-phase\\nproof must bind the same claim/source identity and check the full historical\\npopulation, not merely its manifest file. SourceRef validity, supplied scope and\\nobserved delivery remain distinct from semantic independence.\\n\\nPositive: an exact structured unique population includes both implementation\\nand fixture parents; a prior fixture read is detected for that claim. Adverse:\\nduplicate/dangling/competing-parent refs refuse or retain their precise basis\\ngap, never infer a mapping. Unknown: opaque or absent extra scope cannot certify\\nclean exposure, and an unobserved external acquisition remains unknown. These\\nare uses of review.prepare and existing reads, not a new method sequence.\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[821,880]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"9856eb588b416380c9a8f660ed95dd2c5114d66c29308ac9728e6887632800c6\",\"size_bytes\":4192,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[821,880]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:3fe832295eb2997004e12101b0745608774faa74434c0d8e3cb8798c80c55f44","sha256":"3fe832295eb2997004e12101b0745608774faa74434c0d8e3cb8798c80c55f44"},"id":"p2-read-how-014","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=b976c48d169838a8fc2925cde04f43d83c062c4d4c449fc355a977fdef3f0ba2]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"revisions refuse unsupported_contract/contract_violation as appropriate; an\nunreadable or mismatched source retains the applicable basis gap. Policy bounds\nfinite populations. Source/body validity supplies no semantic authority.\n\nThe normative schema below is JSON Schema 2020-12 with closed object keys.\nThe strict JSON parser additionally rejects all decimal/exponent number tokens\n(including 1.0), duplicate keys and nonfinite values before schema validation;\nJSON Schema's mathematical integer test alone does not enforce that lexical\nrule. All quantities are integers, exact integer ratios or explicit null; an\ninteger is never a Boolean. No implicit null/empty/default substitution occurs.\nId is a nonempty string; Sha256 is lowercase 64-hex. ArtifactRef.id must equal\n`sha256:` plus its sha256, beyond the shape check. SourceRef engine spellings\nare those already pinned in the unchanged method profile. Its object is a full\n40/64-hex Git object only for immutable-git-blob and null otherwise; selectors,\nregular-blob/path/read-scope and parent-hash laws above still apply. The schema\nis a finite serialization, not a replacement method or arbitrary schema engine.\n\nJudgmentRef names an exact pointer from the complete envelope root into an actually produced,\nverified retained record: an authenticated Return's original performed evaluation, or this tool's\nactual OperationEvidence result.value.judgment. Imported/caller-authored JSON\nwith the same shape cannot satisfy it. The selected predicate, subject/basis,\noriginal domain outcome and provenance are checked; no pointer to an arbitrary\nBoolean is a judgment. ProofCondition.evaluation null means missing evidence,\nnever a satisfied condition. Applicability null means the source-qualified plan\nstates an unconditional obligation/assessment. A nonnull Applicability has an\nexact applicability predicate and actual judgment: satisfied requires it;\nfalsified excludes it under ACT §1; unresolved/missing/other values leave it\nrequired and unresolved. Its exclusion is a state, not a result of the skipped\nobligation. This only serializes ACT Applicability, whose result is preserved.\n\n#### Review claim population and exposure scope\n\nThe public review.prepare.claim argument remains a SourceRef. Its acquired\nstructured body is exactly ReviewClaim: `{\"id\": Id, \"candidate_sources\":\n[SourceRef,...]}`. The finite unique list is the F_P supplier's explicitly\ncomplete declared candidate-source population; that claim of scope is not a\ntool-inferred semantic mapping. The claim parent's identity is distinct from\nthese member parents. Exact shape/ref validation rejects duplicate declared\nrefs, ambiguous whole-parent hashes, dangling/out-of-scope/wrong-parent bindings\nunder the existing boundary codes. Adding the explicit candidate to the\npopulation uses exact union, not a second copy of the same ref. Before candidate\nphase, member locators/hashes can be inspected without reading candidate bytes.\n\nAll declared refs plus the explicit candidate participate in historical\nexposure overlap and actual-delivery checks, including earlier test/fixture\nmember acquisitions. Matching retains source/parent/selection identity and\nuncertain overlaps. Opaque prose is retained verbatim; its extra population is\nunknown, so no clean source-first/independence conclusion covers a broader unseen\npopulation. Missing or opaque declarations can yield truthful unknown output;\nactual qualification selects a structured complete population. Candidate-phase\nproof must bind the same claim/source identity and check the full historical\npopulation, not merely its manifest file. SourceRef validity, supplied scope and\nobserved delivery remain distinct from semantic independence.\n\nPositive: an exact structured unique population includes both implementation\nand fixture parents; a prior fixture read is detected for that claim. Adverse:\nduplicate/dangling/competing-parent refs refuse or retain their precise basis\ngap, never infer a mapping. Unknown: opaque or absent extra scope cannot certify\nclean exposure, and an unobserved external acquisition remains unknown. These\nare uses of review.prepare and existing reads, not a new method sequence.\n","coordinates":{"lines":[821,880]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005","selected_sha256":"9856eb588b416380c9a8f660ed95dd2c5114d66c29308ac9728e6887632800c6","size_bytes":4192,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[821,880]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017YfTkG2H68aJdhGP9brCcy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
