{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P6kDVbfxC1t639KS6M8zWa","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:fe628e73d9417939afc35ee834faa8e1396b17ce6a9195dfb7b36eae5394897e\",\"sha256\":\"fe628e73d9417939afc35ee834faa8e1396b17ce6a9195dfb7b36eae5394897e\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-028\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=f05e7d231ed1f4f9d776be24785a2205f6356cdabbd574a0978b67b6e2c6e84f]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"\\n## Module contracts and composition\\n\\nUse Python 3.11+ stdlib, the existing codec and explicit typed JSON/dataclasses.\\nNo package installation, global MCP configuration, network service, database\\nor second runtime is required. Three files separate deterministic relations,\\nlocal effects and public transport; no speculative generic framework is added.\\n\\n| Module | Owned boundary and exported seam |\\n|---|---|\\n| `code/ac_support_core.py` | Strict grammar and refusal type, Runtime/policy/source/profile binding, source/observation/model/context relations, read/query/review/return/check/conjunction/refresh/resource operations and inventory/schema data. Exports `SupportError(code, reason, gaps, source_refs)`, `Runtime.from_policy(path, expected_sha256, principal)`, `canonical(value)`, `digest(value)`, `read_source(runtime, ref)`, `observe(runtime, scope)`, `check_preconditions(runtime, recheck_set)`, `inventory(operation=None)`, `request_schema(operation=None)`, `parse_request(raw_bytes)`, `validate_request(request)`, `make_artifact(kind, payload, provenance)`, `execute_read(runtime, request) -> CoreOutcome`, `build_preflight(runtime, request) -> EffectPlan` and `prepare_write(runtime, request) -> EffectPlan`. No F_P actor, registered-executor or general-effect launches, and no authoritative carrier writes. Fixed-argv read-only Git plumbing is allowed solely as the immutable-source acquisition primitive, bound to the exact registered root, full object, member path and blob hash, with observed Git executable/configuration scope; no shell, hooks, filters, checkout, configuration mutation, moving-ref substitution or lazy network fetch. This allowance exposes no arbitrary subprocess primitive or new capability. |\\n| `code/ac_support_effects.py` | Protected EvidenceStore, exact preflight receipt persistence, attempt reservation/supervisor, fixed-executor dispatch/observe/cancel/events, Writer effect membrane and retained evidence. Imports core; core does not import effects. Exports `EvidenceStore(runtime)`, `execute_effect(runtime, request, plan) -> CoreOutcome` and `persist_outcome(runtime, request, outcome) -> Response`, plus private fixed-supervisor reentry `supervise(runtime, attempt_ref) -> int`. The int is the OS-supervisor exit code, never a semantic/Worker result. execute_effect remains the sole public-request effect entry; other dispatch/observe/cancel/events/Writer helpers remain internal. Core constructs the Writer EffectPlan; effects only rechecks and executes it. |\\n| `code/ac_support.py` | Thin authoritative dispatcher, JSON CLI and legacy MCP stdio adapter. Imports both modules. Exports `execute(runtime, request)` and `main(argv=None)`. Validates once, routes to existing operations, retains exact response evidence; no independent method logic. Also owns the fixed internal supervisor entry point, which calls exactly `effects.supervise(runtime, ArtifactRef)`. |\\n| `design/fd-method-claude-rc9.json` | Exact data binding to RC9 member bytes and owner routes. Unchanged profile identity/digest required by supported Runtime. No method source-body copy. |\\n\\nCore receives narrow read-only callbacks `resolve_artifact(ArtifactRef)->bytes`\\nand `query_artifacts(kind, exact_match_fields)->HistoryQuery` from the effect\\nedge. It never writes the store or imports effects. `Runtime.from_policy` may\\nreceive these callbacks as optional named parameters; an operation needing an\\nabsent callback returns the exact evidence gap, never an empty successful\\nhistory. The immutable Runtime contains no mutable current-request slot.\\nCore returns the complete-envelope CoreOutcome settled below or the exact EffectPlan below;\\nthe effect membrane retains the envelope and performs only its named operation.\\nEvery handler receives the full strict request, including its identity/hash;\\nWriter and cancel calls cannot lose their idempotence/provenance key. Full raw\\nbytes and canonical parsed/provenance identities are distinct. This seam avoids\\na circular import or hidden mutable request state.\\n\\nThe core Worker owns the public argument/schema inventory in the core module;\\nthe integration Worker emits that one inventory and owns top-level routing\\ntests. All Workers honor the operation names and argument keys above. If a\\nrequired implementation changes a material semantic boundary,\\nit returns the exact design gap to Executive; it does not silently pick another\\npolicy, algebra, state machine or authority route. Equivalent local algorithms,\\nhelper names and internal immutable types remain ordinary realization choices.\\n\\n## Repaired immutable carrier and history seams\\n\\nThese are v2 clarifications/repairs A–G selected by Executive under the exact\\n[T-008 repair contract](../../../.ai-workspace/qualification/t008/design/design-repair-001-contract.json).\\nThey preserve the frozen v1 subject and its original hashes; they do not claim\\nthat the v1 design passed independent assessment or that code already exists.\\nPublic request/response version 1 is still an unreleased construction contract;\\n“v2” identifies this source design revision. Independent assessment of the\\nseparate frozen v1 subject returned falsified for decision completeness. That\\nhistorical result is neither erased nor automatically adopted as disposition.\\nV2 constructed only A–G and retained the additional supported review gaps.\\nThe separately admitted repair-002 now supplies the F1–F5 decisions below.\\nIndependent v3 assessment/disposition remains required; no historical review is\\nrewritten and no overall design-acceptance or implementation-readiness decision\\nis inferred from this authored candidate.\\n\\n### One retained envelope and stable payloads\\n\\nEvery retained domain artifact has exactly these keys:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"a_c.fd-support.artifact/1\\\",\\n  \\\"kind\\\": \\\"context\\\",\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1931,1990]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"a90a18aa31dff905a00cb561b9a4fcc06666c48ee8cfa2282380d975b9d3ed2e\",\"size_bytes\":5794,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1931,1990]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"044166cc-26d9-4f80-bea7-9f9461d028f0","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:52:09.618Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:fe628e73d9417939afc35ee834faa8e1396b17ce6a9195dfb7b36eae5394897e\",\"sha256\":\"fe628e73d9417939afc35ee834faa8e1396b17ce6a9195dfb7b36eae5394897e\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-028\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=f05e7d231ed1f4f9d776be24785a2205f6356cdabbd574a0978b67b6e2c6e84f]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"\\n## Module contracts and composition\\n\\nUse Python 3.11+ stdlib, the existing codec and explicit typed JSON/dataclasses.\\nNo package installation, global MCP configuration, network service, database\\nor second runtime is required. Three files separate deterministic relations,\\nlocal effects and public transport; no speculative generic framework is added.\\n\\n| Module | Owned boundary and exported seam |\\n|---|---|\\n| `code/ac_support_core.py` | Strict grammar and refusal type, Runtime/policy/source/profile binding, source/observation/model/context relations, read/query/review/return/check/conjunction/refresh/resource operations and inventory/schema data. Exports `SupportError(code, reason, gaps, source_refs)`, `Runtime.from_policy(path, expected_sha256, principal)`, `canonical(value)`, `digest(value)`, `read_source(runtime, ref)`, `observe(runtime, scope)`, `check_preconditions(runtime, recheck_set)`, `inventory(operation=None)`, `request_schema(operation=None)`, `parse_request(raw_bytes)`, `validate_request(request)`, `make_artifact(kind, payload, provenance)`, `execute_read(runtime, request) -> CoreOutcome`, `build_preflight(runtime, request) -> EffectPlan` and `prepare_write(runtime, request) -> EffectPlan`. No F_P actor, registered-executor or general-effect launches, and no authoritative carrier writes. Fixed-argv read-only Git plumbing is allowed solely as the immutable-source acquisition primitive, bound to the exact registered root, full object, member path and blob hash, with observed Git executable/configuration scope; no shell, hooks, filters, checkout, configuration mutation, moving-ref substitution or lazy network fetch. This allowance exposes no arbitrary subprocess primitive or new capability. |\\n| `code/ac_support_effects.py` | Protected EvidenceStore, exact preflight receipt persistence, attempt reservation/supervisor, fixed-executor dispatch/observe/cancel/events, Writer effect membrane and retained evidence. Imports core; core does not import effects. Exports `EvidenceStore(runtime)`, `execute_effect(runtime, request, plan) -> CoreOutcome` and `persist_outcome(runtime, request, outcome) -> Response`, plus private fixed-supervisor reentry `supervise(runtime, attempt_ref) -> int`. The int is the OS-supervisor exit code, never a semantic/Worker result. execute_effect remains the sole public-request effect entry; other dispatch/observe/cancel/events/Writer helpers remain internal. Core constructs the Writer EffectPlan; effects only rechecks and executes it. |\\n| `code/ac_support.py` | Thin authoritative dispatcher, JSON CLI and legacy MCP stdio adapter. Imports both modules. Exports `execute(runtime, request)` and `main(argv=None)`. Validates once, routes to existing operations, retains exact response evidence; no independent method logic. Also owns the fixed internal supervisor entry point, which calls exactly `effects.supervise(runtime, ArtifactRef)`. |\\n| `design/fd-method-claude-rc9.json` | Exact data binding to RC9 member bytes and owner routes. Unchanged profile identity/digest required by supported Runtime. No method source-body copy. |\\n\\nCore receives narrow read-only callbacks `resolve_artifact(ArtifactRef)->bytes`\\nand `query_artifacts(kind, exact_match_fields)->HistoryQuery` from the effect\\nedge. It never writes the store or imports effects. `Runtime.from_policy` may\\nreceive these callbacks as optional named parameters; an operation needing an\\nabsent callback returns the exact evidence gap, never an empty successful\\nhistory. The immutable Runtime contains no mutable current-request slot.\\nCore returns the complete-envelope CoreOutcome settled below or the exact EffectPlan below;\\nthe effect membrane retains the envelope and performs only its named operation.\\nEvery handler receives the full strict request, including its identity/hash;\\nWriter and cancel calls cannot lose their idempotence/provenance key. Full raw\\nbytes and canonical parsed/provenance identities are distinct. This seam avoids\\na circular import or hidden mutable request state.\\n\\nThe core Worker owns the public argument/schema inventory in the core module;\\nthe integration Worker emits that one inventory and owns top-level routing\\ntests. All Workers honor the operation names and argument keys above. If a\\nrequired implementation changes a material semantic boundary,\\nit returns the exact design gap to Executive; it does not silently pick another\\npolicy, algebra, state machine or authority route. Equivalent local algorithms,\\nhelper names and internal immutable types remain ordinary realization choices.\\n\\n## Repaired immutable carrier and history seams\\n\\nThese are v2 clarifications/repairs A–G selected by Executive under the exact\\n[T-008 repair contract](../../../.ai-workspace/qualification/t008/design/design-repair-001-contract.json).\\nThey preserve the frozen v1 subject and its original hashes; they do not claim\\nthat the v1 design passed independent assessment or that code already exists.\\nPublic request/response version 1 is still an unreleased construction contract;\\n“v2” identifies this source design revision. Independent assessment of the\\nseparate frozen v1 subject returned falsified for decision completeness. That\\nhistorical result is neither erased nor automatically adopted as disposition.\\nV2 constructed only A–G and retained the additional supported review gaps.\\nThe separately admitted repair-002 now supplies the F1–F5 decisions below.\\nIndependent v3 assessment/disposition remains required; no historical review is\\nrewritten and no overall design-acceptance or implementation-readiness decision\\nis inferred from this authored candidate.\\n\\n### One retained envelope and stable payloads\\n\\nEvery retained domain artifact has exactly these keys:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"a_c.fd-support.artifact/1\\\",\\n  \\\"kind\\\": \\\"context\\\",\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1931,1990]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"a90a18aa31dff905a00cb561b9a4fcc06666c48ee8cfa2282380d975b9d3ed2e\",\"size_bytes\":5794,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1931,1990]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:fe628e73d9417939afc35ee834faa8e1396b17ce6a9195dfb7b36eae5394897e","sha256":"fe628e73d9417939afc35ee834faa8e1396b17ce6a9195dfb7b36eae5394897e"},"id":"p2-read-how-028","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=f05e7d231ed1f4f9d776be24785a2205f6356cdabbd574a0978b67b6e2c6e84f]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"\n## Module contracts and composition\n\nUse Python 3.11+ stdlib, the existing codec and explicit typed JSON/dataclasses.\nNo package installation, global MCP configuration, network service, database\nor second runtime is requir