{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SYPtkRop5jZRVuZgMkoTan","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:5709384e36b757ba246e10b60339ee16caa3875673c961c6eeac827c626c0f6e\",\"sha256\":\"5709384e36b757ba246e10b60339ee16caa3875673c961c6eeac827c626c0f6e\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-030\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=ad6e8e4ad32cdcaf63cf012584b4395cd22a6028b0c1c46acc99443f5bdf946b]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"  \\\"request_sha256\\\": \\\"64 hex characters\\\",\\n  \\\"requester_principal\\\": \\\"executive\\\",\\n  \\\"target_principal\\\": \\\"worker\\\",\\n  \\\"policy_sha256\\\": \\\"64 hex characters\\\",\\n  \\\"recheck\\\": {},\\n  \\\"payload\\\": {}\\n}\\n```\\n\\n`target_principal` is null where there is no activation target. The prepared\\npayload contains the exact admitted operation binding above, not arbitrary\\nexecutable instructions. No public request accepts a raw EffectPlan or changes\\nits operator identity. The dispatcher constructs it from the validated request\\nand trusted policy; the effect membrane compares the full request digest and\\npolicy and reruns the named checks at the actual effect edge.\\n\\nRecheckSet has exactly `schema` (`a_c.fd-support.recheck/1`), `policy_sha256`,\\n`product_definition`, `method_profile`, `sources`, `observations` and\\n`executor_dependencies`. `check_preconditions(runtime,recheck_set)` freshly\\nacquires those exact source/preimage and Observation scopes and returns actual\\nobservations, changes and gaps. A required stale/missing premise prevents the\\ndependent effect; new observations are retained by effects. An old successful\\nboolean is not a fresh check. Core preflight returns a plan with its finite\\nfindings; the admission decision/receipt becomes durable only through the\\nselected effect-owned mechanism and protected policy authority.\\n\\nEffects exports `EvidenceStore.resolve(ref)->bytes`,\\n`EvidenceStore.query_artifacts(kind,exact_match_fields)->HistoryQuery` and\\n`EvidenceStore.retain(envelope)->ArtifactRef`. Retain accepts the complete\\ncore-created provenance envelope, verifies its canonical bytes/ref and publishes\\nthose exact bytes; it never constructs or patches semantic payloads. The only\\npublic-request effect entry is `execute_effect(runtime,request,plan)`; the private fixed-supervisor cross-module reentry is `supervise(runtime,attempt_ref)->int`. Every other internal\\nhandler receives the full request, not an arguments-only object or hidden\\nmutable current-request global. Equivalent local immutable helper types are\\nallowed; these cross-module JSON meanings and effect ownership are fixed.\\n\\n### Verified cross-process history and exposure\\n\\nHistoryQuery has exactly `refs`, `complete`, `gaps`, `scope` and\\n`observed_at_ns`. The store enumerates/rebuilds its protected immutable operation\\nhistory within the declared Product/principal/evidence scope. Any index is only\\nan accelerator: entry bytes/hashes and exact match fields are verified, and a\\nstale index cannot hide a later record. Core independently resolves and checks\\nreturned matching envelopes. Unreadable/corrupt/in-flight history or an unknown\\nhistory prefix produces explicit incomplete coverage/gaps, never an apparently\\ncomplete empty list. A caller can still acquire partial known records; a\\npredicate requiring complete history cannot rely on that incomplete result.\\n\\nEvery operation actually supplying source/candidate-derived content retains an\\nacquisition record: recipient/requester actor, exact parent source/model/carrier\\nidentity, supplied selection/range/record population, operation, observed\\ndelivery interval and request/attempt provenance. This includes source.read,\\nrecords.read/find, graph.project, evidence.read of such content, review content\\nacquisition and actual dispatched context delivery. A manifest/hash alone is\\nnot recorded as full payload delivery. Partial/unknown delivery stays scoped.\\n\\nA known structured ReviewClaim supplies its explicitly declared complete\\ncandidate-source population through its bound claim source, unioned with the\\nexplicit candidate reference. Opaque prose retains unknown additional scope;\\nit is never parsed as an implicit source map. Matching uses verified source\\nidentity/digest and actual selection overlap; model acquisition may additionally\\nmatch an exact model id/digest under its declared representation equivalence.\\nNo guessed semantic source mapping is introduced. When a claim becomes known,\\nits check queries earlier acquisitions retrospectively; source.read or record\\nreads before review.prepare cannot disappear across CLI processes or sessions.\\nConcurrent intervals that do not establish order remain uncertain. Unobserved\\nexternal exposure is always a separate unknown, even when public history is\\ncomplete. The tool reports observed ordering, not an unconditional certificate\\nof independent reasoning or absence of prior knowledge.\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[2060,2129]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"a98760ba3b65d645df97b31cfb2ad3e668dbbd7159e83f82ad7493d1b3bcd27b\",\"size_bytes\":4363,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[2060,2129]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"3d036867-9cb4-4790-9ab5-443cf346a38b","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:52:31.210Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:5709384e36b757ba246e10b60339ee16caa3875673c961c6eeac827c626c0f6e\",\"sha256\":\"5709384e36b757ba246e10b60339ee16caa3875673c961c6eeac827c626c0f6e\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-030\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=ad6e8e4ad32cdcaf63cf012584b4395cd22a6028b0c1c46acc99443f5bdf946b]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"  \\\"request_sha256\\\": \\\"64 hex characters\\\",\\n  \\\"requester_principal\\\": \\\"executive\\\",\\n  \\\"target_principal\\\": \\\"worker\\\",\\n  \\\"policy_sha256\\\": \\\"64 hex characters\\\",\\n  \\\"recheck\\\": {},\\n  \\\"payload\\\": {}\\n}\\n```\\n\\n`target_principal` is null where there is no activation target. The prepared\\npayload contains the exact admitted operation binding above, not arbitrary\\nexecutable instructions. No public request accepts a raw EffectPlan or changes\\nits operator identity. The dispatcher constructs it from the validated request\\nand trusted policy; the effect membrane compares the full request digest and\\npolicy and reruns the named checks at the actual effect edge.\\n\\nRecheckSet has exactly `schema` (`a_c.fd-support.recheck/1`), `policy_sha256`,\\n`product_definition`, `method_profile`, `sources`, `observations` and\\n`executor_dependencies`. `check_preconditions(runtime,recheck_set)` freshly\\nacquires those exact source/preimage and Observation scopes and returns actual\\nobservations, changes and gaps. A required stale/missing premise prevents the\\ndependent effect; new observations are retained by effects. An old successful\\nboolean is not a fresh check. Core preflight returns a plan with its finite\\nfindings; the admission decision/receipt becomes durable only through the\\nselected effect-owned mechanism and protected policy authority.\\n\\nEffects exports `EvidenceStore.resolve(ref)->bytes`,\\n`EvidenceStore.query_artifacts(kind,exact_match_fields)->HistoryQuery` and\\n`EvidenceStore.retain(envelope)->ArtifactRef`. Retain accepts the complete\\ncore-created provenance envelope, verifies its canonical bytes/ref and publishes\\nthose exact bytes; it never constructs or patches semantic payloads. The only\\npublic-request effect entry is `execute_effect(runtime,request,plan)`; the private fixed-supervisor cross-module reentry is `supervise(runtime,attempt_ref)->int`. Every other internal\\nhandler receives the full request, not an arguments-only object or hidden\\nmutable current-request global. Equivalent local immutable helper types are\\nallowed; these cross-module JSON meanings and effect ownership are fixed.\\n\\n### Verified cross-process history and exposure\\n\\nHistoryQuery has exactly `refs`, `complete`, `gaps`, `scope` and\\n`observed_at_ns`. The store enumerates/rebuilds its protected immutable operation\\nhistory within the declared Product/principal/evidence scope. Any index is only\\nan accelerator: entry bytes/hashes and exact match fields are verified, and a\\nstale index cannot hide a later record. Core independently resolves and checks\\nreturned matching envelopes. Unreadable/corrupt/in-flight history or an unknown\\nhistory prefix produces explicit incomplete coverage/gaps, never an apparently\\ncomplete empty list. A caller can still acquire partial known records; a\\npredicate requiring complete history cannot rely on that incomplete result.\\n\\nEvery operation actually supplying source/candidate-derived content retains an\\nacquisition record: recipient/requester actor, exact parent source/model/carrier\\nidentity, supplied selection/range/record population, operation, observed\\ndelivery interval and request/attempt provenance. This includes source.read,\\nrecords.read/find, graph.project, evidence.read of such content, review content\\nacquisition and actual dispatched context delivery. A manifest/hash alone is\\nnot recorded as full payload delivery. Partial/unknown delivery stays scoped.\\n\\nA known structured ReviewClaim supplies its explicitly declared complete\\ncandidate-source population through its bound claim source, unioned with the\\nexplicit candidate reference. Opaque prose retains unknown additional scope;\\nit is never parsed as an implicit source map. Matching uses verified source\\nidentity/digest and actual selection overlap; model acquisition may additionally\\nmatch an exact model id/digest under its declared representation equivalence.\\nNo guessed semantic source mapping is introduced. When a claim becomes known,\\nits check queries earlier acquisitions retrospectively; source.read or record\\nreads before review.prepare cannot disappear across CLI processes or sessions.\\nConcurrent intervals that do not establish order remain uncertain. Unobserved\\nexternal exposure is always a separate unknown, even when public history is\\ncomplete. The tool reports observed ordering, not an unconditional certificate\\nof independent reasoning or absence of prior knowledge.\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[2060,2129]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"a98760ba3b65d645df97b31cfb2ad3e668dbbd7159e83f82ad7493d1b3bcd27b\",\"size_bytes\":4363,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[2060,2129]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:5709384e36b757ba246e10b60339ee16caa3875673c961c6eeac827c626c0f6e","sha256":"5709384e36b757ba246e10b60339ee16caa3875673c961c6eeac827c626c0f6e"},"id":"p2-read-how-030","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=ad6e8e4ad32cdcaf63cf012584b4395cd22a6028b0c1c46acc99443f5bdf946b]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"  \"request_sha256\": \"64 hex characters\",\n  \"requester_principal\": \"executive\",\n  \"target_principal\": \"worker\",\n  \"policy_sha256\": \"64 hex characters\",\n  \"recheck\": {},\n  \"payload\": {}\n}\n```\n\n`target_principal` is null where there is no activation target. The prepared\npayload contains the exact admitted operation binding above, not arbitrary\nexecutable instructions. No public request accepts a raw EffectPlan or changes\nits operator identity. The dispatcher constructs it from the validated request\nand trusted policy; the effect membrane compares the full request digest and\npolicy and reruns the named checks at the actual effect edge.\n\nRecheckSet has exactly `schema` (`a_c.fd-support.recheck/1`), `policy_sha256`,\n`product_definition`, `method_profile`, `sources`, `observations` and\n`executor_dependencies`. `check_preconditions(runtime,recheck_set)` freshly\nacquires those exact source/preimage and Observation scopes and returns actual\nobservations, changes and gaps. A required stale/missing premise prevents the\ndependent effect; new observations are retained by effects. An old successful\nboolean is not a fresh check. Core preflight returns a plan with its finite\nfindings; the admission decision/receipt becomes durable only through the\nselected effect-owned mechanism and protected policy authority.\n\nEffects exports `EvidenceStore.resolve(ref)->bytes`,\n`EvidenceStore.query_artifacts(kind,exact_match_fields)->HistoryQuery` and\n`EvidenceStore.retain(envelope)->ArtifactRef`. Retain accepts the complete\ncore-created provenance envelope, verifies its canonical bytes/ref and publishes\nthose exact bytes; it never constructs or patches semantic payloads. The only\npublic-request effect entry is `execute_effect(runtime,request,plan)`; the private fixed-supervisor cross-module reentry is `supervise(runtime,attempt_ref)->int`. Every other internal\nhandler receives the full request, not an arguments-only object or hidden\nmutable current-request global. Equivalent local immutable helper types are\nallowed; these cross-module JSON meanings and effect ownership are fixed.\n\n### Verified cross-process history and exposure\n\nHistoryQuery has exactly `refs`, `complete`, `gaps`, `scope` and\n`observed_at_ns`. The store enumerates/rebuilds its protected immutable operation\nhistory within the declared Product/principal/evidence scope. Any index is only\nan accelerator: entry bytes/hashes and exact match fields are verified, and a\nstale index cannot hide a later record. Core independently resolves and checks\nreturned matching envelopes. Unreadable/corrupt/in-flight history or an unknown\nhistory prefix produces explicit incomplete coverage/gaps, never an apparently\ncomplete empty list. A caller can still acquire partial known records; a\npredicate requiring complete history cannot rely on that incomplete result.\n\nEvery operation actually supplying source/candidate-derived content retains an\nacquisition record: recipient/requester actor, exact parent source/model/carrier\nidentity, supplied selection/range/record population, operation, observed\ndelivery interval and request/attempt provenance. This includes source.read,\nrecords.read/find, graph.project, evidence.read of such content, review content\nacquisition and actual dispatched context delivery. A manifest/hash alone is\nnot recorded as full payload delivery. Partial/unknown delivery stays scoped.\n\nA known structured ReviewClaim supplies its explicitly declared complete\ncandidate-source population through its bound claim source, unioned with the\nexplicit candidate reference. Opaque prose retains unknown additional scope;\nit is never parsed as an implicit source map. Matching uses verified source\nidentity/digest and actual selection overlap; model acquisition may additionally\nmatch an exact model id/digest under its declared representation equivalence.\nNo guessed semantic source mapping is introduced. When a claim becomes known,\nits check queries earlier acquisitions retrospectively; source.read or record\nreads before review.prepare cannot disappear across CLI processes or sessions.\nConcurrent intervals that do not establish order remain uncertain. Unobserved\nexternal exposure is always a separate unknown, even when public history is\ncomplete. The tool reports observed ordering, not an unconditional certificate\nof independent reasoning or absence of prior knowledge.\n\n","coordinates":{"lines":[2060,2129]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005","selected_sha256":"a98760ba3b65d645df97b31cfb2ad3e668dbbd7159e83f82ad7493d1b3bcd27b","size_bytes":4363,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[2060,2129]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-suppor