{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014sNMCexYiXhSwHX8tC4bDn","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:ce42e430676ddaffa29056f9b5959d942149257169670fa707cd5f33d6c4212f\",\"sha256\":\"ce42e430676ddaffa29056f9b5959d942149257169670fa707cd5f33d6c4212f\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-047\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=adebb2907e86bf5649e2ad6e2f95d538a5701308ee3eee32216e25ae6a0685f0]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"(`indefinite`). The Grant has the sole notification selection field\\n`notification_sink`, required in every Grant: an existing registered sink id or\\nnull. If its permitted operations include dispatch.start it must be a nonnull\\nregistered id; null is permitted only for a non-dispatch grant. Executor records\\nhave no notification-selection field or authority. Preflight resolves this id\\nfrom the selected Grant, requires the sink consumer to equal the activated\\npacket's declared consumer, and rechecks sink/Grant/policy bytes at the effect\\nedge. Attempt.notification is exactly `{\\\"sink_id\\\":string,\\\"binding\\\":SinkRecord}`;\\n`binding` is the complete exact registered record above, whose directory is\\nresolved only beneath the same protected evidence root bound by policy. The\\nconsumer is derived only from that binding, never from request or Executor\\nsettings. No default sink or implicit sole-sink selection exists. Missing/null\\ndispatch selection, mismatched consumer or unknown id refuses before\\nreservation/launch as contract_violation (or authority_missing where the\\nunderlying grant itself is absent). Unsupported kind, escaped path, absent\\nconsumer/authority or unknown sink\\nrefuses before delivery; public requests cannot register an endpoint. Sinks are\\nnot independent sources of work-state truth. Indexes/cursors are projection\\nmetadata, not an alternate admission ledger.\\n\\nWhole-family contraction uses eight semantic atoms, with admitted domains:\\n**Acquire** (permitted exact bytes/typed records); **Project** (authored finite\\nrelationships/content); **Evaluate** (supported source-bound predicate/join);\\n**Render** (selected packet to measured exact context); **Admit** (complete\\nProduct-bound finite relation); **Invoke** (registered exact effect);\\n**Observe** (declared external/effect/time/resource facts); and **Record**\\n(atomic existing-grant evidence or Writer unit with explicit source owner).\\nThese are implementation operation families, not new functor kinds.\\n\\n| Public operations | Derived atoms / module projection |\\n|---|---|\\n| tools.describe | Acquire+Project registered contract data; core, thin adapter. |\\n| workspace.observe; source.read; records.find/read; evidence.read; work.project | Acquire+Project; core with representation-specific adapters. Raw/source/record/carrier reads share authority/path/hash law instead of becoming competing acquisition centers. |\\n| graph.project; relations.query | Acquire+Project finite declared relations; reuse codec closure; no inferred semantic dependency engine. |\\n| context.assemble | Acquire+Project+Render+Evaluate fit; core, effect-owned immutable retention. |\\n| contract.preflight | Acquire+Evaluate+Admit; core prepares exact relation, effect edge commits receipt once. |\\n| dispatch.start | Admit existing receipt+Invoke+Record intent/actual observations; effects. |\\n| dispatch.observe; dispatch.cancel; events.wait | Observe or already-authorized Invoke cancellation+Observe+Record; effects. No scheduler/continuation atom. |\\n| return.capture; return.check | Acquire+Record original, then Evaluate exact binding/currentness; core plus store. |\\n| review.prepare | Acquire+Project+Record supplied F_P assertion/exposure; no semantic-review oracle. |\\n| checks.evaluate; results.conjoin | Evaluate only qualified declared predicates/operators; core. |\\n| work.write | Core prepares exact existing-owner Writer relation; effects Admit+Record one transition and Observe actual result. |\\n| refresh.prepare | Acquire+Project+Evaluate selected impact/reuse, Render handoff; no autonomous refresh policy. |\\n| resources.aggregate | Acquire+Project counters and Evaluate selected limits; core, no benefit inference. |\\n\\nThe three modules are realization projections of these atoms. Core owns typed\\nrelations/complete envelopes, effects owns atomic persistence/external edges,\\nand adapter owns only wire dispatch/serialization. Public read variants remain\\nuseful typed projections of Acquire/Project; they do not duplicate authority.\\nThe carrier inventory is irreducible for this selected boundary: trusted\\nsource/policy, observed exact inputs, activated Context/receipt, Attempt anchor,\\noriginal Return and evidence cannot be merged without collapsing authority,\\ncurrentness, invocation or predicate distinctions. Helper classes, indexes and\\nprotocol wrappers are subordinate representations, not additional semantic\\ncenters. No functionality row is unowned: all 23 operations are derived above;\\nunsupported cross-method/calculus/provider/distributed forms are explicit\\nexcluded domains, with no fallback route.\\n\\nContract state is an explicit field separate from receipt decision and\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[2791,2849]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"d34170d3faee4a0eb8050998c4274cbdabff4819730cc3987433ad9160d013c9\",\"size_bytes\":4642,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[2791,2849]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"a3aed561-f05b-4c26-b662-a28a7646ab1f","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:54:13.125Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:ce42e430676ddaffa29056f9b5959d942149257169670fa707cd5f33d6c4212f\",\"sha256\":\"ce42e430676ddaffa29056f9b5959d942149257169670fa707cd5f33d6c4212f\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-047\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=adebb2907e86bf5649e2ad6e2f95d538a5701308ee3eee32216e25ae6a0685f0]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"(`indefinite`). The Grant has the sole notification selection field\\n`notification_sink`, required in every Grant: an existing registered sink id or\\nnull. If its permitted operations include dispatch.start it must be a nonnull\\nregistered id; null is permitted only for a non-dispatch grant. Executor records\\nhave no notification-selection field or authority. Preflight resolves this id\\nfrom the selected Grant, requires the sink consumer to equal the activated\\npacket's declared consumer, and rechecks sink/Grant/policy bytes at the effect\\nedge. Attempt.notification is exactly `{\\\"sink_id\\\":string,\\\"binding\\\":SinkRecord}`;\\n`binding` is the complete exact registered record above, whose directory is\\nresolved only beneath the same protected evidence root bound by policy. The\\nconsumer is derived only from that binding, never from request or Executor\\nsettings. No default sink or implicit sole-sink selection exists. Missing/null\\ndispatch selection, mismatched consumer or unknown id refuses before\\nreservation/launch as contract_violation (or authority_missing where the\\nunderlying grant itself is absent). Unsupported kind, escaped path, absent\\nconsumer/authority or unknown sink\\nrefuses before delivery; public requests cannot register an endpoint. Sinks are\\nnot independent sources of work-state truth. Indexes/cursors are projection\\nmetadata, not an alternate admission ledger.\\n\\nWhole-family contraction uses eight semantic atoms, with admitted domains:\\n**Acquire** (permitted exact bytes/typed records); **Project** (authored finite\\nrelationships/content); **Evaluate** (supported source-bound predicate/join);\\n**Render** (selected packet to measured exact context); **Admit** (complete\\nProduct-bound finite relation); **Invoke** (registered exact effect);\\n**Observe** (declared external/effect/time/resource facts); and **Record**\\n(atomic existing-grant evidence or Writer unit with explicit source owner).\\nThese are implementation operation families, not new functor kinds.\\n\\n| Public operations | Derived atoms / module projection |\\n|---|---|\\n| tools.describe | Acquire+Project registered contract data; core, thin adapter. |\\n| workspace.observe; source.read; records.find/read; evidence.read; work.project | Acquire+Project; core with representation-specific adapters. Raw/source/record/carrier reads share authority/path/hash law instead of becoming competing acquisition centers. |\\n| graph.project; relations.query | Acquire+Project finite declared relations; reuse codec closure; no inferred semantic dependency engine. |\\n| context.assemble | Acquire+Project+Render+Evaluate fit; core, effect-owned immutable retention. |\\n| contract.preflight | Acquire+Evaluate+Admit; core prepares exact relation, effect edge commits receipt once. |\\n| dispatch.start | Admit existing receipt+Invoke+Record intent/actual observations; effects. |\\n| dispatch.observe; dispatch.cancel; events.wait | Observe or already-authorized Invoke cancellation+Observe+Record; effects. No scheduler/continuation atom. |\\n| return.capture; return.check | Acquire+Record original, then Evaluate exact binding/currentness; core plus store. |\\n| review.prepare | Acquire+Project+Record supplied F_P assertion/exposure; no semantic-review oracle. |\\n| checks.evaluate; results.conjoin | Evaluate only qualified declared predicates/operators; core. |\\n| work.write | Core prepares exact existing-owner Writer relation; effects Admit+Record one transition and Observe actual result. |\\n| refresh.prepare | Acquire+Project+Evaluate selected impact/reuse, Render handoff; no autonomous refresh policy. |\\n| resources.aggregate | Acquire+Project counters and Evaluate selected limits; core, no benefit inference. |\\n\\nThe three modules are realization projections of these atoms. Core owns typed\\nrelations/complete envelopes, effects owns atomic persistence/external edges,\\nand adapter owns only wire dispatch/serialization. Public read variants remain\\nuseful typed projections of Acquire/Project; they do not duplicate authority.\\nThe carrier inventory is irreducible for this selected boundary: trusted\\nsource/policy, observed exact inputs, activated Context/receipt, Attempt anchor,\\noriginal Return and evidence cannot be merged without collapsing authority,\\ncurrentness, invocation or predicate distinctions. Helper classes, indexes and\\nprotocol wrappers are subordinate representations, not additional semantic\\ncenters. No functionality row is unowned: all 23 operations are derived above;\\nunsupported cross-method/calculus/provider/distributed forms are explicit\\nexcluded domains, with no fallback route.\\n\\nContract state is an explicit field separate from receipt decision and\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[2791,2849]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"d34170d3faee4a0eb8050998c4274cbdabff4819730cc3987433ad9160d013c9\",\"size_bytes\":4642,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[2791,2849]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:ce42e430676ddaffa29056f9b5959d942149257169670fa707cd5f33d6c4212f","sha256":"ce42e430676ddaffa29056f9b5959d942149257169670fa707cd5f33d6c4212f"},"id":"p2-read-how-047","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=adebb2907e86bf5649e2ad6e2f95d538a5701308ee3eee32216e25ae6a0685f0]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"(`indefinite`). The Grant has the sole notification selection field\n`notification_sink`, required in every Grant: an existing registered sink id or\nnull. If its permitted operations include dispatch.start it must be a nonnull\nregistered id; null is permitted only for a non-dispatch grant. Executor records\nhave no notification-selection field or authority. Preflight resolves this id\nfrom the selected Grant, requires the sink consumer to equal the activated\npacket's declared consumer, and rechecks sink/Grant/policy bytes at the effect\nedge. Attempt.notification is exactly `{\"sink_id\":string,\"binding\":SinkRecord}`;\n`binding` is the complete exact registered record above, whose directory is\nresolved only beneath the same protected evidence root bound by policy. The\nconsumer is derived only from that binding, never from request or Executor\nsettings. No default sink or implicit sole-sink selection exists. Missing/null\ndispatch selection, mismatched consumer or unknown id refuses before\nreservation/launch as contract_violation (or authority_missing where the\nunderlying grant itself is absent). Unsupported kind, escaped path, absent\nconsumer/authority or unknown sink\nrefuses before delivery; public requests cannot register an endpoint. Sinks are\nnot independent sources of work-state truth. Indexes/cursors are projection\nmetadata, not an alternate admission ledger.\n\nWhole-family contraction uses eight semantic atoms, with admitted domains:\n**Acquire** (permitted exact bytes/typed records); **Project** (authored finite\nrelationships/content); **Evaluate** (supported source-bound predicate/join);\n**Render** (selected packet to measured exact context); **Admit** (complete\nProduct-bound finite relation); **Invoke** (registered exact effect);\n**Observe** (declared external/effect/time/resource facts); and **Record**\n(atomic existing-grant evidence or Writer unit with explicit source owner).\nThese are implementation operation families, not new functor kinds.\n\n| Public operations | Derived atoms / module projection |\n|---|---|\n| tools.describe | Acquire+Project registered contract data; core, thin adapter. |\n| workspace.observe; source.read; records.find/read; evidence.read; work.project | Acquire+Project; core with representation-specific adapters. Raw/source/record/carrier reads share authority/path/hash law instead of becoming competing acquisition centers. |\n| graph.project; relations.query | Acquire+Project finite declared relations; reuse codec closure; no inferred semantic dependency engine. |\n| context.assemble | Acquire+Project+Render+Evaluate fit; core, effect-owned immutable retention. |\n| contract.preflight | Acquire+Evaluate+Admit; core prepares exact relation, effect edge commits receipt once. |\n| dispatch.start | Admit existing receipt+Invoke+Record intent/actual observations; effects. |\n| dispatch.observe; dispatch.cancel; events.wait | Observe or already-authorized Invoke cancellation+Observe+Record; effects. No scheduler/continuation atom. |\n| return.capture; return.check | Acquire+Record original, then Evaluate exact binding/currentness; core plus store. |\n| review.prepare | Acquire+Project+Record supplied F_P assertion/exposure; no semantic-review oracle. |\n| checks.evaluate; results.conjoin | Evaluate only qualified declared predicates/operators; core. |\n| work.write | Core prepares exact existing-owner Writer relation; effects Admit+Record one transition and Observe actual result. |\n| refresh.prepare | Acquire+Project+Evaluate selected impact/reuse, Render handoff; no autonomous refresh policy. |\n| resources.aggregate | Acquire+Project counters and Evaluate selected limits; core, no benefit inference. |\n\nThe three modules are realization projections of these atoms. Core owns typed\nrelations/complete envelopes, effects owns atomic persistence/external edges,\nand adapter owns only wire dispatch/serialization. Public read variants remain\nuseful typed projections of Acquire/Project; they do not duplicate authority.\nThe carrier inventory is irreducible for this selected boundary: trusted\nsource/policy, observed exact inputs, activated Context/receipt, Attempt anchor,\noriginal Return and evidence cannot be merged without collapsing authority,\ncurrentness, invocation or predicate distinctions. Helper classes, indexes and\nprotocol wrappers are subordinate representations, not additional semantic\ncenters. No functionality row is unowned: all 23 operations are derived above;\nunsupported cross-method/calculus/provider/distributed forms are explicit\nexcluded domains, with no fallback route.\n\nContract state is an explicit field separate from receipt decision and\n","coordinates":{"lines":[2791,2849]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005","selected_sha256":"d34170d3faee4a0eb8050998c4274cbdabff4819730cc3987433ad9160d013c9","size_bytes":4642,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[2791,2849]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014sNMCexYiXhSwHX8tC4bDn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
