{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAzvznsCZFwqmHP438oJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TyVkfkQKnSZVtaXgbEagHK","name":"mcp__ac_review__source_read","input":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-how-051","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[3076,3140]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11028,"cache_read_input_tokens":378504,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11028},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"8dbf1b34-e9e6-41b0-997a-a1d30d128667","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:55:00.687Z","request_id":"req_011CgAzvz6D6dQxNFWoww4zy","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01TyVkfkQKnSZVtaXgbEagHK":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"p2-read-how-051","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[3076,3140]},"sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TyVkfkQKnSZVtaXgbEagHK","display_name":"Source Read","server_display_name":"a_c.graphify.fd-support","tool_name":"source.read"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TyVkfkQKnSZVtaXgbEagHK","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:14720c6cc6a37f3d615d06fdb18bbf767fca0e09a69bffc1b92c43a2cfad6c9c\",\"sha256\":\"14720c6cc6a37f3d615d06fdb18bbf767fca0e09a69bffc1b92c43a2cfad6c9c\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-051\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=3d69d7d68b8dd4688b04366db4a446312ad1b68b77410001c0567e6469f05891]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"verifies the complete outgoing result/artifact graph, publishes dependencies\\nbefore its complete owning marker, and then builds one complete OperationEvidence\\nfrom the original request and final response with evidence=null. Its final ref\\nis inserted only into the specified response evidence field by the declared\\nwrapper. That fixed nonrecursive wrapper construction is not permission to\\npatch arbitrary core semantics. Typed artifacts and original raw bytes retain\\nseparate identities. The outer response always has the exact keys shown above,\\nincluding `operation_outcome`; its result is the explicit artifact/value object\\nor null where no result is available.\\n\\nCore `execute_read(runtime,request)->CoreOutcome`,\\n`build_preflight(runtime,request)->EffectPlan` and\\n`prepare_write(runtime,request)->EffectPlan` receive the whole request.\\n`check_preconditions(runtime,recheck_set)` returns newly acquired observations,\\nchanges and gaps; effects records and freshly reruns it at the actual edge.\\nEffects `execute_effect(runtime,request,plan)->CoreOutcome` is the sole\\npublic-request cross-module effect entry. The separate private fixed-supervisor\\nreentry is `supervise(runtime,attempt_ref)->int`, not another public operation. `plan` is the core-produced immutable EffectPlan\\nfor contract.preflight/work.write and is null for the other named effect\\noperations; these route only to fixed internal full-request helpers. Effects\\nnever constructs the Writer plan or accepts a CLI/MCP-supplied plan. It checks\\nthe exact request/plan/policy identity and reruns preconditions at the edge.\\n`persist_outcome(runtime,request,outcome)->Response` is the sole retention and\\nresponse-wrapper entry. It maps only the closed boundary status table, retaining\\ninner judgments unchanged. Old names such as dispatch, write_record and\\nretain_operation denote internal helpers only, or are absent; none is an\\nalternative export or persistence path. There is\\nno arbitrary plan input accepted from CLI/MCP. Effects constructs actual post-\\neffect observations with the same core envelope constructor, then persists\\ncomplete final bytes. A prepared intent is not an actual post-effect record.\\n\\nEvery source/candidate-content acquisition records its exact prepared/supplied\\nscope. Actual observed transport/context delivery, where available, is a\\nseparate complete event. A lost response never becomes proof of no exposure:\\nprepared content with uncertain delivery is potential exposure/unknown in the\\nhistory check. Actual public return or acknowledged context delivery is an\\nobserved route, not a claim that an actor mentally attended to every byte.\\nMissing/in-flight delivery proof cannot certify clean source-first ordering.\\n\\nAfter a complete actual CLI/MCP response write and flush, the fixed adapter\\ncalls the pure `core.transport_observation(runtime,request,response,interval,\\nbytes_sha256,byte_count)` builder, then `EvidenceStore.retain` once. The complete\\n`acquisition` envelope payload is exactly `schema`\\n(`a_c.fd-support.transport-observation/1`), `operation` (OperationEvidence ref),\\n`response_sha256`, `request_sha256`, `recipient`, `acquisitions`, `delivery` and\\n`wire`. `delivery` is exactly `{\\\"state\\\":\\\"write_flushed\\\",\\\"interval\\\":Interval}`;\\n`wire` is exactly `{\\\"sha256\\\":Sha256,\\\"bytes\\\":nonnegative integer}`. The builder\\nreacquires/verifies the protected operation against the exact original request\\nand response (its evidence coordinate is separate), and derives acquisition\\nrefs only from that operation's actual public-response content scope for the\\nfixed principal. The envelope provenance binds the original request/principal\\nand actual interval. A Context summary is not delivery of its retained body.\\nThe response digest covers the public tool response; the wire digest/byte count\\ncover the actual full CLI or JSON-RPC bytes written, including its framing.\\nThis event is an observed local write/flush, never consumer acquisition, mental\\nreceipt or a second result. `persist_outcome` remains the sole response wrapper;\\nthere is no second public operation, prior-envelope patch or fabricated receipt.\\nIn-flight/partial/failed writes and missing/failed event publication remain\\npotential exposure/unknown. A post-write publication failure reports the gap on\\nstderr without changing the already written response or silently retrying it.\\nHistory matches the verified operation/acquisition/recipient/interval relation;\\nmissing evidence cannot certify clean source-first ordering.\\n\\nThe internal supervisor entry is fixed:\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[3076,3140]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"40006ea94c28dba7b1cec5dc06952b638d5136c3572d36ae93e65955760f4340\",\"size_bytes\":4512,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[3076,3140]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d70f2d0-ea95-44de-98cd-d06e9ca7170b","uuid":"6eae7126-a0db-4552-8b78-34e2fb071799","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:55:00.848Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:14720c6cc6a37f3d615d06fdb18bbf767fca0e09a69bffc1b92c43a2cfad6c9c\",\"sha256\":\"14720c6cc6a37f3d615d06fdb18bbf767fca0e09a69bffc1b92c43a2cfad6c9c\"},\"id\":\"p2-read-how-051\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=3d69d7d68b8dd4688b04366db4a446312ad1b68b77410001c0567e6469f05891]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"verifies the complete outgoing result/artifact graph, publishes dependencies\\nbefore its complete owning marker, and then builds one complete OperationEvidence\\nfrom the original request and final response with evidence=null. Its final ref\\nis inserted only into the specified response evidence field by the declared\\nwrapper. That fixed nonrecursive wrapper construction is not permission to\\npatch arbitrary core semantics. Typed artifacts and original raw bytes retain\\nseparate identities. The outer response always has the exact keys shown above,\\nincluding `operation_outcome`; its result is the explicit artifact/value object\\nor null where no result is available.\\n\\nCore `execute_read(runtime,request)->CoreOutcome`,\\n`build_preflight(runtime,request)->EffectPlan` and\\n`prepare_write(runtime,request)->EffectPlan` receive the whole request.\\n`check_preconditions(runtime,recheck_set)` returns newly acquired observations,\\nchanges and gaps; effects records and freshly reruns it at the actual edge.\\nEffects `execute_effect(runtime,request,plan)->CoreOutcome` is the sole\\npublic-request cross-module effect entry. The separate private fixed-supervisor\\nreentry is `supervise(runtime,attempt_ref)->int`, not another public operation. `plan` is the core-produced immutable EffectPlan\\nfor contract.preflight/work.write and is null for the other named effect\\noperations; these route only to fixed internal full-request helpers. Effects\\nnever constructs the Writer plan or accepts a CLI/MCP-supplied plan. It checks\\nthe exact request/plan/policy identity and reruns preconditions at the edge.\\n`persist_outcome(runtime,request,outcome)->Response` is the sole retention and\\nresponse-wrapper entry. It maps only the closed boundary status table, retaining\\ninner judgments unchanged. Old names such as dispatch, write_record and\\nretain_operation denote internal helpers only, or are absent; none is an\\nalternative export or persistence path. There is\\nno arbitrary plan input accepted from CLI/MCP. Effects constructs actual post-\\neffect observations with the same core envelope constructor, then persists\\ncomplete final bytes. A prepared intent is not an actual post-effect record.\\n\\nEvery source/candidate-content acquisition records its exact prepared/supplied\\nscope. Actual observed transport/context delivery, where available, is a\\nseparate complete event. A lost response never becomes proof of no exposure:\\nprepared content with uncertain delivery is potential exposure/unknown in the\\nhistory check. Actual public return or acknowledged context delivery is an\\nobserved route, not a claim that an actor mentally attended to every byte.\\nMissing/in-flight delivery proof cannot certify clean source-first ordering.\\n\\nAfter a complete actual CLI/MCP response write and flush, the fixed adapter\\ncalls the pure `core.transport_observation(runtime,request,response,interval,\\nbytes_sha256,byte_count)` builder, then `EvidenceStore.retain` once. The complete\\n`acquisition` envelope payload is exactly `schema`\\n(`a_c.fd-support.transport-observation/1`), `operation` (OperationEvidence ref),\\n`response_sha256`, `request_sha256`, `recipient`, `acquisitions`, `delivery` and\\n`wire`. `delivery` is exactly `{\\\"state\\\":\\\"write_flushed\\\",\\\"interval\\\":Interval}`;\\n`wire` is exactly `{\\\"sha256\\\":Sha256,\\\"bytes\\\":nonnegative integer}`. The builder\\nreacquires/verifies the protected operation against the exact original request\\nand response (its evidence coordinate is separate), and derives acquisition\\nrefs only from that operation's actual public-response content scope for the\\nfixed principal. The envelope provenance binds the original request/principal\\nand actual interval. A Context summary is not delivery of its retained body.\\nThe response digest covers the public tool response; the wire digest/byte count\\ncover the actual full CLI or JSON-RPC bytes written, including its framing.\\nThis event is an observed local write/flush, never consumer acquisition, mental\\nreceipt or a second result. `persist_outcome` remains the sole response wrapper;\\nthere is no second public operation, prior-envelope patch or fabricated receipt.\\nIn-flight/partial/failed writes and missing/failed event publication remain\\npotential exposure/unknown. A post-write publication failure reports the gap on\\nstderr without changing the already written response or silently retrying it.\\nHistory matches the verified operation/acquisition/recipient/interval relation;\\nmissing evidence cannot certify clean source-first ordering.\\n\\nThe internal supervisor entry is fixed:\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[3076,3140]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32