ain a\\nseparate registered binding and cannot override this startup/own-code scope.\\nThe fixed adapter entry calls\\nexactly `effects.supervise(runtime, ArtifactRef)`. This private reentry resolves\\nonly a complete protected Attempt reservation, recovers its original full strict\\nrequest and exact retained Context, and rechecks policy, grant, target, fixed\\nexecutable and dependency binding before the already registered launch. It\\ncreates no forged public request, new public operation, hidden Runtime mode or\\nalternate admission path. supervise returns an integer OS-supervisor exit code,\\nnot a semantic judgment or Worker result. Other effect helpers remain internal. Supervisor\\nstdout/stderr go to separate protected diagnostic files; they never contaminate\\nCLI/MCP stdout or substitute for actual executor stdout/stderr. Exact stdin,\\nworker outputs, invocation observations and unknown usage remain distinct.\\n\\nStartup failure before trusted policy/store binding emits a CLI refusal/error\\nwith null evidence and explicit unretained scope (or a protocol initialization\\nerror); it writes no untrusted location and creates no admission/result. A\\nmalformed call before a bound operation has id/operation null where they cannot\\nbe trusted, status refused and operation_outcome null; it may retain raw input\\nas protected diagnostic evidence only if a trusted store is available. Store\\nfailure emits status error, null/unavailable durable refs and the actual\\npublication gap. It never emits a computed-but-unpublished ref as durable\\nsupport. If an external effect may have happened, the durable pre-effect intent\\nand actual known/unknown subject state are retained/reconstructed; no failed\\nrecording path manufactures rollback or completed work. The caller can acquire\\nvalid partial evidence while the output-availability predicate remains held.\\n\\n### Ordinary CLI and pinned MCP projection\\n\\nCLI passes the exact full versioned request envelope to the single dispatcher.\\nFor MCP, each ordinary operation is published as its tool name, and\\n`tools/call.arguments` is that same **full envelope**, including schema, stable\\nrequest.id, operation and arguments. `tools/call.params.name` must equal\\nrequest.operation; the published inputSchema is the core full-envelope schema\\nwith that operation fixed. The caller's request.id is the effect idempotence\\nidentity. JSON-RPC session/request ids are transport identities and never\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[3141,3199]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\",\"selected_sha256\":\"6b2fc7f083bf98f7fb089010e6be01a518445ec9c2642c7d71eae026808f56c2\",\"size_bytes\":3846,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[3141,3199]},\"sha256\":\"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:177b4bec31d910f389bf221a95566adc0848e6046c5c15a46ae7016fda4ebc88","sha256":"177b4bec31d910f389bf221a95566adc0848e6046c5c15a46ae7016fda4ebc88"},"id":"p2-read-how-052","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=e6024ecfa30fa059485043d9070c0da7ffa598da4461f2e298bf151f06d397fd]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"```text\n<operator-startup Python> <exact ac_support.py> _supervise\n  --policy <operator-selected absolute policy path>\n  --policy-sha256 <exact digest>\n  --principal <original requester principal>\n  --attempt-id <protected immutable anchor id>\n  --attempt-sha256 <exact anchor digest>\n```\n\nOnly the effects module creates this argv from the retained reservation; public\nrequests supply none of these path/argv values. Before supervisor spawn, the\nimmutable Attempt invocation seals its `supervisor` binding: `python` is the\nresolved regular-file path/SHA-256 of the actual startup interpreter; `modules`\ncontains exact path/SHA-256 pins for ac_support.py, ac_support_core.py and\nac_support_effects.py; `startup` retains Python invocation, policy path/digest\nand principal; `argv_template` identifies the fixed private entry and `argv`\nretains its fixed construction. The anchor-coordinate suffix alone uses the\nfixed `<immutable-anchor-id>` / `<immutable-anchor-sha256>` placeholders until\nthat complete anchor is hashed; filling those two values is not re-pinning.\nInterpreter/module pins are checked before supervisor spawn and at private\nreentry before actor launch. Drift/unreadability/unavailability refuses or\nholds without launch; reentry never silently selects new bytes. Canonical\nsymlink resolution identifies the actual operator-started Python, not a\nrequest-selected authority. Actor Executor executable/argv/settings remain a\nseparate registered binding and cannot override this startup/own-code scope.\nThe fixed adapter entry calls\nexactly `effects.supervise(runtime, ArtifactRef)`. This private reentry resolves\nonly a complete protected Attempt reservation, recovers its original full strict\nrequest and exact retained Context, and rechecks policy, grant, target, fixed\nexecutable and dependency binding before the already registered launch. It\ncreates no forged public request, new public operation, hidden Runtime mode or\nalternate admission path. supervise returns an integer OS-supervisor exit code,\nnot a semantic judgment or Worker result. Other effect helpers remain internal. Supervisor\nstdout/stderr go to separate protected diagnostic files; they never contaminate\nCLI/MCP stdout or substitute for actual executor stdout/stderr. Exact stdin,\nworker outputs, invocation observations and unknown usage remain distinct.\n\nStartup failure before trusted policy/store binding emits a CLI refusal/error\nwith null evidence and explicit unretained scope (or a protocol initialization\nerror); it writes no untrusted location and creates no admission/result. A\nmalformed call before a bound operation has id/operation null where they cannot\nbe trusted, status refused and operation_outcome null; it may retain raw input\nas protected diagnostic evidence only if a trusted store is available. Store\nfailure emits status error, null/unavailable durable refs and the actual\npublication gap. It never emits a computed-but-unpublished ref as durable\nsupport. If an external effect may have happened, the durable pre-effect intent\nand actual known/unknown subject state are retained/reconstructed; no failed\nrecording path manufactures rollback or completed work. The caller can acquire\nvalid partial evidence while the output-availability predicate remains held.\n\n### Ordinary CLI and pinned MCP projection\n\nCLI passes the exact full versioned request envelope to the single dispatcher.\nFor MCP, each ordinary operation is published as its tool name, and\n`tools/call.arguments` is that same **full envelope**, including schema, stable\nrequest.id, operation and arguments. `tools/call.params.name` must equal\nrequest.operation; the published inputSchema is the core full-envelope schema\nwith that operation fixed. The caller's request.id is the effect idempotence\nidentity. JSON-RPC session/request ids are transport identities and never\n","coordinates":{"lines":[3141,3199]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"b38eedbe85ee32ef11d945d6a60ed3f9bb2312ac10e873d8ddc9b7986744a005","selected_sha256":"6b2fc7f083bf98f7fb089010e6be01a518445ec9c2642c7d71eae026808f56c2","size_bytes":3846,"source":